const RFP_DATABASE = [{"id": "rfp_001", "category": "AI", "question": "Please describe any unique technology/AI tools you use and how they are utilized in the service delivery process.", "answer": "At the company, we leverage cutting-edge AI tools to enhance the experience for both candidates and recruiters, ensuring a seamless, efficient service delivery process.\n\nFor Candidates, the company uses creates a personalized journey from the moment they access the platform. Our AI-driven Smart Job Matching technology analyzes resumes and quickly identifies roles that align with a candidate's skills, even if the job titles don’t match. This focus on Skills-Based Matching helps candidates discover opportunities that best fit their expertise. Additionally, our AI-Powered Chatbot assists candidates throughout their journey, from uploading resumes to finding the right job, all through a mobile-optimized platform. Candidates can also manage their communication preferences, sign up for AI matched job alerts, and maintain control over their personal data, ensuring a secure, tailored experience.\n\nFor Recruiters, the company utilizes Generative AI to support content creation, simplifying the development of application questions, campaigns, and communications. This helps recruiters save time while ensuring consistent and engaging messaging. Our AI also enhances the matching process by quickly analyzing candidate profiles and pairing them with the most suitable roles, even across varying job titles. This reduces the time spent on manual searches and allows recruiters to focus on high-quality candidates.\n\nImportantly, our AI-driven matching technology has passed a rigorous third-party audit, ensuring its accuracy, efficiency, and lack of bias, providing both recruiters and candidates with a reliable, fair platform.\n\nBy integrating AI into both the candidate and recruiter workflows, the company delivers a smarter, more efficient experience that streamlines the hiring process from start to finish."}, {"id": "rfp_002", "category": "AI", "question": "Not a question, but if you have any additional information on the AI matching I could circulate with legal", "answer": "https://trust.holisticai.com/nyc-bias-audit/eyJjbGllbnRJZCI6ImN1cmF0ZWx5LWFpLTB2azF1IiwiZW50aXR5SWQiOiI2YTVkNTU5MC0wZGZmLTQwZjItYjZlNS1kNGEwNzFlMDBkMmEiLCJzeXN0ZW1JZCI6IjZhNWQ1NTkwLTBkZmYtNDBmMi1iNmU1LWQ0YTA3MWUwMGQyYSJ9"}, {"id": "rfp_003", "category": "AI", "question": "Can you please describe what AI you are using - do you own it?  Anything else as it pertains to your LLM.", "answer": "Our proprietary machine learning model, securely hosted on a private AWS instance, is trained on an extensive dataset encompassing more than 147,000 unique job and skill taxonomies. This comprehensive foundation enables the model to maintain a deep, current understanding of virtually every job role and skill set in today’s market.\n\nInitially, our matching scores were based on four main criteria: Job Title, Skills, Education, and Job Stability. However, following the COVID-19 pandemic, Job Stability became less relevant as a reliable indicator and was seamlessly removed from the scoring process. Because we own our model, we can readily incorporate new criteria or remove existing ones as hiring landscapes evolve. We also give users full control over the weighting of each factor for every individual job search. In addition, our system provides complete transparency into which roles, related positions, and skills influenced the results, empowering talent acquisition teams to manually include or exclude certain job types or skill sets. This ensures that human decision-makers maintain ultimate authority over refining and focusing their search parameters.\n\nBeyond adaptability and transparency, our platform delivers robust AI-powered matching and scoring functionalities. It supports \"Job-to-Candidate\" matching, \"Candidate-to-Job\" matching, and \"Candidate-to-Candidate\" matching. For instance, recruiters can upload a single résumé to identify a pool of similar candidates, enabling more accurate, efficient, and contextually relevant hiring.\n\nFurthermore, we have undergone and successfully passed a comprehensive third-party bias audit. This independent review affirms that our model’s methodologies and outcomes adhere to strict fairness standards, ensuring that users can trust our platform to deliver equitable, unbiased results.\n\nHere is the link to the results from the independent third party bias audit:\nhttps://trust.holisticai.com/nyc-bias - audit/eyJjbGllbnRJZCI6ImN1cmF0ZWx5LWFpLTB2azF1IiwiZW50aXR5SWQiOiI2YTVkNTU5MC0wZGZmLTQwZjItYjZlNS1kNGEwNzFlMDBkMmEiLCJzeXN0ZW1JZCI6IjZhNWQ1NTkwLTBkZmYtNDBmMi1iNmU1LWQ0YTA3MWUwMGQyYSJ9"}, {"id": "rfp_004", "category": "AI Voice Bot", "question": "Is the Bot integrated with Job Diva", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_005", "category": "AI Voice Bot", "question": "How do the API's work with the Voice Bot", "answer": "We are integrated using APIs. Jobs can be seamlessly pushed from the ATS and synced. Maya also pushes candidates back into JobDiva when they are added directly to Maya, ensuring a smooth, bidirectional workflow."}, {"id": "rfp_006", "category": "AI Voice Bot", "question": "Can the Bot speak different languages?", "answer": "Technically, the bot is capable of speaking different languages, but we have not prioritized this feature since most recruiting interactions currently occur in English."}, {"id": "rfp_007", "category": "AI Voice Bot", "question": "What happens if a candidate isn't avaialble.", "answer": "If the candidate doesn’t answer, the bot will leave a voicemail. Additionally, the candidate has the option to instruct the bot to call back at a specified time."}, {"id": "rfp_008", "category": "AI Voice Bot", "question": "What  is provided to the recrutier after the bot call", "answer": "The recruiter receives a full transcript of the conversation, along with a score for each question posed to the candidate. Additionally, if the candidate indicates they are not interested, that status will be recorded and tracked."}, {"id": "rfp_009", "category": "AI Voice Bot", "question": "Can the bot make a decision based on the candidate’s responses?", "answer": "No, the bot will proceed with all the questions and leave the decision-making to the recruiter, who can assess the candidate’s fit based on their responses."}, {"id": "rfp_010", "category": "AI Voice Bot", "question": "Can the bot connect to a recrutier?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_011", "category": "Candidate Engagement", "question": "Describe your organization's strategy to ensure a great candidate experience when interacting with your platform?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub delivers an outstanding candidate experience by focusing on five key areas:\n\n1.\tUser Experience: KnowledgeHub is designed to be intuitive and easy to navigate, streamlining the process of applying for jobs or joining the community.\n2.\tAutomation and Personalization: By embedding AI into the candidate job match process, KnowledgeHub surfaces relevant roles for candidates, eliminating the need for manual searches. It also offers automated tools like job alerts, credential management, and a chatbot, alongside features that help recruiters seamlessly engage with candidates. Balancing efficiency with a human touch is key.\n3.\tCommunication: KnowledgeHub’s automated updates keep candidates informed of their application status and next steps, reducing frustration caused by lack of communication or unclear timelines.\n4.\tMobile Compatibility: With a mobile-first approach, KnowledgeHub allows candidates to apply and engage with recruiters on the go—a crucial advantage for younger, mobile-centric users.\n5.\tData Privacy: KnowledgeHub prioritizes transparency and security, offering clear privacy policies and robust data protection to instill confidence in candidates."}, {"id": "rfp_012", "category": "Candidate Engagement", "question": "How do you engage candidates within the technology? Provide a workflow of what is automated vs. manual messaging.", "answer": "At KnowledgeHub, candidate engagement is powered by a mix of automation and personalized outreach to ensure every candidate feels connected throughout their journey. KnowledgeHub gives the Curation team options on how they want to configure the workflow when candidates join the community or apply to a job. \n\nSample Workflow - https://curatelyaiinc-my.sharepoint.com/:p:/g/personal/jsemler_curatelyai_com/EZd6V8TFIQRAsSKrZrbhRPkBpEWt21evUCeTJybjInXvSQ?e=bbK11Y\n\nAutomation\n\nChatbot: KnowledgeHub's AI-driven chatbot engages candidates as soon as they land on the platform. It gathers key information, answers common questions, and guides candidates to apply for relevant job opportunities or access resources.\nCandidate Journey Mapping: Once a candidate creates a profile, they're automatically placed into a personalized journey based on their skills, interests, and engagement history. Automated campaigns—like job alerts and personalized recommendations—are triggered along the way.\nCampaigns: Candidates receive regular automated email and text campaigns with tailored job recommendations, application status updates, and reminders for next steps. This keeps them informed and engaged without requiring manual intervention.\n\nManual\n\nSMS and Email: While automation drives much of the communication, KnowledgeHub values the personal touch. Recruiters step in at key moments for manual messaging via text or email, particularly during critical stages like interviews, assessments, or offer negotiations. This human interaction ensures candidates feel supported and valued throughout the process.\nOngoing Engagement (Automated & Manual Blend): After initial contact, automated communication continues to nurture candidates with updates, new opportunities, and community invitations. Recruiters also send personalized messages to high-potential or highly engaged candidates, tailoring responses to their needs."}, {"id": "rfp_013", "category": "Candidate Engagement", "question": "Does your technology allow for different talent pools by type? Can you send targeted messaging to these groups vs. across the entire talent pool?", "answer": "Yes, KnowledgeHub provides filtering capabilities within a talent pool, helping curators determine exactly who they wish to message."}, {"id": "rfp_014", "category": "Candidate Engagement", "question": "What other values does your technology provide the candidate vs. connecting them to a potential job?", "answer": "At KnowledgeHub, the candidate will be able to;\n•\tRefer friends and colleagues to roles.\n•\tManage their credentials and licenses - Get reminders about upcoming expiration dates for your credentials and licenses to keep them current.\n•\tManage their data privacy and opt out of the community."}, {"id": "rfp_015", "category": "Candidate Engagement", "question": "Describe what tools are available within your platform to assist curation partners to build and execute an email marketing nurture strategy. Are any of these services/tools provided by a third party?", "answer": "Embedded in the KnowledgeHub platform is the capability for Curation Partners to create email campaigns and journeys that nurture the candidate community. Within a journey or campaign, the Curation Team can craft different experiences, like gathering information from candidates, conducting surveys, and creating calls to action that drive engagement. Additionally, the Curation Team can develop email templates for recruiters to use consistently across communications."}, {"id": "rfp_016", "category": "Candidate Engagement", "question": "Describe how the tool leverages SMS, Chatbot or other messaging options for candidates.", "answer": "Embedded in the KnowledgeHub platform is the capability for Curation Partners to create SMS campaigns that nurture the candidate community. Within a journey or campaign, the Curation Team can design different experiences and craft calls to action that drive engagement. Additionally, the Curation Team can develop SMS templates for recruiters to use consistently across communications.\n\nKnowledgeHub also offers a Chatbot feature that can process candidate job applications and be fully configured to meet the client's specific requirements."}, {"id": "rfp_017", "category": "Candidate Engagement", "question": "What are the technical requirements for a candidate to leverage the technology? Are there any browsers that cannot be used?", "answer": "There are no specific technical requirements for a candidate to leverage the technology, they can access the technology from any browser."}, {"id": "rfp_018", "category": "Candidate Engagement", "question": "Describe all of the features available for the candidate experience", "answer": "Fully Customizable Design to Match Verizon’s Branding\nOur career portal is built on a robust Headless CMS (Content Management System), which gives us unparalleled flexibility in design and functionality. This includes:\n•\tFonts: We can incorporate any custom or proprietary fonts that Verizon uses, ensuring brand consistency across all platforms.\n•\tColors and Themes: All color schemes, button styles, and thematic elements can be customized to reflect Verizon’s brand identity.\n•\tLogos and Imagery: We can seamlessly integrate Verizon’s logos and high-resolution images throughout the portal.\n•\tLayout and Navigation: The overall layout, including menus and navigation paths, can be designed to provide an intuitive user experience that resonates with your audience.\n•\tCustom Content: On the job listing page, both in the banner area and at the bottom of the screen, tailored content such as the Direct Sourcing Program name, program descriptions, and other relevant details can be added to engage candidates effectively. This provides an opportunity to share key information and enhance the candidate experience.\n \nUser-Friendly Drag-and-Drop Visual Editor\nOur platform features a drag-and-drop visual editor, which allows for quick and efficient design, building, and editing of the career portal. This means:\n•\tRapid Development: We can implement design changes swiftly without extensive coding.\n•\tReal-Time Updates: Any updates or tweaks can be made on the fly, ensuring the portal remains up-to-date with Verizon’s latest branding or content changes.\n•\tEase of Collaboration: Our team can work closely with yours to adjust designs in real-time during review sessions.\n \nRich Media Integration for Enhanced Engagement\nTo make the portal more engaging and informative for potential candidates, we can incorporate various media elements:\n•\tVideos: Embed promotional or informational videos that highlight Verizon’s culture and opportunities.\n•\tDynamic Content: Utilize interactive elements like slideshows, animations, or interactive job maps.\n•\tButtons and Call-to-Actions: Strategically placed buttons can guide users to apply, sign up for job alerts, or share postings on social media.\n \nMobile-First Responsive Design\n Understanding that many users access job portals via mobile devices, our platform is designed with a mobile-first approach:\n•\tResponsive Layouts: The portal will automatically adjust to fit desktops, tablets, and smartphones.\n•\tOptimized Performance: Fast loading times and optimized media ensure a smooth user experience on all devices.\n•\tTouch-Friendly Interfaces: Buttons and interactive elements are designed for easy use on touchscreens.\n \nWhite Labeling and Custom Web URLs\nWe offer the ability to white-label the career portal, making it an extension of Verizon’s existing web presence:\n•\tCustom Domain Integration: If Verizon chooses, the portal can be hosted on a custom URL like https://flexjobs.verizon.com, providing a seamless transition for users from your main site.\n•\tConsistent User Experience: The look and feel of the portal will match Verizon’s main website, maintaining brand continuity."}, {"id": "rfp_019", "category": "Candidate Engagement", "question": "Is the platform mobile or app based or does it leverage mobile optimization across all devices? Which device experience is best for the candidate?", "answer": "The platform is web based but built with mobile-first approach. it can be accessed with the next experience accross all devices."}, {"id": "rfp_020", "category": "Candidate Profiles", "question": "How do candidates interact with the platform? What does a candidate profile look like and can the candidate edit their profile?", "answer": "Candidates interact with the platform through a web based app, Candidate profiles have several components such as experience, education, Preferences. Candidates have the ability to edit and update their profile."}, {"id": "rfp_021", "category": "Candidate Profiles", "question": "How are duplicate candidates are managed within the platform?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub identifies duplicate candidates by email and/or phone. Platform offers the users ability to choose if they want allow duplicate candidates to be created or not. and also allows users ability to merge duplicate candidates."}, {"id": "rfp_022", "category": "Candidate Profiles", "question": "How does the platform provide relevant content based on candidate profiles? Do you leverage a specific or prebuilt technology to socialize jobs? Is there a 3rd party application i.e.. Broadbean in the background.", "answer": "platform leverages AI matching capabilities to provide relevant content based on candidates profiles."}, {"id": "rfp_023", "category": "Candidate Profiles", "question": "Are screening criteria applied when making a profile?", "answer": "No"}, {"id": "rfp_024", "category": "Candidate Profiles", "question": "Is it possible to put separate screening criteria on a talent pool and job/assignment level?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_025", "category": "Candidate Profiles", "question": "Can documents be uploaded by both the worker as well as MPG/TAPFIN?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_026", "category": "Candidate Profiles", "question": "Can workers refer other contractors to client/job?  Describe how you leverage referrals in the platform", "answer": "Yes. By accessing a job link, workers can refer candidates to a job. We track all referral information within our reporting suite."}, {"id": "rfp_027", "category": "Candidate Profiles", "question": "Can active assignments can be evaluated and scored?", "answer": "No"}, {"id": "rfp_028", "category": "Candidate Profiles", "question": "Please provide a workflow on how the candidate data is imported into the platform and then into the VMS.", "answer": "Candidates can be importe in KnowledgeHub iva Bulk import feature using a CSV file. Or can be imported directly for ATS system through API. KnowledgeHub pushes candidate data in vms tool via the API's"}, {"id": "rfp_029", "category": "Candidate Profiles", "question": "Can a workers status and availability be automatically and manually set to active or inactive", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_030", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Year of establishment", "answer": "2020-12-16 00:00:00"}, {"id": "rfp_031", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Number of full-time employees", "answer": "42"}, {"id": "rfp_032", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Country of headquarters", "answer": "USA"}, {"id": "rfp_033", "category": "Company Information", "question": "City of headquarters", "answer": "Alpharetta"}, {"id": "rfp_034", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Offices besides HQ", "answer": "India"}, {"id": "rfp_035", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Direct Sourcing Spend under management", "answer": "$10- $30 Mil"}, {"id": "rfp_036", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Company Name (Full Legal Name)", "answer": "KnowledgeHub AI, Inc"}, {"id": "rfp_037", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Doing Business as (dba) name should match as per W9/W8 form", "answer": "KnowledgeHub AI, Inc"}, {"id": "rfp_038", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Where is your company headquartered?", "answer": "Alpharetta, GA"}, {"id": "rfp_039", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Please give a brief overview of your company.", "answer": "the company is a full-stack AI-powered  talent relationship management, direct sourcing and high-volume hiring platform."}, {"id": "rfp_040", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Contact Name", "answer": "Sales Person"}, {"id": "rfp_041", "category": "Company Information", "question": "How many permanent employees do you have?", "answer": "32"}, {"id": "rfp_042", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Which year was your company founded?", "answer": "2021"}, {"id": "rfp_043", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Is your business certified to a supplier diversity classification?", "answer": "No"}, {"id": "rfp_044", "category": "Company Information", "question": "If \"Yes\", please specify the type of diversity certification which you hold.", "answer": "Not Applicable"}, {"id": "rfp_045", "category": "Company Information", "question": "D & B Number", "answer": "007933950"}, {"id": "rfp_046", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Previous Company Name(s)", "answer": "Not Applicable"}, {"id": "rfp_047", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Which of the following does your company fall under?", "answer": "Other (Please specify)"}, {"id": "rfp_048", "category": "Company Information", "question": "How is your company held?", "answer": "Private"}, {"id": "rfp_049", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Has your company every filed bankruptcy?  If yes, please explain.", "answer": "No"}, {"id": "rfp_050", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Has your company ever been involved in litigation?  If so, please describe.", "answer": "No"}, {"id": "rfp_051", "category": "Company Information", "question": "List top five customers.", "answer": "Bristol Myer-Squibb, Red Ventures, HD Supply, Blue Cross Blue Shield Tannessee, Blue Cross Blue Shield Arizona."}, {"id": "rfp_052", "category": "Company Information", "question": "List top five competitors.", "answer": "TalentNet, WorkLlama, LiveHire, Opptly, Bubty"}, {"id": "rfp_053", "category": "Company Information", "question": "List your approximate annual sales for each of the past five (5) years.", "answer": "2019: $0 ARR\n2020: $0 ARR\n2021: $50,000 ARR\n2022: $1,200,000 ARR\n2023: $2,600,000 ARR"}, {"id": "rfp_054", "category": "Company Information", "question": "Do you conduct business currently at any Elevance Health location? If so, please list location and employee contact.", "answer": "No, We do not conduct business currently with Elevance Health."}, {"id": "rfp_055", "category": "Compliance and Regulatory", "question": "How does KnowledgeHub stay aligned with the TCPA rules regarding texting.", "answer": "Recent U.S. privacy regulations concerning text messaging do apply to recruitment activities. The Telephone Consumer Protection Act (TCPA) governs all text communications, including those for recruitment purposes. Under the TCPA, businesses must obtain prior express consent from individuals before sending automated text messages, regardless of whether the content is for marketing or recruitment. However,  in Payton v. Kale Realty, LLC, the court ruled that recruitment messages were not considered telemarketing. \n\nWith KnowledgeHub, the recruiter selects the candidates who receive SMS messages for the purposes of recruitment."}, {"id": "rfp_056", "category": "DE&I", "question": "Does the platform support candidate self-identification during the application process?  Is this form customizable?  If not, does it follow current EEOC guidance?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub takes a unique approach to reporting DE&I information. We use the same algorithm as the U.S. Census Bureau, allowing us to provide insights into the ethnicity and gender makeup of a community without assigning specific attributes to individual candidates.\n\nIf a client wants to capture additional details about a candidate, we can incorporate application questions to gather that information directly from the candidate."}, {"id": "rfp_057", "category": "DE&I", "question": "Does the application have features to anonymize candidate data?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_058", "category": "DE&I", "question": "What capabilities does the platform have to summarize and present candidate and worker diversity data while protecting PII?", "answer": "Platform summarizes and present teh candidate DE&I data in aggregrate, we do not identify or present the DE&I data at individual level making sure the PII protected."}, {"id": "rfp_059", "category": "Direct Sourcing Experience", "question": "How many years of experience does your company have in providing direct sourcing platforms?", "answer": "3 Years. We are also bringing onto the team two Direct Sourcing SME's who have 10+ years combined experience with Direct Sourcing platforms and implementations."}, {"id": "rfp_060", "category": "Direct Sourcing Experience", "question": "What notable clients or case studies can you share that demonstrate your success in this domain?", "answer": "Please see the attached case studies. Attachment 9.3.2"}, {"id": "rfp_061", "category": "Direct Sourcing Experience", "question": "Provide a list of all organizations in which the Bidder has successfully implemented and managed a Direct Sourcing solution similar to that which is required by this solicitation within the last 5 years. Please include the name and location of the organization, as well as the date the implementation was completed. Provide the name, title, email address, and telephone number of a contact person for each organization, together with a brief description of the project or assignment that formed the basis for the business relationship. The Client will determine which, if any, references to contact to assess the quality of the work performed and the staff assigned to the project. The results of any references are provided to the evaluation committee and used when scoring the proposal.", "answer": "1. Organization: Bristol Myer-Squibb\n\nDate of Implementation: July 1st, 2024\n\nContact Name: Gabriel Moreno\n\nTitle: Associate Director – Global Contingent Workforce\n\nLocation: Madison, NJ\n\nEmail Address: gabriel.moreno@bms.com\n\nPhone Number:  908-347-9496\n\nDescription of the project:\n\nBristol-Myers Squibb (BMS) initially launched their direct sourcing program using TalentNet as the technology platform and relied on their current Managed Service Provider (MSP) for curation services. Unfortunately, the program did not achieve the desired results, yielding only six successful hires over 12 months and a talent pool of less than 3,600 candidates.\n\nAs a result, BMS issued a Request for Proposal (RFP) to find a new direct-sourcing technology and curation service provider. KnowledgeHub entered the competitive bidding process against established players like WorkLLama and others. Ultimately, KnowledgeHub was awarded the contract to become the direct sourcing technology platform for BMS's Gen2 direct sourcing program.\n\nWe are currently in the implementation phase, with a scheduled go-live date of July 1, 2024.\n\n\n2. Organization: Red Ventures\n\nDate of Implementation: November, 6th, 2022\n\nContact Name: Cheryl Tracz\n\nTitle: Senior Manager, Contingent Workforce\n\nLocation: Ft. Mill, SC\n\nEmail Address: ctracz@redventures.com\n\nPhone Number: 770.510.3996\n\nDescription of the project:\n\nRed Ventures sought to implement a comprehensive solution for direct sourcing, talent pooling, and freelancer management. To find the best fit, they released a Request for Proposal (RFP). \n\nKnowledgeHub was invited to participate in the bidding process due to our unique positioning in the market as an all-in-one, unified platform capable of addressing all of Red Ventures' requirements within a single solution.\n\nOur platform’s versatility and comprehensive capabilities set us apart from the competition, ultimately leading to KnowledgeHub being awarded the contract.\n\n3. Organization: HD Supply\n\nDate of Implementation: July, 2023\n\nContact Name: Jeff French\n\nTitle: Director, Customer Care & Solutions\n\nLocation: Atlanta, GA\n\nEmail Address: jeffrey.french@hdsupply.com\n\nPhone Number: 925 324 4853\n\nDescription of the project:\n\n\nHD Supply was searching for a robust talent pooling and high-volume hiring platform to streamline its customer support hiring process. After evaluating various options, they conducted a demo of the KnowledgeHub platform. Impressed by its capabilities and user-friendly interface, HD Supply initiated a pilot program.\n\nThe pilot proved extremely successful, demonstrating the platform’s effectiveness in meeting their high-volume hiring needs. As a result, HD Supply chose to adopt KnowledgeHub for staffing all their future training classes, including both phone support and chat support teams.\n\n\n4. Organization: Jeld-Wen\n\nDate of Implementation: August 17, 2021\n\nContact Name: Jen Torres\n\nTitle: Vice President, Partnerships and Solutions \n\nLocation: Charlotte, NC 28273\n\nEmail Address: jen.torres@pontoonsolutions.com\n\nPhone Number: 704.517.4702 \n\nDescription of the project:\n\nJeld-Wen, the largest manufacturer of doors and windows in the USA, initially launched a direct sourcing program using a competitor’s technology platform. However, the platform lacked essential functionality for the sourcing team, leading to poor program performance. Seeking a solution, Jeld-Wen's Managed Service Provider (MSP) reached out to KnowledgeHub to explore options that wouldn't necessitate replacing the existing direct sourcing platform.\n\nKnowledgeHub responded by delivering a customized solution that seamlessly integrated with the existing direct sourcing technology. This enhancement enabled the sourcing team to perform all their activities within the KnowledgeHub platform, eliminating the need to switch between different tools and platforms. As a result, the sourcing team could operate more efficiently, improving the overall performance of Jeld-Wen's direct sourcing program."}, {"id": "rfp_062", "category": "Direct Sourcing Experience", "question": "How many clients fall within each of the following spend ranges: <$10m, $10m-$50m, $50m-$100m.", "answer": "1 Client: $50M - $100M, 2 Clients: $10M to $50M"}, {"id": "rfp_063", "category": "Global", "question": "What is the international coverage? Please provide the split per country.", "answer": "No answer at this time"}, {"id": "rfp_064", "category": "Integrations", "question": "Are we integratied with What's App or RingCentral", "answer": "We are not integrated with RingCentral, or we don't do WhatsApp yet. Now, we cannot support RingCentral. It's obvious, no voice AI bot can do that. They have to be on our own phone lines, and we cannot integrate with the company phone line. That's just not a feasibility for Maya or any voice bot for that matter."}, {"id": "rfp_065", "category": "Global", "question": "What are your global capabilities - what you are able to do in what countries.  Do you need to do anything to make you viable in those countries? Feel free to specify India.", "answer": "Technology Platform:\nOur platform is globally ready and fully adheres to GDPR regulations, ensuring the highest level of data protection and privacy compliance. In addition, we are in the final stages of launching a multilingual career portal, expected to be operational within the next four weeks. This expansion will enable users to seamlessly engage with our services in their preferred language, further enhancing the reach and inclusivity of our technology.\nNote: We have successfully completed and passed Manpower Group’s comprehensive and rigorous global security and data privacy assessment.\n\nCuration Services: \nCurrently available in the United States, the United Kingdom, India, and Canada, our curation services leverage our worldwide expertise to identify and recommend top-tier talent. With a deep understanding of local markets and industry trends, we help organizations find the right candidates efficiently and effectively.\n\nEOR (Employer of Record) Services:\nOffered in the United States, Canada, and India, our EOR solutions provide a streamlined and compliant way for businesses to employ and manage talent across borders. From navigating complex labor laws to handling payroll and benefits, we empower companies to build and scale their global workforce effortlessly.\n\nLocal Presence and Expertise:\nWe maintain a robust on-the-ground presence, particularly in the United States and India, where we have substantial teams dedicated to client support and operational excellence. Our local experts ensure personalized attention, market insight, and timely assistance, resulting in a more responsive and impactful partnership with our clients."}, {"id": "rfp_066", "category": "Global", "question": "Explain how you leverage language or regionalization tools to provide a global solution.  What languages are available natively in your platform? Can separate client talent pools be hosted regionally based on global teams?", "answer": "Currently we only have English as the native language in the platform."}, {"id": "rfp_067", "category": "Global Approach to Talent Pool/Communities", "question": "Where (using what service and in which country) is data in your application hosted?", "answer": "We utilize AWS services and data is hosted in the local country of the origin."}, {"id": "rfp_068", "category": "Global Approach to Talent Pool/Communities", "question": "Describe who is owns the client data in an MSP relationship. How does the platform secure EU-specific candidate data and GDPR controls?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is the processor of the data we are not the controller or owner of the data. Who is the controller/owner is determined between the curation partner, client, and the MSP."}, {"id": "rfp_069", "category": "Global Approach to Talent Pool/Communities", "question": "How are Client specific talent pools protected from a data privacy perspective? How are talent pool access points controlled? How might this impact a TAPFIN administrator across multiple accounts?", "answer": "client specific talent pools are stored physically separate databases. Only the user with appropriate permissions have access to the talent pools. Administrators with access permission to multiple client specific talent pools can toggle between clients across multiple accounts to access the talent pools without having to logout and re-login each time."}, {"id": "rfp_070", "category": "Global Approach to Talent Pool/Communities", "question": "Describe how you support global clients specifically around language support, data hosting.", "answer": "Certain aspects of our platform are only in English, but the candidate facing career portal is offered in multi-language. Data is hosted regionally local to clients specific region."}, {"id": "rfp_071", "category": "Implementation", "question": "What is the typical implementation timeline for your platform?", "answer": "Our typical implementation timeline is 8 to 12 weeks."}, {"id": "rfp_072", "category": "Implementation", "question": "Describe your implementation procedures for your Direct Sourcing solution and provide a sample implementation project plan including implementation timescales, tasks, required client stakeholders, time commitments and dependencies. This should include installation procedures (if applicable) for webpages/access.", "answer": "Considering this is a second-generation implementation, the groundwork (including marketing and legal approval) has already been completed. Therefore, the implementation of KnowledgeHub should be relatively straightforward. \n\nPlease consult the Implementation Guide for additional information."}, {"id": "rfp_073", "category": "Implementation", "question": "What are typical implementation challenges (installation of solution, webpages, and interfaces) and how do you overcome them? Outline your key learnings from previous implementations?", "answer": "1. VMS integrations can be challenging and potentially delay implementation. To mitigate this, KnowledgeHub offers a VMS wrapper that can serve as an interim or permanent solution. The wrapper features bi-directional sync and captures all job requisition information and updates, including submittals, interviews, and offers. This ensures seamless data flow and minimizes disruption during the integration process.\n\n2. Brand Marketing Coordination:\nGaining time and approval from the brand marketing organization can lead to delays, particularly when building custom career sites that align with the client’s brand guidelines. Marketing teams often become bottlenecks when providing final approval. To avoid delays, we recommend that the program sponsor schedule regular meetings with the marketing team during the implementation phase to ensure timely progress and feedback.\n\n3. Division-Specific Requirements:\nWe encountered challenges when we did not fully understand a specific division's unique requirements, culture, and need for significant process variations. This led to user dissatisfaction and impacted the overall success of the implementation. This experience underscored the importance of conducting thorough assessments of division-specific needs before implementation.\n\nLessons Learned and Strategies for Success:\n\nComprehensive Assessments:\n\nConduct detailed assessments to understand the unique needs and cultural nuances of each division. This enables us to tailor the solution to meet specific requirements, ensuring a more customized and successful implementation.\n\nProactive Stakeholder Engagement:\n\nEngage proactively with division stakeholders through in-depth discussions to understand their unique requirements and necessary process variations. This ensures alignment and satisfaction across different divisions.\n\nRegular Scheduling and Coordination:\n\nSchedule regular meetings with key teams, such as brand marketing, during the implementation phase. This ensures that approvals and feedback are received in a timely manner, keeping the project on track.\n\nBy implementing these strategies, KnowledgeHub aims to ensure smooth and successful integrations, timely coordination with brand marketing teams, and tailored solutions that meet the specific needs of each division."}, {"id": "rfp_074", "category": "Implementation", "question": "Describe how you would transition data from existing Direct Sourcing platform to your platform.", "answer": "To transition data from an existing Direct Sourcing platform to our platform, we undertake a meticulous and collaborative process to ensure a seamless and effective data migration. Here’s how we approach it:\n\nConsultative Planning: Initially, we engage in detailed consultations with our customers to thoroughly understand their existing internal processes and data structure. This understanding is critical as it allows us to tailor the migration process to meet specific needs and ensure that all relevant data is accurately mapped from the current system to KnowledgeHub.\nData Mapping and Reparsing: Leveraging our deep knowledge of data structures, including our past experience migrating data from  Talentnet, we meticulously map data to the KnowledgeHub structure. We also reparse all job descriptions and candidate resumes to ensure comprehensive data integrity and that no critical information is overlooked or misplaced during the transition.\nData Migration and Validation: After mapping, we proceed with the data migration, during which every piece of data is carefully transferred to ensure completeness and accuracy. Post-migration, we utilize advanced diagnostic tools to scan the entire dataset. This scan helps us generate a detailed data quality report which identifies if any additional cleaning or adjustments are necessary.\nQuality Assurance and Cleanup: Based on the insights from the data quality report, we undertake any required data cleanup activities. This step is crucial to ensuring that the data in the new system is clean, accurate, and fully usable for your business needs.\nOngoing Support and Optimization: After the migration, we remain engaged to provide support and ensure that the data adapts well to the new system. We also offer ongoing optimization services to enhance data utility and performance over time."}, {"id": "rfp_075", "category": "Implementation", "question": "Describe your approach to assisting us in managing change in process, policy, and personnel both during the implementation of your solution and once the program is fully operational.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub has designed a comprehensive change management strategy to ensure the success of your direct sourcing program and we have outlined below:\n  \nDuring Implementation: \n\n1. Comprehensive Stakeholder Engagement: \n\nEngage key stakeholders, including HR, management, and end-users, early in the process to communicate the new solution's benefits. Conduct workshops to address concerns and gather feedback. \n\n2. Clear Communication Strategies: \n\nImplement a robust communication plan detailing changes in processes and policies. Utilize various channels, such as emails, workshops, and intranet updates, to ensure information reaches all relevant parties.\n\n3. Training Programs: \n\nDevelop tailored training programs for end-users and managers to ensure a smooth transition. Provide hands-on sessions, documentation, and ongoing support to facilitate the learning curve. \n\n4. Change Champions: \n\nIdentify and empower change champions within the client's organization. These individuals advocate for the new solution, fostering a positive attitude toward the change.  \n\nPost-Implementation: \n\n1. Continuous Feedback Mechanisms: \n\nEstablish mechanisms for continuous feedback from end-users. Conduct regular surveys and feedback sessions to identify areas for improvement and address evolving needs.\n \n2. Adaptable Support Structures: \n\nMaintain adaptable support structures, including helpdesk services and user forums. Ensure a responsive support system to address challenges and provide solutions promptly. \n\n3. Regular Check-ins and Reviews: \n\nConduct regular check-ins and reviews with key stakeholders to assess the effectiveness of the implemented solution. Address any emerging issues promptly to prevent dissatisfaction among users."}, {"id": "rfp_076", "category": "Integrations", "question": "Please describe your VMS integration strategy. Include who is responsible to stand up the integration. Are there any additional costs for VMS integration?", "answer": "We consume the API's provided by the VMS tools as we have found that to be the best approach. KnowledgeHub is responsible to stand up the integration we work closely with our clients and MSP partners to get all required access for a smooth and swift integration. No there are no additional cost for VMS integrations."}, {"id": "rfp_077", "category": "Integrations", "question": "What third-party technologies or platforms do you leverage or integrate with to enable your direct sourcing solutions?", "answer": "Currently, we have VMS integrations with Beeline and Fieldglass.  In addition, we have more than 80 ATS integrations as well as integrations with various 3rd party platforms utilized for background checks, video interviewing , assessments as well as multiple global job boards."}, {"id": "rfp_078", "category": "Integrations", "question": "Which VMS partners do you have tested and live system integrations in place with?. Beeline, VNDLY, Fieldglass, Simplify, or others? Please describe your experience with each VMS tool?.", "answer": "Currently,. we have one program live with Beeline.  Overall, we had a good experience. as beeline direct sourcing API has come a long way.  In addition, we are integrated with Fieldglass and have developed a partnership with VNDLY.  Once a VNDLY opportunity has been identified, VNDLY will assign resources to complete the integration.  We are open to integrations with other VMS companies as well once we have identified a need for an integration with them."}, {"id": "rfp_079", "category": "Integrations", "question": "Does your technology allow for multiple-to-1 VMS integration in the same instance? For example, if a shared talent pool were established supporting multiple end-clients with their own VMS platforms, is it possible to establish systems integrations into each of their systems from a single instance of your platform?", "answer": "Not out of the box. But this can be accomplished with a little bit of custom development."}, {"id": "rfp_080", "category": "Integrations", "question": "For each VMS platform you support, are there standard connectors or custom integrations that need to build per customer?", "answer": "There are standard  connectors, however we recognize that some clients will require some level of customer integrations."}, {"id": "rfp_081", "category": "Integrations", "question": "How long does the average implementation take? What are the key variables that determine how quickly an implementation can be executed?", "answer": "The platform can be configured in less than a week, enabling clients to source candidates and match them against jobs.   That said, the average implementation is approximately 6 weeks as there are factors that may delay the implementation process.\n\nImplementation can be delayed due to client approvals for branding & messaging, the curation workflow process, and VMS integration. KnowledgeHub offers a workaround to simulate the VMS integration, eliminating the need for a swivel seat and the requirement for integration to be complete prior to go-live."}, {"id": "rfp_082", "category": "Integrations", "question": "Which ATS partners you have supported. Workday, Avature,  or others? Previous experience with each ATS tool?", "answer": "We have more than 80 ATS integrations including Workday and Avature."}, {"id": "rfp_083", "category": "Integrations", "question": "Do you require client ATS access for \"known candidates\"? How do you leverage the client's current static databases?", "answer": "Using our ATS integrations clients can connect KnowledgeHub to their ATS and import known candidates into cordately."}, {"id": "rfp_084", "category": "Integrations", "question": "What client resources are required for an implementation?", "answer": "Executive Sponsor - The Executive Sponsor will assist in setting the strategy, obtaining internal approvals, and resolving escalations.\n\nPlatform Super User - The Platform Super User will closely align with the Executive Sponsor and the KnowledgeHub implementation team. This team member will be heavily involved in creating operational procedures and learning how to utilize the self-service features. \n\nMarketing - Marketing will approve the branding and logo's. Additionally, they will assist in adding the KnowledgeHub link to the clients careers page.\n\nLegal - The legal team will need to approve any issues with co-employment and risk.\n\nInformation Technology - KnowledgeHub will not integrate with the clients internal technologies. \n\nPMO Team Lead - Engagement from the PMO team is critical to the success of the program. While not all members need to be involved in the implementation, having a representative who can partner with the Platform Super User and KnowledgeHub is essential to ensure alignment of operational elements necessary for compliance and connectivity with the payroll team. The PMO Team Leader and the Platform Super User could potentially be the same employee.\n\nCuration Team - The Curation Team will be involved during the training phase. It would also be prudent to keep them informed of the implementation progress and the features that will begin to benefit them once they are live on the new platform."}, {"id": "rfp_085", "category": "Integrations", "question": "Define Wrapper", "answer": "Integrating with a Vendor Management System (VMS) can be complex and may delay your implementation process. To simplify this, KnowledgeHub provides an Automated Sync that delivers the exact same functionality as a VMS integration. It serves as a flexible option—whether temporary or permanent—and features bi-directional syncing to capture all job requisition details, including submittals, interviews, and offers. This ensures seamless data flow and minimizes disruptions during the integration process."}, {"id": "rfp_086", "category": "Partnership - MSP", "question": "Does your company have experience in working together with a MSP?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_087", "category": "Partnership - MSP", "question": "Number of different MSP's?", "answer": "4"}, {"id": "rfp_088", "category": "Partnership - MSP", "question": "In which country or countries?", "answer": "USA"}, {"id": "rfp_089", "category": "Pricing", "question": "What is your pricing model, and what does it include? (Examples: fee as percentage of spend, fee per worker, fee per user, fixed fee periodically, license fees, Clearly indicate which services, if any, are excluded from the fee, and their respective additional cost(s) would be maintenance fees, support fees or other)? Please indicate all respective fees.", "answer": "We offer flexible pricing options, allowing clients to choose between fees as a percentage of spend or license fees, depending on which ends up being the most cost-effective and beneficial for their needs.\n\nFees as Percentage of Spend:\n\nStarting Rate: Our fees begin at 1.50% of the total spend, with a minimum monthly fee of $5,000.\nTiered Discounts: As the spend increases, the percentage fee decreases. For example, once the spend exceeds $5 million, the fee percentage is reduced, and it continues to decrease as higher spend thresholds are reached.\nIncluded Services: This model encompasses all essential services, including maintenance, support, data migration, unlimited users, and training fees. There are no additional costs for these services, ensuring a comprehensive package for our clients.\n\nCalculation Examples:\n\nLow Monthly Spend: For a monthly spend of $200,000, the fee at 1.50% would be $3,000. However, since our minimum fee is $5,000, the client would pay the minimum fee of $5,000.\n\nCalculation: $200,000 * 1.50% = $3,000 (minimum fee of $5,000 applies)\nTotal Monthly Fee: $5,000\nHigher Spend: For a monthly spend of $1,000,000, the fee at 1.50% would be $15,000. Since this is above the minimum fee, the client would pay $15,000.\n\nCalculation: $1,000,000 * 1.50% = $15,000\nTotal Monthly Fee: $15,000\nIncreased Spend: If the monthly spend increases to $6,000,000, and the fee percentage for spends over $5 million drops to 1.25%, the fee would be calculated as follows:\n\nFor the first $5,000,000: 1.50% of $5,000,000 = $75,000\nFor the remaining $1,000,000: 1.25% of $1,000,000 = $12,500\nTotal Monthly Fee: $75,000 + $12,500 = $87,500\nLicense Fees:\n\nFixed Periodic Fee: Clients may opt for a license fee model, which involves a fixed fee paid periodically (e.g., monthly or annually). The specific amount is determined based on the scale and requirements of the client’s operations.\n\nIncluded Services: Similar to the percentage of spend model, this option includes maintenance, support, data migration, and training fees at no extra cost.\n\nExcluded Services and Additional Costs:\n\nOur pricing models are designed to be all-inclusive, covering the full spectrum of services needed for effective platform utilization. Therefore, there are no hidden or additional costs for maintenance, support, data migration, or training.\n\nBy offering these flexible pricing options, we ensure that our clients can choose a model that best aligns with their budget and operational needs, providing both value and comprehensive support."}, {"id": "rfp_090", "category": "Pricing", "question": "Identify any rebates, cash incentives, or volume discounts included upon Contract execution or during the term of the Contract.  How does your company proactively generate, document, and deliver year-over-year savings for your clients?", "answer": "Presenting tailored commercial incentives for Elevance Health:\n\nUpon Contract Execution:\n\nCash Incentive upon contract execution: A one-time $100,000 cash incentive applicable towards consulting initiatives with third-party providers. KnowledgeHub will be responsible for payments. This may encompass internal change management communication, technology enhancements and integrations, project management fees for a lift and shift of direct sourcing technology, talent marketing advisory, business unit training, historical data syncs, API integrations, and analytics.\n\n\nKnowledgeHub will offer the tiered pricing structure for the percentage fees of the spend.\n\n•     $0 to $5,000,000: 1.50%\n•     $5,000,001 to $50,000,000: 1.25%\n•     $50,000,001 to $100,,000,000: 1.00%\n•     Above $100,000,000: 0.75%\n\n\nDelivering Year-Over-Year Savings:\n\nOur platform empowers clients to achieve dynamic and multifaceted cost savings through growth, strategic expansion, and loyalty rewards. This comprehensive approach not only generates immediate savings but also establishes a foundation for sustained cost reduction and efficiency in the long term.\n\nGrowth and Efficiency:\n\nInitial Focus: At the onset of a direct sourcing program, our platform assists clients in starting with selected job titles, working towards achieving a 100% fill rate. Initially, savings might be minimal, but our objective is to rapidly elevate the fill rate, setting a strong foundation for success.\n\nEarly Stage Strategy: In the initial phases, our platform helps clients establish a robust talent pool from scratch. Although initial savings may be negligible, our agile approach ensures a swift increase in fill rates.\n\nBuilding for the Future: Our platform also prepares clients for subsequent roles, labor categories, and regional expansions. This forward-thinking strategy ensures that once the fill rate goals in one area are met, clients are ready to replicate this success in others.\n\nMeasuring Success: The key metric here is the fill rate percentage. Achieving a high fill rate quickly is a tangible indicator of our platform’s efficiency and effectiveness in talent acquisition.\nStrategic Expansion:\n\nSystematic Growth: Our platform supports clients in expanding strategically by adding more job titles, categories, and entering new regions. This expansion ensures the talent community remains robust and capable of sustaining high fill rates.\n\nScalable Growth: Our expansion is systematic and scalable. Starting with a set number of roles and regions, the scope is broadened methodically, maintaining quality and efficiency.\n\nTimeline and Roadmap: Our platform’s strategic roadmap envisions expansion every three months, aiming to reach saturation in about two years. This structured approach allows clients to plan, execute, and measure growth effectively.\n\nSustained Excellence: As clients expand, our platform ensures that maintaining high fill rates and exceptional service quality remains the top priority. This consistency is crucial for long-term client satisfaction and savings.\n\nRebates and Cost Savings:\nEfficiency and Scale: As fill rates increase, clients begin to see considerable cost savings facilitated by our platform. These efficiencies are amplified with scope expansion, leading to exponential savings.\n\nRewarding Client Loyalty: Our platform recognizes and rewards increased client spending with volume discounts. These rebates result from the efficiencies achieved through scale and represent a significant portion of the cost savings offered.\n\nContinuous Improvement: Our commitment to continuous process enhancement ensures that clients benefit from ongoing optimization. This enables even greater savings over time, reflecting our dedication to maximizing efficiency.\n\nWe keep detailed records of the savings derived from each of these three key areas, along with their year-over-year progression. For further insight, please refer to our sample report on annual savings trends, detailed in attachment 9.11.2."}, {"id": "rfp_091", "category": "Pricing", "question": "Are you able to receive payment for agreed pricing via our payroll provider rather than direct payment?", "answer": "Can comply"}, {"id": "rfp_092", "category": "Product", "question": "What Parsing tool do we use", "answer": "Sovren"}, {"id": "rfp_093", "category": "Rate Determination", "question": "Do workers provide rates in their profiles with their preferred min/max rates? How is this determined? What part is automated vs. human interaction?", "answer": "Yes, Workers can provide rates in their profile with their preferred Min/Max rates."}, {"id": "rfp_094", "category": "Rate Determination", "question": "Does the matching criteria use rate information as a component for qualification?", "answer": "No"}, {"id": "rfp_095", "category": "Rate Determination", "question": "Can worker rates be benchmarked?", "answer": "No"}, {"id": "rfp_096", "category": "Recruitment", "question": "Are licenses linked to a specific person, or to a maximum amount of people?", "answer": "Maximum amount of people"}, {"id": "rfp_097", "category": "Recruitment", "question": "Can different user roles be specified with different access rights?  Can user roles and descriptions be provided?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_098", "category": "Recruitment", "question": "Describe how candidates are matched within the platform.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub matches candidates in the platform by utilizing AI to parse resumes and compare them against parsed job descriptions. Based on job title, skill set, and education, the platform automatically returns candidates with a percentage match. Recruiters can adjust the match criteria by emphasizing specific skills or job titles, and they can also apply filters to refine the search and surface the best-matched candidates."}, {"id": "rfp_099", "category": "Recruitment", "question": "How are new positions shared within the community?", "answer": "New positions can be shared within the community in several ways. Candidates can set up job alerts to be notified when new roles that match their skills and job titles are posted. Additionally, the platform can be automatically configured to invite candidates to jobs where they are an 80% or greater match. Lastly, Curation Team members can invite canddiates to jobs."}, {"id": "rfp_100", "category": "Recruitment", "question": "Can candidates be grouped according to different selection criteria?", "answer": "Yes. KnowledgeHub provides filters that can be used group candidates according to specific criteria."}, {"id": "rfp_101", "category": "Recruitment", "question": "Candidates can be labelled/tagged on different criteria?", "answer": "Yes. In addition to tags and ratings, KnowledgeHub allows curation teams to create custom fields that can be incorporated into the candidate profile. These fields can be completed by the recruiter and are not visible to the candidate."}, {"id": "rfp_102", "category": "Recruitment", "question": "Do you have automated workflows to speed up the process? Automatically generate triggers if certain steps have been taken, or if there is a lack of activity?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_103", "category": "Recruitment", "question": "Can lists of leads be imported for high volume sourcing or new pools?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_104", "category": "Recruitment", "question": "Is there a separate process or workflow for redeploying past contractors, alumni, payrollees, etc.?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_105", "category": "Recruitment", "question": "Can contracting can be performed in the system?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_106", "category": "Recruitment Marketing", "question": "If you had an opportunity to meet with our recruitment marketing operations team - what questions would you pose to them about brand marketing?\n\nExpand the question - more answers hidden in the cell", "answer": "Careers Page\n \nBranding & Guidelines:\n•       Are we authorized to use Verizon branding? Will brand assets and guidelines (e.g., logos, images) be provided?\n•       Assets Specifications:\n•       Logos, Favicon, Chatbot Image, Social Media Post: Max dimensions 200px x 200px, JPG/PNG/SVG formats, max size 1MB (500kb for favicon).\n•       Banner: Max dimensions 1200px x 200px, same file format/size requirements.\n•       Direct Sourcing Program Name:\n•       What should we name the program? Suggestions can be provided.\n•       Page Content:\n•       Is there specific language Verizon wants included? Content spaces available: under the banner and at the bottom of the page.\n•       Terms & Conditions:\n•       Will Verizon Marketing or Legal provide this language?\n•       Co-Branding:\n•       Should the site be co-branded with Talent Solutions?\n•       Link Placement:\n•       Discuss link location on the Careers page and is there a need for notification about redirection to the Verizon <<Program Name>> page.\n•       Custom URL Hosting:\n•       Determine URL structure: https://flexjobs.verizon.com (seamless) vs. https://careers.curately.ai/jobs/verizon.\n \nBranded Email Templates\n \n•       Marketing Team Involvement:\n•       What role will Verizon Marketing play in developing email, campaign, and job description content?\n•       Bandwidth for Collaboration:\n•       Does the Marketing team have capacity to partner with Talent Solutions for campaign management?\n \nCandidate Invitations to the Known Candidates\n \n•       Audience:\n•       Known candidates include former employees, alumni, and independent contractors.\n•       Ownership:\n•       Will Verizon send these invites, or should KnowledgeHub handle this?\n•       Content:\n•       What level of involvement does Verizon want in drafting content? Templates can be provided.\n \nInternal Change Management\n \n•       Stakeholder Communication:\n•       Will Verizon commit to informing internal stakeholders (e.g., Hiring Managers) about the program?\n•       Content Ownership:\n•       What role will Verizon play in composing communication content? Templates can be provided.\n \nVerizon Domain Name for Emails\n \n•       Branded Emails:\n•       Can the Verizon domain be used for emails from Curation and Program teams? This is highly recommended.\nChatbot\n \n•       Usage:\n•       Does Verizon want to use the KnowledgeHub chatbot?\n•       Content Review:\n•       If yes, does the chatbot content require Verizon review?"}, {"id": "rfp_107", "category": "Reporting", "question": "Please describe any unique information or data reporting on industry or hiring trends available to clients.", "answer": "This answer is in support of an ASK RFP \n\nKnowledgeHub offers a comprehensive view of industry and hiring trends by aggregating data across 150 clients nationwide. This wealth of data provides clients with valuable insights into hiring trends, including pay rates, bill rates, and time-to-fill metrics, which can be segmented by location, industry, job title, and more. This granular data empowers clients to make more informed decisions based on specific market conditions.\n \nIn addition to this, KnowledgeHub has access to a database of over 700 million passive candidates globally, sourced from social media platforms like LinkedIn and Instagram, rather than traditional job boards. This allows KnowledgeHub to provide detailed analysis on the availability of candidates in specific regions, helping clients understand candidate supply and demand and make strategic decisions about talent acquisition.\n \nKnowledgeHub also offers integration capabilities with other platforms that specialize in tracking industry data, ensuring clients can access a robust and dynamic set of insights to guide their workforce planning and hiring strategies."}, {"id": "rfp_108", "category": "Reporting", "question": "How does the platform track and measure key performance indicators related to sourcing and recruitment?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub offers a comprehensive tracking system for key performance indicators (KPIs) related to sourcing and recruitment. When jobs are entered into the system, a primary and secondary recruiter can be assigned to each position. The platform meticulously tracks various KPIs for these recruiters, including:\nThe number of jobs assigned to each recruiter.\nThe number of jobs for which they have made submissions.\nThe total number of submissions they have made.\nThe time taken to make these submissions.\nThe ratio of submissions to shortlisted candidates.\nThe ratio of submissions to interviews.\nThe ratio of interviews to job offers.\nThe ratio of offers to candidates who do not start.\nThe ratio of starts to successful completions.\nPlease see attached sample 9.8.1 Recruiter KPI Report"}, {"id": "rfp_109", "category": "Reporting", "question": "What built-in analytics does your platform provide? Can users build custom reports? Please provide examples.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub offers a comprehensive suite of built-in analytics with over 70 pre-built dashboards, categorized into six sections: \n\n1. Executive Insights\n2. Community Insights\n3. Recruiter Activity Insights\n4. Sourcing Insights\n5. Pipeline Insights\n6. Hiring Insights. \n\nThese dashboards provide detailed and segmented views to help users understand various aspects of their operations. In addition to the pre-built options, KnowledgeHub provides a user-friendly, no-code, drag-and-drop self-service feature that allows users to create custom dashboards tailored to their specific needs. Users can also generate custom reports and export data to Excel or CSV file formats, facilitating further analysis or integration with external reporting tools.\n\nMoreover, KnowledgeHub includes an AI data analyst which assists in creating reports, building dashboards, and performing complex data calculations, particularly with data from Fieldglass. This feature allows users to combine data from both Fieldglass and KnowledgeHub, creating comprehensive data visualizations that support informed, data-driven decision-making. Please see attachment 9.8.2 for example dashboards."}, {"id": "rfp_110", "category": "Reporting", "question": "Please explain how your system provides access to job posting history and candidate profile history?", "answer": "Job Posting History:\n\nWhen a job is received from Fieldglass and parsed into KnowledgeHub, the job description, along with roles and responsibilities, is saved in the original job posting section for internal use only. For jobs to be posted on the career portal and external job boards, the original job description is copied into the public job position section, where users can make necessary edits. This process ensures that the original content remains intact while allowing flexibility for modifications before posting. \n\nKnowledgeHub meticulously tracks all activities related to a job posting, including status changes such as open, closed, re-opened, and canceled. Each time an edit is made, the system logs the changes, capturing details like the nature of the edits, the date and time, and the user responsible. Furthermore, KnowledgeHub monitors job posting activity on the career portal and external job boards, providing a summarized timeline view of all these actions for easy reference.\n\nCandidate Profile History:\n\nKnowledgeHub provides a detailed snapshot of each candidate's application history, including every job they have applied to and the disposition information. The system tracks all interactions, such as emails, SMS messages, and notes, as well as engagements like profile views, career portal visits, and profile updates. All of this information is consolidated within the candidate's profile, offering a comprehensive view of their history and interactions with your organization. This enables recruiters to easily access and review a candidate's complete history, facilitating more informed decision-making."}, {"id": "rfp_111", "category": "Reporting", "question": "What database technologies (DBMS) are used by the solution? (DB2, Oracle, MySQL, NoSQL, Hadoop, etc)", "answer": "Our application uses SQL Server and Mongo DB."}, {"id": "rfp_112", "category": "Security", "question": "Does your company have an information security management system (ISMS) in place?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_113", "category": "Security", "question": "Is this ISO 27001 certified", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_114", "category": "Security", "question": "Does your company have additional security certifications?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_115", "category": "Security", "question": "What other measures does your company take to ensure security?", "answer": "We implement a multi-layered security approach. This includes Quick Heal for antivirus and endpoint detection, AWS Security Groups for network traffic control, AWS GuardDuty for continuous threat detection and monitoring, and AWS CloudWatch for real-time logging and alerting. This comprehensive solution ensures robust protection and rapid response to potential security incidents across our infrastructure."}, {"id": "rfp_116", "category": "Sourcing", "question": "For the public marketplace, how often is this information refreshed? Daily?", "answer": "90 days."}, {"id": "rfp_117", "category": "Support", "question": "In which languages can you provide customer support?", "answer": "English"}, {"id": "rfp_118", "category": "Support", "question": "What times is your company available to deliver support?", "answer": "8 AM to 8 PM EST"}, {"id": "rfp_119", "category": "Support", "question": "Way of offering support", "answer": "Chat, Email, Phone"}, {"id": "rfp_120", "category": "Support", "question": "Please describe your customer support offerings and the service-level agreements (SLAs).", "answer": "Customer support comprises the following:\n\n- Online Support Catalog & Training videos.\n- Chat Support with a Technical Lead\n- Access to an Account Manager to address more complex or urgent issues."}, {"id": "rfp_121", "category": "Support", "question": "What is your standard response time to resolve issues that may arise in our DS operations?", "answer": "Our Standard response times to resolve issues. \n\nLevel 1  -  under 1 hour\nLevel 2 - Under 4 hours, \nLevel 3 issue - Under 24 hours."}, {"id": "rfp_122", "category": "Support", "question": "How do we access your product catalog and/ or user manual and how often is it updated?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub offers an online help feature accessible to Elevance. The catalog is regularly updated to reflect new feature releases and enhancements to existing features."}, {"id": "rfp_123", "category": "Support", "question": "Describe your trouble-ticket tracking system and resolution process.", "answer": "At KnowledgeHub AI, we understand how crucial exceptional support is to your experience and success. We've designed our trouble-ticket tracking and resolution process to not only resolve issueQs efficiently but also provide a personalized, caring interaction at every step.\nPersonalized Customer Support:\nWhen you join us, you are assigned a dedicated Customer Success Manager (CSM), who will be your main point of contact. Think of your CSM as your personal guide and advocate within our company. Whether you encounter a small query or a significant issue, your CSM is ready to assist with warmth and expertise.\n\nSubmitting and Tracking Your Issue:\n\nYou have two convenient options to report any problems:\n\nDirect Contact: Simply reach out to your CSM with the details of your issue. Your CSM will personally handle the submission of the trouble ticket on your behalf.\n\nSelf-Service: You may also choose to submit the trouble ticket directly through our HubSpot CRM system. Once submitted, your CSM is immediately notified and takes ownership of your issue.\n\nResolution Process:\n\nUpon receiving your ticket, your CSM will:\n\nEvaluate and Route: Quickly assess your issue and route the ticket to the appropriate team member who specializes in that particular area.\n\nRegular Updates: While your ticket is being resolved, your CSM will keep you regularly informed about the progress. You’ll receive updates and any necessary follow-up actions will be communicated transparently.\n\nClosing the Loop:\nYour CSM will ensure that your issue is resolved to your satisfaction and will follow up to close the ticket only when you feel that everything has been addressed properly.\n\nOur Commitment:\n\nWe believe in humanizing customer support. With us, you will never feel like you are just submitting a ticket into an impersonal system. Your dedicated CSM will ensure your experience is as seamless and comfortable as possible, handling all aspects of your query with care and attention. We are committed to not only meeting but exceeding your expectations, providing a red-carpet service experience that makes you feel valued and respected.\n\nTypical Resolution Steps:\n\nSubmit a Request: You describe the issue you're facing, either directly or through our system.\nRoute the Ticket: Your CSM ensures the right team member is engaged to address your specific concerns.\n\nResolve the Issue: Your ticket is diligently worked on by the appropriate expert until it is resolved.\n\nClose the Ticket: With your confirmation that the issue has been satisfactorily resolved, the ticket is closed."}, {"id": "rfp_124", "category": "Support", "question": "Please briefly describe your organization’s ability to have in person and/or virtual resources available for implementation and post-implementation support.", "answer": "The majority of our implementation team is based in the USA. As a best practice, our team will be available in-person for the implementation process. Post-implementation support can be provided both virtually and in-person as needed, ensuring flexibility and comprehensive assistance tailored to your requirements."}, {"id": "rfp_125", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Are there database or DW prebuilt API's for exporting into DW tools. How can data be presented back to the MSP to allow TAPFIN to provide aggregate level data and business intelligence on the processes that are conducted within the direct sourcing platform?", "answer": "Platform offers multiple options for the data to be moved from platform to the BI tools used by clients. exporting to excel.cvs file, Api access to the  database."}, {"id": "rfp_126", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "How are the success measures represented within the tool? Are there standard dashboards to track progress toward those goals?", "answer": "KPI goals can be set in the platform and progress against the goals can be tracked."}, {"id": "rfp_127", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "What are the common dashboard views and is there an option to build custom dashboards?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub offers 70+ pre-built dashboards that are grouped under 6 categories (Talent community Insights, Executive Insights, Sourcing Insights, Recruiter activity Insights, Pipeline Insights, Hiring Insights) additionally it also offers self-service capabilities for users to create custom dashboard using the no-code drag and drop tool and also has a Ai data analyst that users can interact conversationally and AI analyst will built visualizations, create charts and graphs and do complex calculations."}, {"id": "rfp_128", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Will you allow TAPFIN to white label the partnership for a seamless client experience? Describe how you have created a white label platform experience for other MSPs", "answer": "We can allow TapFin to white label the partnership for seamless client experience but would need to understand the scope of white-labeling. We currently fo not white label the platform for other MSPs so are not able to provide any details."}, {"id": "rfp_129", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Describe how the platform uses Artificial Intelligence or Machine Learning within the system to understand candidate capabilities and to match candidates to opportunities.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub matches candidates in the platform by parsing resumes and comparing them against parsed job descriptions. Based on job title, skill set, and education, the platform automatically returns candidates with a percentage match. Recruiters can adjust the match criteria by emphasizing specific skills or job titles, and they can also apply filters to refine the search and surface the best-matched candidates."}, {"id": "rfp_130", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Is the AI built native in the app or does it leverage a 3rd party source? Please provide a workflow on how this is used.", "answer": "We currently leverage 3rd party source for AI."}, {"id": "rfp_131", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Which countries are you supporting today? How do you ensure compliance with local legislation in the country that the platform is being used?", "answer": "Currently, we support, the United States, Canada, India and the UK."}, {"id": "rfp_132", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Does the curation partner have capabilities such as predictive analytics, forecasting demand, AI, machine learning, etc. that are part of the platform/solution?", "answer": "We have some predictive analytics in the platform but we have several enhancements and advancements on our roadmap to be launched soon."}, {"id": "rfp_133", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "What built-in tools does your platform have for posting open job opportunities to job boards and social media? Please list the sites you integrate with.", "answer": "Platform offers ability to post jobs onto 1000+ job boards globally and to major social media platform."}, {"id": "rfp_134", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Does your tool integrate or leverage any skill assessments, video interviews or other candidate screening tools?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_135", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Statement of work capabilities", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_136", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Automatic document verification", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_137", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "The system can be customized to adapt to MSP specific needs. E.g. use own lay-out, change fields, add/delete fields, etc.", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_138", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Please specify the core capabilities of your Direct Sourcing Platform. (Limit 1000 words and no attachments).", "answer": "KnowledgeHub AI's core capabilities include the following:\n\n- Branded Job listing page \n- AI driven job suggestions \n- Transparent AI candiate matching\n- Automated email & SMS messaging and candidte engagement tools\n- Automated Talent Pool development\n- Self Service Reporting and Analytics\n- Self-Service features including workflows, custom fields, brand management, reporting, etc.\n- Access to large database of Ask candidates to seed the talent community\n- Targeted access to 265M candidates using social media profiles."}, {"id": "rfp_139", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Can the solution support Elevance Health management of encryption keys for Elevance Health data within SAP Fieldglass.", "answer": "Conforms \"Out of Box\""}, {"id": "rfp_140", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Please describe how solution provides client data segregation and/or isolation?", "answer": "Database Schema: Our solution employs a multi-tenant architecture, where each client's data is kept in its own dedicated database schema or table. This guarantees logical separation, ensuring that data belonging to one client is kept entirely separate from another’s.\n\nTenant-Specific Access Control: Access control mechanisms such as role-based access control (RBAC) or attribute-based access control (ABAC) are used to regulate data access according to the client's identity. This ensures that users only have permission to view and manage the data specific to their organization.\n\nData Encryption: To further secure client data, our solution incorporates encryption both at rest and in transit. This means that even if unauthorized access is attempted, sensitive data will remain secure and unreadable.\n\nLogical Separation: Our application ensures logical separation, preventing users from accidentally viewing or modifying data that belongs to other clients.\n\nData Masking: When sharing data for purposes like testing or reporting, data masking techniques are employed to anonymize or obfuscate sensitive client information, preventing unintended exposure."}, {"id": "rfp_141", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Does your solution allow direct access to the production database(s)? How can your data be integrated for scheduled reports with a third-party BI tool (ex: DOMO)?", "answer": "Conforms \"Out of Box\""}, {"id": "rfp_142", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Please describe your network architecture (DMZ, firewalls, IDS, etc )? Please provide diagrams", "answer": "Here is the overview of our network architecture:\n1. Network Perimeter\nFirewalls\nPosition: Located at the network's edge to prevent unauthorized access.\nFunction: Configured to allow or block traffic based on security policies. Act as a protective barrier between secured internal networks and untrusted external networks, such as the internet.\n2. Intrusion Detection and Prevention Systems (IDS/IPS)\nIDS/IPS Placement and Roles\nNetwork-Based IDS/IPS: Deployed at key points within the network to monitor traffic to and from all networked devices. Identifies suspicious patterns that may indicate a security breach.\nEndpoint-Based IDS/IPS (e.g., Quick Heal): Installed on individual devices to monitor and block malicious activities, detect policy violations, and protect against malware.\n3. Monitoring and Response (e.g., Datadog)\nSecurity Information and Event Management (SIEM)\nFunction: Integrates with IDS/IPS, firewalls, and other security tools to collect, analyze, and correlate security logs, providing centralized viewing of security alerts.\nNetwork Monitoring Tools \nFunction: Provides real-time visibility into network performance and security. Assists in detecting anomalies, monitoring system health, and triggering alerts for abnormal activities.\n4. Advanced Security Measures\nEncryption\nFunction: Encrypts data transmissions within the network and across the internet to protect data integrity and confidentiality.\n5. Access Control\nNetwork Access Control (NAC)\nFunction: Ensures that only authorized and compliant devices can access network resources, enforcing policy compliance.\n6. Cloud Security\nCloud-Based Firewalls, IDS/IPS\nFunction: Protects cloud infrastructure and applications by extending security policies to cloud environments, ensuring a consistent security posture both on-premises and in the cloud.\n\nPlease the attachment 9.2.5 for the network architecture diagram."}, {"id": "rfp_143", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "What regulatory frameworks and standards do you currently comply and or maintain certification with (e.g. HIPAA, PCI, Sox, ISO 17799/27001, HITRUST, etc.)? Please list all that apply.  Please attach executive summaries or full reports of all certifications.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is  GDPR and CCPA compliant. Additionally, we maintain SOC2, ISO 27001, and SO 27701 certifications, Certfications are attached."}, {"id": "rfp_144", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Elevance Health’s requirement for SSL/TLS is TLS 1.1 (with RC4 disabled) or TLS 1.2 (preferred). Older versions (including SSLv3 and TLS 1.0) must be disabled. Does the solution comply with this requirement?", "answer": "Conforms \"Out of Box\""}, {"id": "rfp_145", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Elevance Health requires AES-256 encryption for any Confidential (including but not limited to PHI/PII) data at rest. Does the solution comply with this requirement?", "answer": "Conforms \"Out of Box\""}, {"id": "rfp_146", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Does the solution utilize an encryption key management solution? (e.g.: key management server or hardware security module)", "answer": "Conforms \"Out of Box\""}, {"id": "rfp_147", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Does this solution support SAML 2.0 based authentication? In the case of single sign-on not working, are backup logins available for manual sign-on?", "answer": "Conforms \"Out of Box\""}, {"id": "rfp_148", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Please provide a complete list of data centers with physical locations used?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is hosted with AWS. Data centers are located in Oregon, Ohio, Northern California, and Northern Virginia."}, {"id": "rfp_149", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Does your platform integrate with SAP Fieldglass? Please list and describe what all is integrated. (For example submitals, interviews, updates on former contractors, etc) What other VMS’s do you currently have an integration with?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub Integrates with Fieldglass and other VMS tools such as Beeline and Workday VNDLY. We can add any specific integration endpoints the client needs. General integrations include:\n\n•\tAuto job parsing\n•\tSubmittal\n•\tHiring process flow (shortlist, rejections)\n•\tInterview scheduling\n•\tWork-order management"}, {"id": "rfp_150", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Does your platform have a demo environment that our team can access during this process that mirrors the production environment?  How many users would be able to get access to the demo environment from our team?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub will provide a sandbox environment that your team can utilize to access the platform. There is no limit to the number of users."}, {"id": "rfp_151", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "What are the key features and functionalities of your direct sourcing platform?", "answer": "Key features include:\n\n•\tTalent Sourcing\n•\tAI Candidate Matching\n•\tIntegrated job board search\n•\tJob posting on 1000+ job boards\n•\tLiedin Chrome Extension\n•\t275+ Million people directory\n•\tRecruitment Workflow automation\n•\tAsynchronous Video interview\n•\tHigh volume Hiring\n•\tCandidate Screening\n•\tAI Conversational Chatbot\n•\tDynamic Talent pooling\n•\tExtensive library of pre-built dashboards\n•\tCreate custom dashboards with our no-code drag-drop self-service functionality\n•\tAI Data Analyst\n•\tBulk Email and SMS\n•\tCustomize the recruitment process with a No-code drag and drop process builder\n•\tAutomate candidate touchpoints and candidate engagement with no-code drag-drop Journey builder.\n•\tAi Enabled Career portal\n•\tMobile-Enabled candidate portal\n•\tReferral Management\n•\tIntegrations with 80+ ATS including Workday, SAP SuccessFactors, Taleo and others"}, {"id": "rfp_152", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "How can your platform be customized to meet our organization's specific needs?  What is your expected timeline for implementation of new features / functionalities?", "answer": "The KnowledgeHub platform is designed with high configurability, leveraging no-code technology to enable Elevance to tailor various aspects such as recruiting workflows, applicant workflows, reporting and analytics, automated campaigns, talent pools, and custom fields. As a highly iterative company, we adhere to the operating principles established by Sam Altman, CEO of OpenAI: listen to customers, iterate, launch, and repeat. Our iteration cycles are every 4 hours, allowing us to implement new features and functionalities within a timeframe ranging from as little as 4 hours to a maximum of 3 weeks, depending on the complexity of the request."}, {"id": "rfp_153", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Please detail how users can customize/ automate workflows in your Direct Sourcing Platform?", "answer": "Using our no code technology, Elevace users can create autoamted workflows (candidate journeys) to support different job titles."}, {"id": "rfp_154", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Is your application Multi-Tenant or Single Tenant?   Also, please describe how your application’s ability to offer a white-labeled/client-branded service?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub AI is designed as a multi-tenant application, allowing multiple clients to utilize the platform simultaneously while keeping their data segregated and secure. Additionally, our platform offers a robust, out-of-the-box, no-code solution for client branding. Clients can fully customize the candidate-facing career portal to reflect their unique brand identity. This includes the ability to incorporate their specific logo, color scheme, chosen font size, and style. Clients can also upload their own images and favicons to further personalize the portal, ensuring a cohesive and branded user experience that aligns with their corporate aesthetics."}, {"id": "rfp_155", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Does the application incorporate artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning, and robotic process automation? If so, please briefly describe including the context in which the capability is utilized, and the resulting benefits.", "answer": "Conforms \"Out of Box\""}, {"id": "rfp_156", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "How does your application architecture promote performance? How slow is the slowest page you have running in production?", "answer": "Datadog is utilized for SIEM, providing real-time monitoring and incident response, while SSL/TLS encryption is implemented at the application level for data protection. Using AWS WAF (Web Application Firewall) further enhances security by protecting web applications from common cyber threats such as SQL injection and cross-site scripting attacks."}, {"id": "rfp_157", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Describe your Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) and associated timeframes.   Please provide any active quality certifications (e.g., CMMI, Capability Maturity Model Integration). Include verifying documentation where possible.", "answer": "Here is the overview of our Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) policy.\nCURATELY AI INC. is a highly iterative company, capturing customer feedback and working on enhancements with a 4-hour iterative cycle. Enhancements are released and the process is repeated. This culture and philosophy drive our SDLC process, which includes the following stages: Requirement Gathering, Design, Development, Testing, Implementation, Operations, and Maintenance.\nRequirement Gathering Stage\nFor each new feature being planned to any software or for changes to existing features, the high-level requirements should be documented by the Product team in consultation with business users. The output of the requirement gathering will form inputs for the Design team.\nWhere required, it is the responsibility of the Product team to ensure the high-level requirements are detailed into low-level/functional requirements to better facilitate the subsequent tasks of design and development.\nDesign Stage\nThe Design team is responsible for detailing the UI and UX flows for the requirements shared by the Product team. These details are important inputs to the Engineering team to plan out their development activities.\n Development Stage\nThe inputs from the Product team and Design team form the basis for planning the development stage.\nTeam leads in the engineering team are responsible for breaking down the requirements into tasks and ensuring all engineers are aware of the tasks assigned to them.\nEngineers are responsible for following secure coding practices during development. They should also ensure the use of the latest code libraries and fix any code-level vulnerabilities.\nAll development activities should be facilitated by appropriate version control systems to ensure the latest version of code is used for development.\nThe Engineering Head and Infosec officer must ensure the development environment is segregated from the staging and production environments.\nTesting Stage\nAll features shall be tested after the development is done.\nTesting should be performed by any user apart from the developer to ensure segregation of duties. It is recommended to ensure the software is working as intended.\nThe Engineering Head and Information Security Officer must ensure that testing happens in a staging environment separate from the development and production environments.\nOnly after adequate testing is completed, the deployment process should commence.\nDeployment Stage\nAny deployment should follow the change management process. It is essential that all deployments are tracked via a version control system or ticketing tool.\nAll deployments/changes must be approved before merging with production code by an independent engineer who is different from the author to ensure segregation of duties.\nMaintenance Stage\nThe engineering team must facilitate the reporting of any errors or bugs identified by the end users. All such errors/bugs must be tracked.\nAny changes related to bug fixes must follow the change management process."}, {"id": "rfp_158", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Which systems and applications have you successfully integrated with (e.g., E-mail, Text)?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub seamlessly integrates with various productivity tools such as email, calendars, SMS, and Zoom. It also connects with over 80 Applicant Tracking System (ATS) platforms, including Workday and SAP SuccessFactors. Additionally, KnowledgeHub integrates with Vendor Management System (VMS) platforms like Fieldglass, Beeline, and VNDLY, as well as assessment platforms like Criteria Corp. For job postings, KnowledgeHub links directly with job boards such as Indeed, LinkedIn, and Monste"}, {"id": "rfp_159", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "How have you configured your application to ensure system availability on a 24-hour basis?", "answer": "To ensure 24/7 availability, our SaaS application employs the following measures:\n\nCloud Infrastructure: A global cloud network provides redundancy and automatic failover.\n\nRedundant Architecture: Multiple layers of redundancy protect against hardware failure.\n\nRegular Backups: Automated backups allow for quick data restoration when necessary.\n\nProactive Monitoring: Continuous monitoring detects and resolves issues preemptively.\n\nDisaster Recovery Plan: A well-defined plan ensures rapid system restoration.\n\nMaintenance Windows: Scheduled maintenance is planned to minimize disruptions.\n\nSecurity Protocols: Robust security measures safeguard against potential attacks."}, {"id": "rfp_160", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "What is your application capacity for the number of users and data transactions? How many simultaneous users can your application support effectively? What is the historical maximum?", "answer": "Our application is built on a modern tech stack and hosted on AWS, providing robust scalability and reliability. Designed to support growth and adapt to changing demands, our application ensures high scalability for both users and data transactions without compromising performance.\n\nUser Capacity: Our application can support a significant number of simultaneous users, with the flexibility to adjust based on client needs. Leveraging AWS's infrastructure, we can scale resources as required. Historically, our platform has effectively managed tens of thousands of simultaneous users during peak usage and is continuously optimized for increased loads.\n\nData Transactions: Engineered to handle a high volume of operations seamlessly, our system utilizes advanced AWS services for rapid data processing and responsiveness. The architecture is optimized for efficiency and speed, enabling a large number of transactions per second, scalable according to demand."}, {"id": "rfp_161", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "What type of network perimeter security is implemented at the hosting site?", "answer": "Datadog is utilized for Security Information and Event Management (SIEM), providing real-time monitoring and incident response, while SSL/TLS encryption is implemented at the application level for data protection. Additionally, AWS Web Application Firewall (WAF) enhances security by protecting web applications from common cyber threats such as SQL injection and cross-site scripting attacks.\n\nFor Intrusion Detection and Prevention (IDPS), Datadog's monitoring capabilities and Quick Heal's endpoint security provide comprehensive protection. Datadog detects potential threats in real-time and aids in incident response, while Quick Heal's IDPS monitors system activities and blocks suspicious behavior to prevent unauthorized access. The use of AWS Virtual Private Clouds (VPCs) enables network segmentation to isolate different parts of the hosting environment, ensuring that sensitive data and services are protected from unauthorized access.\n\nNetwork Traffic Filtering is achieved through AWS Network Access Control Lists (ACLs), which enable fine-grained control over inbound and outbound traffic. This allows the restriction of traffic to and from specific IP addresses, protocols, or ports, providing an additional layer of security at the network perimeter. Secure Socket Layer (SSL) and Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocols are used to encrypt data during transmission, ensuring that sensitive information remains confidential and protected against interception.\n\nAWS Web Application Firewall (WAF) filters malicious traffic targeting web applications, defending against various web vulnerabilities like SQL injection and cross-site scripting. It provides customizable rules to block or allow traffic based on specific patterns. Overall, these layers of security—including network segmentation, intrusion detection and prevention, and encryption—create a robust network perimeter that minimizes the risk of unauthorized access and data breaches at the hosting site."}, {"id": "rfp_162", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "What type of intrusion detections and monitoring are in place at the hosting site?", "answer": "We use Datadog and Quickheal for intrusion detection and monitoring."}, {"id": "rfp_163", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "What backup and recovery capabilities are provided in your application? Please briefly describe.", "answer": "In our SaaS application, we provide comprehensive backup and recovery capabilities designed to ensure data integrity and availability, even in the event of system failure or data loss. Here is a brief description of these capabilities:\n\nAutomated Backups: The application automatically performs regular backups of all data, including user data, application settings, and system configurations. These backups are scheduled during off-peak hours to minimize impact on system performance and ensure up-to-date data restoration capabilities.\nRedundant Storage: Backup data is stored in redundant formats across multiple secure, geographically dispersed data centers. This redundancy not only protects against data loss due to physical damage at one location but also improves data recovery times.\nEncryption: All backed-up data is encrypted using industry-standard encryption protocols both in transit and at rest. This ensures the security and privacy of your data against unauthorized access.\nPoint-in-Time Recovery: Our application supports point-in-time recovery, allowing users to restore data from any specific time point at which a backup was taken. This feature is particularly useful for recovering from data corruption or loss incidents.\nDisaster Recovery: We have robust disaster recovery processes in place that include detailed plans for rapid recovery in various scenarios. These plans are regularly tested to ensure they are effective and can be activated immediately when needed.\n\nContinuous Monitoring and Alerts: The system continuously monitors the health of the backup and recovery setup, providing alerts on issues like failed backups or potential security breaches, ensuring proactive management of data integrity."}, {"id": "rfp_164", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "What is your standard system up-time rate? Please provide an up-time report. When was the last system outage?", "answer": "The standard system uptime rate is 99.9%, with any outages typically occurring during scheduled maintenance to ensure optimal performance and security. Our most recent system outage was on March 31, 2024, due to server maintenance and disaster recovery plan testing.. Please see attachment 9.4.14 KnowledgeHub Uptime report."}, {"id": "rfp_165", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Describe your standard methodology for handling platform maintenance and upgrades. Is there a documented contingency and business continuity plan for hosting your platform? If yes, please include a copy in your response.", "answer": "Standard Methodology for Handling Platform Maintenance and Upgrades\n\nPlanning and Notification:\n\nScheduled Maintenance: Regular maintenance windows are scheduled to ensure minimal disruption to service. Maintenance activities are planned during off-peak hours, and stakeholders are notified in advance through emails, dashboard notifications, or SMS.\n\nImpact Analysis: Before any upgrade or maintenance, an impact analysis is conducted to understand the potential effects on various system components and stakeholders.\n\nTesting and Validation:\n\nStaging Environment: All upgrades and patches are first tested in a staging environment that mirrors the production environment to ensure they do not introduce new vulnerabilities or bugs.\n\nValidation Checks: Post-deployment validation checks are performed to ensure that the system operates as expected without any issues.\nImplementation:\n\nRollout Strategy: Upgrades are rolled out incrementally, starting with less critical systems before updating critical production systems. This phased approach helps isolate issues before they affect the entire platform.\n\nMonitoring: The system is closely monitored for any irregularities or performance issues during and after the upgrade. Monitoring tools and dashboards are utilized to keep real-time tabs on the platform's health.\nDocumentation:\n\nChange Logs: All changes are documented, including details about the system’s state before and after the maintenance, to assist in future audits and troubleshooting. \n\nA detailed business continuity plan is also documented and attached."}, {"id": "rfp_166", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "How often do you provide updates or enhancements to your platform?", "answer": "The assigned KnowledgeHub Account Manager will meet with the Elevance team monthly to review new enhancement updates. For urgent requests affecting Elevance performance, we will provide updates on the status of development and notify Elevance as soon as the enhancement has been released."}, {"id": "rfp_167", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "How do you stay up to date with industry trends and advancements to continuously improve your support offerings?", "answer": "Staying up to date with industry trends and advancements is crucial for continuously improving our support offerings. Here are some ways we achieve this:\n\nIndustry Research and Publications: We regularly review industry reports, whitepapers, and publications from leading analysts and research firms to stay informed about the latest trends and technological advancements. Examples include Staffing Industry Analysts (SIA), Everest Group, and Ardent Partners.\n\nProfessional Networks and Conferences: Our team actively participates in industry conferences, webinars, and networking events. These platforms provide valuable insights, foster connections with industry leaders, and offer opportunities to learn about new tools and best practices. We attend the SIA Contingent Workforce Strategies conference, VMS Professionals, ClubVMSA, Institute of Supply Chain Management (ISM) conferences, Sourcing Industry Group (SIG), HR Tech, and others.\n\nCustomer Feedback: We place a strong emphasis on listening to our customers. Regular feedback sessions, surveys, and user group meetings help us understand their evolving needs and challenges, allowing us to tailor our support offerings accordingly.\n\nTraining and Development: Continuous professional development is encouraged within our team. We invest in ongoing training programs and certifications to ensure our staff is knowledgeable about the latest technologies and industry standards.\n\nCollaborations and Partnerships: We collaborate with technology partners and industry associations to stay at the forefront of innovation. These partnerships often provide early access to new tools and technologies, enabling us to integrate cutting-edge solutions into our support offerings.\n\nInternal Innovation: We foster a culture of innovation within our organization. Regular brainstorming sessions, hackathons, and innovation challenges encourage our team to develop new ideas and improvements for our services.\n\nBy leveraging these strategies, we ensure that our support offerings continuously evolve to meet the demands of the dynamic direct-sourcing technology landscape."}, {"id": "rfp_168", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "How do you stay up to date with industry trends and advancements to continuously improve your support offerings?", "answer": "A significant portion of our product enhancements stem directly from feedback provided by our clients and partners. Additionally, our team maintains active engagement with prominent industry analysts, including Staffing Industry Analysts (SIA), VMSA, the American Staffing Association (ASA), TalentBelt, Ardent Partners, and Forrester, among others. This engagement ensures we stay abreast of the latest trends and developments in the workforce solutions industry, including updates on regulatory requirements, labor laws, and other factors influencing the landscape."}, {"id": "rfp_169", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "How does your platform ensure regulatory compliance to relevant Industry laws and standards (ex: Artificial Intelligence, co-employment)?", "answer": "Our platform is designed with a strong commitment to upholding regulatory compliance and adhering to industry-specific laws and standards. Here’s how we ensure compliance:\n\n1. Continuous Monitoring and Updates: We actively monitor legal and regulatory changes that impact the HRtech industry, including emerging standards related to artificial intelligence and other issues. Our legal team works closely with regulatory experts to understand these changes and their implications for our platform and our clients.\n\n2. Compliance by Design: Our platform incorporates compliance into the product design and development stages. This approach includes embedding privacy, security, and compliance features into the software architecture, ensuring that compliance is an integral part of the user experience and not just an afterthought.\n\n3. Artificial Intelligence Governance: For features powered by artificial intelligence, we implement a governance framework that addresses ethical considerations, data bias, transparency, and accountability. We ensure that our AI algorithms are auditable and comply with relevant AI ethics and fairness guidelines.\n\n4. Data Protection and Security: We adhere to stringent data protection regulations, such as GDPR and CCPA, ensuring that personal data is processed securely and with the necessary consents. Our security measures include data encryption, secure data storage, and controlled access, which safeguard sensitive information from unauthorized access or breaches.\n\n5. Employee Training and Awareness: We conduct regular training sessions for our employees on compliance issues, focusing on areas critical to our industry such as data protection, and AI ethics. This training ensures that our team is equipped to handle compliance proactively.\n\n6. Legal and Compliance Resources: We have a dedicated compliance team, including legal experts who specialize in employment law and the specific challenges of the HRtech sector. This team is tasked with ensuring that our platform continuously meets all regulatory requirements and industry standards.\n\n7. Client Collaboration: We work directly with our clients to ensure that the platform meets their specific compliance needs. This includes configuring the platform to align with local employment laws and industry standards and providing detailed documentation on how we manage compliance."}, {"id": "rfp_170", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "How is data backup and disaster recovery handled?", "answer": "Data backup and disaster recovery are crucial for maintaining data integrity and ensuring business continuity. Here’s how we handle these processes:\n\nRegular Data Backups: We implement automated backups of all critical data at regular intervals. This ensures that the most recent version of the data is always available for recovery. The frequency of these backups is based on the data's importance and our clients' business requirements.\n\nSecure Storage: Backup data is stored in multiple, geographically dispersed data centers that offer robust physical and cybersecurity protections. This setup mitigates risks associated with physical damage, such as natural disasters, and provides redundancy to ensure data availability.\n\nEncryption: All data, both in transit and at rest, is encrypted using industry-standard encryption protocols. This practice safeguards the data from unauthorized access, enhancing security during the backup and restore processes.\n\nDisaster Recovery Planning: Our disaster recovery plan outlines specific strategies and procedures to recover from various types of data loss incidents. This plan is regularly updated and tested to ensure its effectiveness and to adapt to new technological and business developments.\n\nTesting and Drills: Regular testing of the backup and recovery processes is conducted to ensure they are functional and efficient. This includes drills that simulate various scenarios, helping to identify any weaknesses in the recovery plan and ensuring that our team is prepared for real-life data recovery operations.\n\nPoint-in-Time Recovery: Our systems are capable of point-in-time recovery, allowing us to restore data to a specific moment before a corruption or loss occurred. This capability is critical for minimizing the impact of data integrity issues.\n\nMonitoring and Alerts: Continuous monitoring systems are in place to detect and alert on issues that could affect the backups or the overall data integrity. This proactive monitoring helps in quickly addressing potential problems before they escalate."}, {"id": "rfp_171", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Does your company have System and Data Security Certifications (e.g., ISO, ISAE, SSAE, HIPAA, PCI/DSS)? Please provide an overview.", "answer": "Yes, We have ISO 27701 Data privacy certification. Please see attachment 9.5.3 ISO 27701"}, {"id": "rfp_172", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "How does your company guarantee compliance with Private Data Protection Laws (for example GDPR in EU, Privacy Shield, CCPA)?", "answer": "Our company is deeply committed to ensuring compliance with global data protection laws, such as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) in the EU, Privacy Shield, and the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA). To achieve this, we have implemented comprehensive privacy policies and procedures that govern the meticulous handling of personal data across our operations.\n\nWe proactively address Data Subject Rights requests with established mechanisms that ensure responses are timely and effective, safeguarding the rights of individuals to access, correct, delete, or transfer their personal data. Our approach includes systematic processes to handle such requests efficiently, ensuring compliance with specific regulatory timelines and requirements.\n\nAdditionally, we maintain a rigorous privacy compliance program that continuously monitors changes in data protection laws and adapts our practices accordingly. This dynamic program ensures that our data handling practices are always in alignment with the latest legal standards and best practices.\n\nTo further bolster our commitment to data privacy, we employ a full-time Data Privacy Officer (DPO) whose role is dedicated to overseeing our data protection strategy and compliance. The DPO ensures that privacy considerations are an integral part of our business operations and helps foster a culture of data protection within the organization.\n\nMoreover, we engage with one of the most renowned data privacy consulting firms, retained on a continual basis, to provide expert guidance and verify our adherence to privacy regulations. This collaboration helps us stay ahead of regulatory changes and implement best-in-class privacy protections.\n\nThrough these structured approaches and dedicated resources, our company not only complies with but strives to exceed the requirements of international data protection laws, thereby safeguarding our clients' and their customers' privacy."}, {"id": "rfp_173", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Does the solution store or process any data that Elevance Health would consider confidential, sensitive or non-public? What security measures are in place to protect sensitive candidate and company data?", "answer": "No, The solution does not store any data that Elevance Health would consider confidential, Sensitive or non-public."}, {"id": "rfp_174", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "What is your process for testing prior to production implementation of new features?", "answer": "Our process for testing prior to production implementation of new features includes:\n\nUnit Testing: Developers run unit tests to identify errors early in individual components.\nCode Review: New features are peer-reviewed for coding standards and potential issues.\nIntegration Testing: Features are tested alongside other modules to ensure proper interaction.\nAutomated Testing: Automated tests identify regressions and validate edge cases for compatibility.\nPerformance Testing: Load and stress tests confirm that performance remains stable under varying conditions.\nUser Acceptance Testing (UAT): End-users or stakeholders evaluate the feature in a controlled environment to verify it meets business requirements.\nSecurity Testing: Vulnerability assessments are conducted to detect and address security risks.\nStaging Environment Testing: The feature is deployed in a staging environment that mirrors production, ensuring realistic testing.\nRelease Approval: Following successful testing, the feature is approved for deployment to the production environment."}, {"id": "rfp_175", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Is there an admin feature to allow an administrator role to have more control over access level for users?", "answer": "Conforms \"Out of Box\""}, {"id": "rfp_176", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Describe how candidates can be vetted using a screening process?", "answer": "In KnowledgeHub, candidates can be effectively vetted using a comprehensive screening process tailored to each job. Our platform allows you to create unique screening questions, including essential knock-out questions, and seamlessly integrate them into the applicant workflow. With our intuitive, no-code drag-and-drop screening question builder, you can design role-specific questions and apply conditional logic to automatically advance, reject, or hold candidates based on their responses.\n\nAdditionally, you can easily clone these screening questions and assign them to various job postings with just one click, ensuring consistency and efficiency across your hiring processes. Candidates can respond to these questions either through the online application process or by interacting with our AI conversation chatbot.\n\nMoreover, KnowledgeHub empowers you with the ability to create data keys for each screening question. This feature allows you to filter applicants, generate detailed reports, and analyze responses to refine your screening strategy continually."}, {"id": "rfp_177", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Please briefly describe your company’s  mobile application, specifically how candidates maintain their profile and other functionalities that you have.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is designed as a Progressive Web Application (PWA), which combines the best of both websites and native apps to offer a seamless user experience across devices. Candidates can easily maintain their profiles and access other functionalities, benefiting from the mobile-friendly interface, offline availability, push notifications, and location-based features. The PWA is also optimized for search engine indexing, ensuring maximum visibility. \n\nWith this flexibility, KnowledgeHub provides an intuitive and versatile solution that adapts to your needs, whether on desktop or mobile. Here is the link to a recent article from Adobe about the benefits of PWA and how some of the largest brands like Starbucks and Uber are using Progressive Web Apps (PWA) to Increase engagement, increase mobile sessions, and decrease bounce rate: \n\nhttps://business.adobe.com/blog/basics/progressive-web-app-examples"}, {"id": "rfp_178", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "For SMS, is it a shared number? How would a candidate respond via SMS, is it directly to the recruiter?", "answer": "We offer both options one shared number for all recruiters or individual number for each recruiter depending on client preference.  When candidates respond via SMS the recruiter receives the sms message in KnowledgeHub application, they can also choose to be notified via email when they are away from their desk."}, {"id": "rfp_179", "category": "System Functionality", "question": "Is there a way to capture notes and tag candidates to a specific req? Are tags customizable?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_180", "category": "System maintenance, support and updates", "question": "How is maintenance and support provided by supplier to client, MSP, and candidate? Please share the current support structure", "answer": "Clients and MSP can reach out to our support via email, in-app chat or Phone. Clients and MSPs are provided with a dedicated customer success manager who will serve as their central point for all support needs. In addition, candidates can reach support via email or text?"}, {"id": "rfp_181", "category": "System maintenance, support and updates", "question": "How are new updates/advancements communicated and implemented? Do customers have the option to opt in or out of these software updates?", "answer": "Updates/Advancements are communicated via email, in-app notification and release notes in the knowledgebase. Customers do not have option to opt-out of the software updates."}, {"id": "rfp_182", "category": "System maintenance, support and updates", "question": "Are there specific ownership rules around who provides update support?", "answer": "Our Customer success team is responsible and owns the function of providing update support."}, {"id": "rfp_183", "category": "System maintenance, support and updates", "question": "How often are updates being done?", "answer": "Bug Fixes are done within 4 hours to 24 hours based on the critically of the bug, New feature release, improvements and updates are done weekly."}, {"id": "rfp_184", "category": "Talent Pools", "question": "How does your technology support building client-specific talent pools? What are the advantages to the customer with this approach vs a shared talent pool model where multiple clients leverage a shared database?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub builds talent communities using a multi-channel sourcing approach that includes clients' known candidates, a referral channels, and job boards. \n\nKnowledgeHub has the unique feature that allows clients to passively grow their talent community by leveraging our Public Marketplace of 650M candidates.\n\n If a use case requires multiple clients to share a community, we can support that. However, in our experience, the shared database approach is typically applied in non-Direct Sourcing scenarios."}, {"id": "rfp_185", "category": "Talent Pools", "question": "Does your software integrate with client career pages or do you build custom career pages hosted elsewhere?", "answer": "Yes. We build custom career pages that are hosted by KnowledgeHub which can be linked with clients career pages."}, {"id": "rfp_186", "category": "Talent Pools", "question": "Is there the ability for the client or TAPFIN to build careers sites independently within the software or is this provided by your company?", "answer": "Yes. Using the standard Careers page template, TAPFIN can configure client branding through our self-service feature."}, {"id": "rfp_187", "category": "Talent Pools", "question": "Do we build careers sites from templates or are they custom configured?", "answer": "We provide a template for TAPFIN to use."}, {"id": "rfp_188", "category": "Talent Pools", "question": "What best practices would you recommend regarding the use of client brand assets within published sites/pages/forms that candidates will access?", "answer": "Best practices include;\n- Use both the Client & TAPFIN logo on all landing pages and communications. \n- Clearly articulate to the candidate the partners involved in the Direct Sourcing program\n- Recruiters should use the client's email domain"}, {"id": "rfp_189", "category": "Talent Pools", "question": "Does your technology have the ability to create multiple talent pools within a single instance?  (For example, if a client wished to maintain separate pools of talent for different regions of the world with different teams supporting the process and controlling data.)", "answer": "In this scenario, we would create talent pools based on region. By utilizing user permissions and assigning roles to specific jobs and pools, we can control and limit access to the pools, jobs, and candidates."}, {"id": "rfp_190", "category": "Talent Pools", "question": "Does your technology allow for the curation of shared talent pools that could be accessed by multiple teams supporting different clients?  If so, are there any limitations to this setup?", "answer": "Yes, we would create a primary community to house all candidates. For each secondary community, we can establish an integration that automatically matches candidates to jobs and dynamically populates talent pools in the secondary community from the primary community. This allows your Curator to stay within one community while leveraging candidates from another."}, {"id": "rfp_191", "category": "Templates", "question": "What do the communications look like via email? Can we brand them or does it look like a generic email?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub can provided fully branded HTML or Text email’s."}, {"id": "rfp_192", "category": "Training", "question": "What training is provided for administrators and users, and what resources are available for ongoing training?", "answer": "We offer comprehensive training programs for both users and administrators, ensuring that all participants are well-equipped to utilize our application effectively.\n\nFor Users:\nWe conduct four detailed 60-minute training and workshop sessions, designed to cover every critical aspect of our application. These sessions include:\n\nJob Creation and Posting: Learn how to create job listings and post them both on your career portal and external job boards.\nApplicant Management: Gain insights into managing applicants effectively, from initial contact through the hiring process.\nAI Matching and Talent Pools: Explore how to use artificial intelligence to match candidates with jobs and how to create dynamic talent pools.\nPersonas and LinkedIn Integration: Understand how to build personas and make use of our LinkedIn Chrome extension for enhanced recruitment.\nAnalytics and Custom Reports: Delve into the analytics, learn to interpret various reports and dashboards, and customize them according to your needs.\nWorkflow Customization: Get hands-on experience in creating and customizing workflows and hiring processes.\nJourney Creation: Learn how to create user journeys within the application to streamline processes and enhance user experience.\nFor Administrators:\nAdministrators receive a specialized 75-minute live training session that focuses on:\n\nUser Permissions and Management: Detailed guidance on creating and managing user permissions to ensure secure and efficient operation.\nCompany Settings: Instructions on how to adjust company settings to align with organizational needs and preferences.\nOngoing Learning and Support:\nTo support continuous learning and adaptation, we provide a self-paced eLearning library. This resource features a comprehensive collection of videos that cover every aspect of the application. It allows users to learn at their own pace and revisit the material anytime for a refresher."}, {"id": "rfp_193", "category": "User Roles", "question": "The system can be extended with a hiring manager portal. Granting the client’s hiring manager(s) access", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_194", "category": "General", "question": "What percentage of the work is being performed in-house vs. being outsourced to a 3rd party provider?", "answer": "100% in-house"}, {"id": "rfp_195", "category": "Public Marketplace", "question": "Where do the profiles in your platform come from?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub collaborates with various partners to compile profile data from a variety of compliant sources. This profile data may include links to, information from, or data shared by the following platforms (among others):\n\nLinkedIn\nX (Twitter)\nGithub\nStack Overflow\nGoogle Scholar\nCrunchbase\t\nConferences\t\nDribbble\nFacebook\nWellfound\nQuora\tXing\nMeetup\nMedium\nEllo\t\nGravatar\nStack Exchange\nFoursquare\t\nGoogle Developer\t\nGitLab\nReddit\t\nRubyGems\t\nDEV\t\nAnd More…"}, {"id": "rfp_196", "category": "Legal", "question": "Is KnowledgeHub a Data Processor or a Data Controller", "answer": "THIS ANSWER MUST BE CONFIRMED BY MANISH PRIOR TO SENDING IT TO ANY CLIENT\n\n\nSummary: Data Controller vs. Data Processor\nIn the context of data protection laws such as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), the roles of data controllers and data processors are defined to establish responsibilities for handling personal data. Below is a summary of each role and how they apply to a platform housing candidate data.\n\n1. Data Controller\nDefinition:\nA data controller determines the purposes and means of processing personal data. Essentially, they decide why and how personal data will be processed.\nResponsibilities:\nEnsure that data processing complies with applicable laws (e.g., GDPR).\nObtain necessary consents from data subjects (candidates, in this case).\nDefine the retention period for data and ensure its secure deletion when no longer needed.\nRespond to data subject rights requests (e.g., access, rectification, deletion).\nExample:\nA company (e.g., a recruitment agency or employer) decides to collect, store, and process candidate data for hiring purposes. This company would be the data controller since it determines the reason and method for data processing.\n2. Data Processor\nDefinition:\nA data processor processes personal data on behalf of the data controller. The processor follows the instructions of the controller and does not determine the purposes or means of data processing.\n\nResponsibilities:\nOnly process data as instructed by the data controller.\nImplement appropriate security measures to protect the data.\nNotify the controller of data breaches.\nMaintain records of processing activities as required by law.\n\nExample:\nA third-party platform that stores or processes candidate data (e.g., a recruitment software or ATS) without deciding why or how the data is used would be a data processor.\nIs a Platform Housing Candidate Data a Data Controller or Processor?\n\nScenario 1: Data Processor:\nIf a platform only provides storage and processing functionality (e.g., talent management software or applicant tracking system) and follows the explicit instructions of the client (e.g., an employer or agency), the platform acts as a data processor.\n\nExample: A software provider that manages candidate data storage and automates communication as instructed by the employer.\n\nScenario 2: Data Controller:\nIf the platform decides how and why candidate data is processed, such as by determining which data is collected, how it is used, or if it uses the data for its own purposes (e.g., improving its services), it acts as a data controller.\n\nExample: A platform that uses candidate data to build talent pools, independently contacts candidates, or markets its own services would likely be classified as a data controller.\nImportant Considerations\nJoint Controllers: In some cases, a platform may act as a joint controller with the client if both entities share responsibility for determining the purposes and means of data processing.\nHybrid Roles: A platform could act as a processor for some activities (e.g., storing candidate data) and a controller for others (e.g., using anonymized data for analytics).\nKey Determination: The role depends on the level of control the platform has over the data and its processing purposes."}, {"id": "rfp_197", "category": "Direct Sourcing Experience", "question": "What percentage of customers \"curate\" direct sourcing in-house versus external?", "answer": "Based on our experience, the majority of programs (over 80%) utliize third-party curation teams."}, {"id": "rfp_198", "category": "Best Practices", "question": "Which roles do you recommend for direct sourcing? All or just key repeatable ones? Why?", "answer": "All roles should be posted through Direct Sourcing rather than limiting it to only repeatable positions. A strong curator, paired with the right tools such as KnowledgeHub, will succeed in identifying and engaging top talent—whether it’s a one-time hire or a high-volume, repeat position.\n\nDirect sourcing is designed to maximize employer branding, reduce hiring costs, and improve candidate quality across all roles. While repeatable positions may benefit from talent pools and pipeline-building, one-time hires still gain efficiency through AI-driven matching, proactive outreach, and faster time-to-fill. By consistently posting all roles, Hilton ensures full utilization of the direct sourcing program, leading to greater cost savings, higher-quality placements, and a more strategic approach to workforce planning."}, {"id": "rfp_199", "category": "Training", "question": "Training: What training resources and support do you offer to ensure our team can effectively use the software?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub offers comprehensive training resources and ongoing support to ensure Hilton’s team can effectively utilize the platform. Our dedicated Customer Success Manager (CSM) will provide hands-on training, ongoing guidance, and best practices to maximize adoption and efficiency.\n\nUser Training\n\nWe conduct four detailed 60-minute training and workshop sessions, covering every critical aspect of the platform, including:\n\n• Job Creation and Posting – How to create and post job listings on the career portal and external job boards.\n• Applicant Management – Managing applicants from initial contact through the hiring process.\n• AI Matching and Talent Pools – Leveraging AI to match candidates with jobs and build dynamic talent pools.\n• Personas and LinkedIn Integration – Creating recruitment personas and using our LinkedIn Chrome extension for enhanced sourcing.\n• Analytics and Custom Reports – Understanding dashboards, reports, and how to customize them for specific needs.\n• Workflow Customization – Hands-on training in creating and optimizing workflows and hiring processes.\n• Journey Creation – Learning how to build user journeys within the application to streamline processes and improve candidate experience.\n\nAdministrator Training – For platform administrators, we provide a specialized 75-minute live training session focused on:\n\n• User Permissions and Management – Configuring user access and permissions for secure and efficient operations.\n• Company Settings – Adjusting company-wide settings to align with Hilton’s hiring and compliance requirements.\n• Ongoing Learning & Support\n\nTo ensure continued learning and easy reference, we provide:\n\n• Self-Paced eLearning Library – A comprehensive video resource covering all aspects of the platform, allowing users to learn at their own pace and revisit materials as needed.\n• CSM-Led Office Hours & Ad Hoc Training – Our Customer Success Manager (CSM) will be available for Hilton’s team to provide one-on-one coaching, Q&A sessions, and refresher training as needed.\n\nWith structured live training, self-paced learning resources, and dedicated CSM support, Hilton’s team will have everything needed to effectively use KnowledgeHub and drive hiring success."}, {"id": "rfp_200", "category": "Program Structure", "question": "Direct Sourcing Program Structure: How do you define a properly structured comprehensive direct sourcing program? What is required, and who is needed?", "answer": "A properly structured Direct Sourcing program requires strategic alignment, clearly defined roles, robust training, and ongoing stakeholder engagement. The foundation of success lies in a well-coordinated team, clear objectives, and a flexible approach that adapts to evolving needs.\n \nKey Elements of a Successful Direct Sourcing Program\n\n1. Alignment with Organizational Objectives\n• The Direct Sourcing program must align seamlessly with Hilton’s workforce strategy to drive efficiency and cost savings.\n• Regular assessments ensure that hiring goals remain consistent with broader business objectives.\n2. Clearly Defined, Measurable Goals\n• Establishing SMART (Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound) goals ensures a clear roadmap for success.\n• These goals guide hiring managers, recruiters, and curators in tracking performance and making data-driven improvements.\n3. Stakeholder Engagement & Buy-In\n• Engaging key stakeholders early in the planning phase ensures alignment across departments, driving adoption.\n• Cross-functional collaboration fosters a seamless experience between hiring managers, HR, and talent curators.\n4. Agile Project Management & Change Management\n• Direct Sourcing requires an iterative approach, allowing flexibility to adapt to market conditions and hiring trends.\n• Proactive change management strategies ensure smooth adoption, with clear communication on new workflows and expectations.\n5. Robust Training & Ongoing Support\n• A comprehensive training and support structure ensures that all participants—hiring managers, curators, and program administrators—fully understand the platform and processes.\n• Post-implementation support includes helpdesk services, refresher training, and continuous performance monitoring.\n \nImplementation & Operational Teams\nA successful Direct Sourcing program requires expert resources to ensure both seamless implementation and long-term operational success.\nImplementation Team (Pre-Launch Phase)\n\nThis 12-person team is responsible for launching the program and ensuring Hilton’s Direct Sourcing solution is effectively deployed.\n\n• VP of Product Enablement (Curation Services) – Leads the implementation process, manages timelines, and ensures smooth transition.\n• Program Director – Works closely with Hilton to define the program scope, goals, and reporting requirements.\n• Core Operational Team (Program Ambassador, Talent Curation Manager, Sourcing Specialist) – Focused on hiring needs, job intake, market research, and sourcing strategies.\n• Talent Marketing Specialist – Manages Hilton’s employer branding, marketing content, and social media presence.\n• Reporting & Analytics Specialist – Develops customized reports and dashboards for tracking program performance.\n• CEO – Ensures strategic alignment and removes obstacles that may hinder implementation.\n• Technical Analyst – Builds workflow automations to streamline processes.\n• Content Specialist – Develops candidate engagement materials, email communications, and video content.\n• Business Process Analyst – Documents business processes and creates workflow diagrams to ensure efficiency.\n• Customer Success Manager (CSM) – Serves as the primary point of contact for Hilton’s team, providing ongoing training, platform optimization, and user adoption support throughout the implementation.\n \nPost-Implementation (Ongoing Operations Team)\n\nOnce the program is launched, key team members remain to ensure long-term success, while some disengage.\n\nCore Operational Team (Ongoing)\n• Program Director\n• Program Ambassador\n• Talent Curation Manager\n• Sourcing Specialist\n• Customer Success Manager (CSM)\n\nExtended Strategic Support\n• CEO\n• Chief Strategy Officer\n\nSupport as Needed\n• Talent Marketing Specialist\n• Reporting & Analytics Specialist\n\nRoles That Disengage Post-Implementation\n• Implementation Manager (Curation Services)\n• Technical Analyst\n• Content Specialist\n• Business Process Analyst"}, {"id": "rfp_201", "category": "General", "question": "What is your typical implementation timeline, and what resources will be required from our side?", "answer": "A typical implementation can be completed in 6 - 8 weeks. Sometimes faster if the client can quicly obtain approvals.\n\nExecutive Sponsor - The Executive Sponsor will assist in setting the strategy, obtaining internal approvals, and resolving escalations. Two Hours Per Week - Weekly thirty minute meetings & Ad Hoc discussions pertaining to approvals\n\nPlatform Super User - The Platform Super User will closely align with the Executive Sponsor and the KnowledgeHub implementation team. This team member will be heavily involved in creating operational procedures and learning how to utilize the self-service features. Alongside the Executive Sponsor, this user will need to collaborate with TalentNet on the transition. Sixteen Hours Per Week - Weekly thirty minute meetings, Ad Hoc discussions to operational items, Managing internal discussions to obtain team guidance\n\nMarketing - Marketing has already approved the use of brand and images in the prior project. Their role will be to provide approvals on any changes. Additionally, they will assist in adding the KnowledgeHub link to the clients careers page. Less than five hours for the project\n\nLegal - The legal team will review and approve any topics around co-employment and bias in AI. In most cases, the legal team will require a clear distinction between contract worker community and a full-time hire community. This is the reason that KnowledgeHub,AI supports dual logo's on candidate facing content. You will see an illustration of this in our simulations. Less than five hours for the project.\n\nInformation Technology - Limited involcement from IT. They will review any InfoSec requirements. Less than five hours for the project.\n\nMSP Team Lead - Engagement from the MSP team is critical to the success of the program. While not all members need to be involved in the implementation, having a representative who can partner with the Platform Super User and KnowledgeHub is essential to ensure alignment of operational elements necessary for compliance and connectivity with the payroll team. The MSP Team Leader and the Platform Super User could potentially be the same full-time employee (FTE). - Two Hours Per Week\n\nCuration Team - The Curation Team will be involved during the training phase. It would also be prudent to keep them informed of the implementation progress and the features that will begin to benefit them once they are live on the new platform."}, {"id": "rfp_202", "category": "General", "question": "How long from go live does it typically take to reach \"steady state\" in terms of roles handled via direct sourcing?", "answer": "Assuming the recruitment team is staffed correctly and best practices are in place, steady state can be achieved within six months."}, {"id": "rfp_203", "category": "General", "question": "What integration lift, if any, should Hilton expect? Will internal Hilton technology input on integrations be required and if so, what specifically is needed?", "answer": "Hilton should expect minimal integration lift as all core integration efforts will be managed by KnowledgeHub, Beeline, and the MSP. Hilton’s IT team will not need to be involved in the integration process, except in one potential scenario:\n\nSingle Sign-On (SSO) Integration: If Hilton requires SSO for secure authentication, Hilton’s IT team may need to provide an API key to facilitate the connection.\nAll other technical integrations, data flows, and system connections will be handled directly between KnowledgeHub, Beeline, and the MSP, ensuring a seamless and low-effort implementation for Hilton."}, {"id": "rfp_204", "category": "General", "question": "What continuous improvement programs do you offer?", "answer": "the company takes an iterative approach to continuous improvement, providing a white-glove service to ensure our clients receive maximum value. We consistently evaluate and enhance platform features to drive meaningful impact. Beyond just using the platform, we offer strategic consulting to help optimize business processes, ensuring seamless adoption and fostering long-term growth for your organization."}, {"id": "rfp_205", "category": "General", "question": "On a $75M program ($60M open-sourced today), what savings should Hilton expect by implementing direct sourcing. Explain the logic and math.", "answer": "In Hilton’s competitively bid $60M program, the approximate pay rates total $41.67M after accounting for a typical 44% markup in the market (information compiled from Staffing Industry Analysts). KnowledgeHub’s pricing model is designed to significantly reduce costs while maintaining high-quality talent acquisition. By growing Hilton’s direct sourcing program, KnowledgeHub aims to capture up to 75% of the $41.67M competitive pay rates, equating to approximately $31.25M in pay rates annually. However, KnowledgeHub only charges fees on the first $7.94M, due to our $150K annual fee cap.\n\nThis structure allows Hilton to save money on the next $10.42M in pay rates, as no additional fees will be applied beyond the capped amount. Additionally, Hilton will realize platform savings of approximately $196,875, since KnowledgeHub will not be charging the standard 1.89% markup on that portion of pay rates.\n\nKnowledgeHub’s pricing includes monthly minimums of $6,000, ensuring flexibility and scalability while keeping costs predictable. The monthly maximum fee is capped at $12,500, ensuring that Hilton never pays more than $150,000 annually, regardless of spend.\n\nUnlike traditional pricing models where costs scale with spend, KnowledgeHub locks in fees, ensuring predictable, lower costs while still supporting a robust, scalable hiring program. Please keep in mind, that this will not happen in year one but will grow within the first 24-36 months."}, {"id": "rfp_206", "category": "General", "question": "Will you guarantee a savings percentage or value for Hilton? If so, how much?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub does not offer a guaranteed savings percentage or fixed value for Hilton. While we are confident that our technology, automation, and direct sourcing expertise will drive significant cost savings and efficiency, the overall success of the program depends on more than just technology.\n\nFor Hilton to fully realize the benefits of Direct Sourcing, it is essential to have strong executive sponsorship and a commitment to change management. Adoption across hiring teams, engagement from stakeholders, and adherence to program workflows all play a critical role in maximizing savings and optimizing talent acquisition. While KnowledgeHub provides the tools, expertise, and support to drive cost reduction, faster hiring, and improved candidate quality, factors such as internal adoption, hiring manager buy-in, and program compliance remain outside of our control.\n\nThat said, we will work closely with Hilton to track savings, optimize processes, and continually refine the program to ensure it delivers maximum financial and operational value over time."}, {"id": "rfp_207", "category": "General", "question": "Product Roadmap: What are your plans for future development and enhancements of the software?", "answer": "We have several significant and minor initiatives on our roadmap, all designed to accelerate speed to candidate, boost recruiter efficiency, enhance the overall talent experience, and address high-volume hiring needs. While we tend to be cautious in sharing details, we are excited to offer you a sneak preview of a major launch we’re rolling out in the next four to six weeks—our new AI Sourcing Assistant. We’ve created a brief video exclusively for Hilton to showcase this upcoming feature.\n\nhttps://share.vidyard.com/watch/JpLYmmGC4dzhEhyqyR8xHs\n\nOur product roadmap is primarily driven by the evolving needs of our customers, and our highly iterative approach ensures their feedback shapes our priorities. We look forward to collaborating closely with you as we continue to refine and expand our offerings."}, {"id": "rfp_208", "category": "General", "question": "Innovation: How do you stay ahead of industry trends and ensure your software remains competitive?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub stays ahead of industry trends and ensures our software remains competitive by continuously evolving our AI capabilities, industry insights, and customer-driven innovation. Our commitment to technology advancements in AI, Large Language Models (LLMs), Machine Learning (ML), and Agentic AI allows us to develop cutting-edge recruitment solutions. We incorporate Voice AI to automate candidate engagement, enabling scalable, real-time screenings, scheduling, and follow-ups, while AI-powered matching goes beyond keyword searches to understand contextual relevance, resulting in higher-quality candidate placements. Additionally, our Agentic AI automates recruitment workflows, reducing manual tasks and optimizing the hiring process. We continuously refine our AI and ML models based on real-world hiring data, ensuring improved accuracy and efficiency over time.\n\nTo stay informed on emerging industry trends, we actively review research from Staffing Industry Analysts (SIA), Everest Group, Ardent Partners, Forrester, and Gartner, tracking workforce innovations and new technologies. Our team also participates in key industry conferences and networks, including SIA’s Contingent Workforce Strategies Conference, VMS Professionals, ClubVMSA, the Institute of Supply Chain Management (ISM), Sourcing Industry Group (SIG), and HR Tech events. These engagements allow us to connect with thought leaders, explore new best practices, and gain early exposure to next-generation technology solutions.\n\nCustomer feedback plays a crucial role in how we enhance our platform. We conduct regular feedback sessions, user group meetings, and surveys to ensure that our technology aligns with real-world hiring challenges. Through pilot programs and continuous software updates, we refine our offerings to provide practical, intuitive, and results-driven solutions. Additionally, our culture of internal innovation encourages ongoing AI and ML training, hackathons, and strategic brainstorming sessions, allowing us to explore new and disruptive recruitment technologies.\n\nOur collaborations and strategic partnerships with workforce strategy consultants, and technology providers keep us at the forefront of recruitment innovation. These partnerships provide early access to next-gen tools and automation platforms, ensuring that KnowledgeHub remains a market leader in direct sourcing technology. By continuously improving through advanced AI, data-driven decision-making, industry engagement, and customer input, we deliver a cutting-edge, scalable, and cost-effective hiring solution that drives measurable success for our clients."}, {"id": "rfp_209", "category": "General", "question": "What, if any, ESG policies does your company have in place? Please list them all and include a description of each.", "answer": "As a SaaS company, the company adheres to key Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) principles to ensure responsible business practices.\n\nFrom an Environmental perspective, the company prioritizes energy efficiency and carbon footprint reduction by leveraging cloud-based infrastructure that minimizes physical hardware usage and optimizes resource allocation. The company also supports remote work policies, reducing the need for commuting and office-related energy consumption.\n\nOn the Social front, the company is committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion (DEI) by fostering an inclusive workplace, implementing fair hiring practices, and ensuring unbiased AI-driven recruitment technology. Additionally, the company prioritizes data privacy and security, adhering to industry best practices and compliance standards such as GDPR and CCPA to protect user information. Furthermore, the company emphasizes employee well-being and ethical labor practices, ensuring that workplace policies support mental health, work-life balance, and professional development.\n\nIn terms of Governance, the company maintains strong corporate ethics and compliance standards, ensuring transparency in operations, responsible AI usage, and accountability in decision-making. The company also adheres to regulatory compliance in SaaS operations, ensuring secure, ethical, and legal technology deployment. Additionally, the company upholds supplier and partner responsibility, working only with ethical vendors and maintaining high integrity in business partnerships.\n\nBy integrating these ESG principles, the company demonstrates its commitment to sustainable, responsible, and ethical business practices in the SaaS industry."}, {"id": "rfp_210", "category": "General", "question": "Does your company participate in the EcoVadis Sustainability Assessment and maintain a valid scorecard?   - If yes, please provide your latest scores (overall and individual themes) and when you last completed assessment.   - If no, please indicate your willingness to complete an EcoVadis Sustainability Assessment.", "answer": "We have not participated in the EcoVadis Sustainability Assessment, but are willing to complete it."}, {"id": "rfp_211", "category": "General", "question": "What ESG certifications have you obtained? Please describe.  (Examples include: management system certifications like ISO 14001, 26000, 45000, and 50001; green building certifications like LEED, WELL, Living Building, Energy Star, and TRUE)Does your company have a policy on forced labor, human trafficking, workplace discrimination and/or child exploitation? If yes, please upload a copy.", "answer": "NA"}, {"id": "rfp_212", "category": "General", "question": "Conduct risk assessments across your operations", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_213", "category": "General", "question": "Review country risks in which you operate", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_214", "category": "General", "question": "Map your supply chain against potential risks", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_215", "category": "General", "question": "Establish standard practices to address human rights concerns or issues", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_216", "category": "General", "question": "Train or educate employees on human rights", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_217", "category": "General", "question": "Report on human rights business practices (internally and/or publicly)", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_218", "category": "General", "question": "What practices have you established in your supplier identification and onboarding processes to protect human rights and reduce risks of human trafficking?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is committed to protecting human rights and mitigating risks of human trafficking through rigorous supplier identification and onboarding practices. We conduct thorough due diligence on all suppliers, ensuring compliance with labor laws, ethical hiring standards, and anti-trafficking regulations. Our process includes vendor screenings, contractual commitments to fair labor practices, and regular audits to uphold responsible sourcing. Additionally, we require transparency in supply chains, mandating that all partners adhere to zero-tolerance policies for forced labor and exploitation. Through these measures, KnowledgeHub ensures a safe, ethical, and compliant workforce environment."}, {"id": "rfp_219", "category": "General", "question": "Has your organization developed whisteblower mechanisms for stakeholders to report misconduct or potential violations of laws or policies? If yes, please describe.", "answer": "Yes, KnowledgeHub has established whistleblower mechanisms to ensure stakeholders can report misconduct or potential violations of laws or policies. Reports can be made directly to compliance officers or leadership, and all concerns are thoroughly investigated. We have strict anti-retaliation protections in place to encourage transparency and accountability. This framework ensures that ethical concerns are addressed promptly and that KnowledgeHub maintains a culture of integrity and compliance."}, {"id": "rfp_220", "category": "General", "question": "Do you conduct any audits or supplier reviews of the staffing companies you list on your platform? Please describe.", "answer": "This is not applicable as no staffing companies are listed on our platform. We are purely a SaaS platform."}, {"id": "rfp_221", "category": "General", "question": "How would you define private and public talent pools? Do you support talent communities that are both private and public?", "answer": "Public talent pools are broad, external talent sources accessible to anyone (job boards, social media sites) and are often unvetted and not yet connected to your brand. Candidates in Private talent pools can’t be seen by others outside of your organization and are curated sources of talent already familiar with or interested in your brand."}, {"id": "rfp_222", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe your talent pool technology capabilities and provide an overview of your differentiators.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub’s core capabilities include:  Branded Job Listing Page, AI driven job suggestions, AI Candidate Matching, Automated Email/SMS messaging, Candidate Engagement Tools, Automated Talent Pool development, Self Service Reporting/Analytics, Self-Service features including Workflows, Custom Fields, Brand Management, Reporting and Analytics, and a public marketplace of 700 million candidates globally."}, {"id": "rfp_223", "category": "General", "question": "What candidate data sources are required to scale Client's contingent talent community quickly?", "answer": "In order to scale your direct sourcing program as quickly as possible, we would prefer to include known talent sources such as alumni, past applicants, silver medalists, retirees, interns and past payrollees."}, {"id": "rfp_224", "category": "General", "question": "Do you offer assistance to clients with developing job descriptions?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_225", "category": "General", "question": "Do you help clients determine market rates for their job taxonomy? If so, how often do you review these with the client and do you provide reporting/analytics related to pay rate?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub integrates with select platforms, such as Brightfield’s Rate Intelligence Platform, to provide data-driven rate guidance for jobs and candidates. Access to tools like Brightfield requires an additional licensing fee. For pay transparency compliance, KnowledgeHub intuitively recognizes state-specific requirements, ensuring pay details are entered before a job posting can be published. This built-in compliance feature helps organizations stay aligned with evolving regulations while maintaining transparency and accuracy in job postings."}, {"id": "rfp_226", "category": "General", "question": "How does your technology ensure a great candidate experience?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub excels in candidate experience with intuitive navigation, AI-driven job matching (alerts, credential tools, chatbot), clear automated status updates, mobile-first design for on-the-go use, and transparent data privacy. By prioritizing usability, smart automation, communication, mobility, and security, it delivers a streamlined, trustworthy journey."}, {"id": "rfp_227", "category": "General", "question": "How does your technology identify candidates that are a match for a given job?", "answer": "Our AI-driven Smart Job Matching analyzes resumes to find roles matching skills even when titles differ. Skills-based matching surfaces opportunities. Our AI-powered chatbot guides candidates from resume upload to job discovery on a mobile-optimized platform. Users can set communication preferences, subscribe to AI-matched job alerts, and control personal data for a secure, tailored experience."}, {"id": "rfp_228", "category": "General", "question": "On average, how long does it take a candidate to sign up for a profile?", "answer": "15 seconds"}, {"id": "rfp_229", "category": "General", "question": "Please list all integrations (i.e. VMS) and describe the level of integration. Is the integration pre-built? What data can flow back and forth through the integration? Can you provide a list of reference clients who are live with your Beeline API? If any part of the API is currently being built/in process, please provide the ETA for completion.", "answer": "Currently, we have VMS integrations with Beeline, VNDLY and Fieldglass.  In addition, we have more than 80 ATS integrations as well as integrations with various 3rd party platforms utilized for background checks, video interviewing , assessments as well as multiple global job boards."}, {"id": "rfp_230", "category": "General", "question": "How does your technology facilitate engagement and communication with candidates?", "answer": "At KnowledgeHub, candidate engagement is powered by a mix of automation and personalized outreach to ensure every candidate feels connected throughout their journey. KnowledgeHub gives the Curation team options on how they want to configure the workflow when candidates join the community or apply to a job.  Recruiters can utilize automation such as chatbots, our AI Agent, automated campaigns, SMS texting, and email."}, {"id": "rfp_231", "category": "General", "question": "How does your technology enable curation partners to efficiently keep contingent talent communities engaged?", "answer": "Embedded in the KnowledgeHub platform is the capability for Curation Partners to create email campaigns and journeys that nurture the candidate community. Within a journey or campaign, the Curation Team can craft different experiences, like gathering information from candidates, conducting surveys, and creating calls to action that drive engagement. Additionally, the Curation Team can develop email templates for recruiters to use consistently across communications."}, {"id": "rfp_232", "category": "General", "question": "What sets your technology apart from others in terms of the candidate experience? Do you have a dashboard available to the candidate for them to understand what job matches they are aligned to and current status in real-time?", "answer": "Our candidate experience begins with an AI-powered search that identifies the best-matched jobs for each candidate. KnowledgeHub is designed as a mobile-first platform, ensuring an intuitive and seamless user experience. Additionally, we offer a conversational chatbot to enhance engagement. Real-time dashboards keep candidates informed of their application status."}, {"id": "rfp_233", "category": "General", "question": "Does your technology provide any options to ensure a candidate is a day 1 arrival? For example, a major challenge for Client can be drop outs for certain positions on day 1 of their assignment, where knowing the candidate is not going to show up can be a huge advantage to finding a replacement in a timely manner.", "answer": "We offer journeys that can be launched before the candidate's start date, prompting them to confirm their attendance for their first day"}, {"id": "rfp_234", "category": "General", "question": "Does your technology have any features that can aid a candidate when the curation team may not be available (for instance, a Chatbot)?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub offers a Voice AI Agent and Chatbot that are available 24/7."}, {"id": "rfp_235", "category": "General", "question": "How does your technology support a referral program within the direct sourcing platform?", "answer": "Our referral module offers a fully integrated system supporting easy referral submission via web and PWA, automatic multi-channel sharing with tracking, gamified engagement features (leaderboards, campaigns, micro‑rewards), transparent referral status updates, automated reward management, and deep ATS integration with analytics. These functionalities are built to the same standards as EmployeeReferrals.com, ensuring a robust, engaging, and efficient referral program experience."}, {"id": "rfp_236", "category": "General", "question": "How configurable are your platform and related processes?", "answer": "The KnowledgeHub platform is designed with high configurability, leveraging no-code technology to enable Elevance to tailor various aspects such as recruiting workflows, applicant workflows, reporting and analytics, automated campaigns, talent pools, and custom fields. As a highly iterative company, we adhere to the operating principles established by Sam Altman, CEO of OpenAI: listen to customers, iterate, launch, and repeat."}, {"id": "rfp_237", "category": "General", "question": "What supporting technologies are you integrated with or do you use to enhance your direct sourcing solution?", "answer": "We are integrated with multiple VMS technologies including Beeline, Fieldglass and VNDLY as well as more than 80 ATS platforms (in the event a client is looking for us to integrate with their internal ATS).  In addition, we are integrated with multiple Background Check organizations, and assessment platforms."}, {"id": "rfp_238", "category": "General", "question": "What balance do you suggest within your platform of human activity from the curator vs. automation within the process?", "answer": "We believe that technology is what enables the curation team to achieve exceptional outcomes. Therefore, we have developed a platform that was built to be highly collaborative with humans. Our recommendation is to allow AI to handle resume parsing, job matching, automated outreach, and routine update, and reserve human effort for relationship building, nuanced assessments, personalized engagement, and final decision-making. This blend ensures efficiency and empathy."}, {"id": "rfp_239", "category": "General", "question": "Is your technology mobile-enabled?", "answer": "Not only is the KnowledgeHub platform mobile-enabled, it is mobile-first. The difference is that a mobile-first platform is specifically designed to maximize the candidate's experience while using any mobile device."}, {"id": "rfp_240", "category": "General", "question": "Does your technology offer SMS texting?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_241", "category": "General", "question": "Provide an overview of disaster recovery procedures.", "answer": "Our SaaS platform offers robust backup and recovery to protect data integrity and ensure availability. We run automated, encrypted backups during off-peak hours, stored redundantly across secure, geo-diverse data centers. Point-in-time recovery allows precise data restoration. Disaster recovery plans are in place and regularly tested. Continuous monitoring and alerts help detect issues early, keeping your data safe and recoverable at all times."}, {"id": "rfp_242", "category": "General", "question": "What reporting/analytics do you offer to support direct sourcing metrics?", "answer": "Our platform offers 70+ built-in dashboards across six categories: Executive, Community, Recruiter Activity, Sourcing, Pipeline, and Hiring Insights. It also features a no-code, drag-and-drop builder for custom dashboards, plus export to Excel/CSV. An AI data analyst helps create reports, dashboards, and complex calculations, merging KnowledgeHub and Beeline data for comprehensive visualizations and data-driven decisions."}, {"id": "rfp_243", "category": "General", "question": "Do you provide scorecards related to curator and client performance?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_244", "category": "General", "question": "Do you provide market supply and demand reporting/analytics?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_245", "category": "General", "question": "How long does your average implementation take?", "answer": "The platform can be configured in less than a week, enabling clients to source candidates and match them against jobs, however the average implementation is approximately 6-8 weeks depending on scope.  In addition, implementation may be delayed due to client approvals for branding & messaging, the curation workflow process, and/or VMS integration. KnowledgeHub offers a workaround to simulate the VMS integration, eliminating the need for configured integrations to be complete prior to go-live."}, {"id": "rfp_246", "category": "General", "question": "What implementation resources do you suggest the client provides to the project? What time commitment or resources are necessary to ensure a successful launch?", "answer": "Executive Sponsor: Sets strategy, gains approvals, resolves escalations (2 hrs./week).\nPlatform Super User: Works with Sponsor and KnowledgeHub, manages setup, ops, and TalentNet transition (16 hrs./week).\nMarketing: Approves brand use and adds KnowledgeHub link (<5 hrs.).\nLegal: Reviews co-employment and AI bias; supports dual logos (<5 hrs.).\nIT: Reviews InfoSec needs (<5 hrs.).\nMSP Lead: Ensures compliance, partners with Super User (2 hrs./week).\nCuration Team: Trained and kept informed during rollout."}, {"id": "rfp_247", "category": "General", "question": "What resources will you provide to support implementation?", "answer": "We provide a dedicated team of functional and technical experts to support project management, platform configuration, and integration."}, {"id": "rfp_248", "category": "General", "question": "Can you share a typical implementation and change management plan for your technology platform?", "answer": "See Mastercard Direct Sourcing Deck"}, {"id": "rfp_249", "category": "General", "question": "What client dependencies exist to deploy your direct sourcing solution? What key factors are necessary for a successful implementation?  Outline your key learnings from previous implementations.", "answer": "Alignment among the Client, the MSP, and the Direct Sourcing program team is essential for the program's success. Clear communication regarding changes to business processes, including the removal of submittal limits and the first right of refusal on all requisitions, is critical. Please see the best practices in the attached deck."}, {"id": "rfp_250", "category": "General", "question": "What is your typical requisition through offboarding workflow?", "answer": "Please see attached Requisition workflow document."}, {"id": "rfp_251", "category": "General", "question": "After implementing a direct sourcing program, how long does it typically take until success is realized?", "answer": "It really depends on how Mastercard defines success.  KnowledgeHub will work with Mastercard to determine the outcomes you are looking to achieve through your direct sourcing program.  Together, we will determine the KPIs and metrics that are most important to you and will continuously measure our success against those KPIs and metrics, and will report our progress on regular basis (to be determined by Mastercard)."}, {"id": "rfp_252", "category": "General", "question": "Based on what you know of Client's program and requirements related to direct sourcing, please list your top 2 recommendations for a curation partner that would make your technology the most successful, if chosen. Please include reasons for why you feel that curation partner would best fit if partnered with your technology.", "answer": "Given that AGS is the MSP, our recommendation is to have AGS also do the curation. Our shadowing team can support a faster ramp and scale. If Mastercard selects a different curation partner, we’re fully capable of collaborating, bringing year of exercise working with various third-party partners."}, {"id": "rfp_253", "category": "General", "question": "Please provide your pricing model for use of your technology application based on the information provided by Client. If needing clarification, please send questions. If applicable, please provide alternative pricing models that reflect a breadth of options you see evolving in the industry, as well as any dependencies.", "answer": "We offer flexible pricing models aligned to Mastercard’s goals. Options include: (1) fixed annual subscription based on curator usage, (2) percentage of contingent labor spend, tiered by volume. Our goal is to deliver maximum value while ensuring scalability, transparency, and cost-efficiency as the program grows."}, {"id": "rfp_254", "category": "General", "question": "Please provide any pricing differences for various regions (if applicable differences exist between the US and other countries the Client program could support).", "answer": "SMS costs differ by country. For countries with higher costs than the United States, those additional fees will be passed through at cost."}, {"id": "rfp_255", "category": "General", "question": "Do you offer volume discounts or tiered pricing based on the amount of spend going through the direct sourcing program? If so, please provide as part of your pricing.", "answer": "We offer tiered pricing based on the amount of spend."}, {"id": "rfp_256", "category": "General", "question": "Please note any other costs, minimums, or fees required to implement & manage your proposed solution if you were awarded the business.", "answer": "No other costs, Minimums or implementation fees."}, {"id": "rfp_257", "category": "General", "question": "Do you have a preference for contracting directly with the client, vs. through a direct sourcing partner who is paid by the client?", "answer": "We are flexible and have experience with the client directly holding the contract, as well as the MSP or Curation Partner holding the contract. We want to make this as easy of a process as possible for Mastercard and are open to your preference."}, {"id": "rfp_258", "category": "General", "question": "Do you require a minimum contract duration?", "answer": "Our typical contract length is 3 years."}, {"id": "rfp_259", "category": "General", "question": "Can you share your standard contract documents a client would be required to sign? If so, please send along with this RFI response.", "answer": "We are OK to sign the clients contract document. We do have a standard contract and will be sharing as pert of the RFI response for your review if you prefer to sign our contract document."}, {"id": "rfp_260", "category": "General", "question": "Please outline the features and tools your technology uses to attract talent.", "answer": "Our platform keeps candidates actively engaged with Mastercard through multi-channel outreach, using automation, targeted campaigns, and AI-driven journeys. From the moment talent joins the Mastercard talent community, we enable continuous interaction. During implementation, we collaborate with the curation team to design tailored engagement strategies that adapt as hiring needs evolve."}, {"id": "rfp_261", "category": "General", "question": "How does your tool leverage a client’s brand to improve Direct Sourcing?", "answer": "The platform will utilize the client's brand across the job listings page, email communications, and other channels to effectively source and engage candidates."}, {"id": "rfp_262", "category": "General", "question": "Describe your approach to landing page management and maintenance.", "answer": "Clients and the MSP can reach out to our support team via email, in-app chat or Phone. Clients and MSPs are provided with a dedicated Customer success Manager who will serve as their central point contact for all support needs. In addition, candidates can reach support via email, in-app chat or text."}, {"id": "rfp_263", "category": "General", "question": "Can existing workers from a client be added to your system?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_264", "category": "General", "question": "Can we export data out of your system? If yes, are there limitations?", "answer": "We have certain report downloads available in our standard dashboards. We can also create custom report downloads per your request."}, {"id": "rfp_265", "category": "General", "question": "Do your dashboards reflect real-time status data? If no, please describe the latency.", "answer": "Yes, Dashboards reflect real-time status data"}, {"id": "rfp_266", "category": "General", "question": "Does your platform have the ability to personalize content based on candidates’ unique profile data (e.g. location, skills, demographics, certifications, etc.)?", "answer": "Yes, To our knowledge we are the only platform that has the personlization capability."}, {"id": "rfp_267", "category": "General", "question": "How does your technology manage security for user access?  Please describe.", "answer": "Clients can create specific user roles and assign permissions to each role, controlling what users can view and the actions they can perform. Additionally, clients can directly deactivate users within the platform."}, {"id": "rfp_268", "category": "General", "question": "How does your technology manage data privacy?  Please explain.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is built with privacy by design. We comply with GDPR, CCPA, and other relevant regulations. Candidate data is collected with consent, securely stored, and access-controlled. Users can manage, export, or delete personal data as needed. Role-based access, audit logs, and regular reviews ensure data is used responsibly and transparently."}, {"id": "rfp_269", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe your minimum encryption standard for secure data transmission.", "answer": "We use TLS 1.2 or higher for all data transmission, ensuring data is encrypted in transit using industry best practices. Our platform supports strong encryption algorithms such as AES-256 and RSA with secure key exchange protocols. We also enforce HTTPS across all endpoints and regularly test for vulnerabilities."}, {"id": "rfp_270", "category": "General", "question": "Does your company have experience working with different program structures (i.e. 3rd Party Curation, MSP-managed, Internally-managed)?  Please describe.", "answer": "Yes.  KnowledgeHub has experience working with multiple curation partners, multiple MSP partners as well as clients who are internally managing their program."}, {"id": "rfp_271", "category": "General", "question": "Does your company have experience working with VMS and non-VMS supported programs?", "answer": "Yes, we can support both types of programs."}, {"id": "rfp_272", "category": "General", "question": "Besides VMS, does your technology integrate with any 3rd party technologies (e.g. talent attraction, engagement, or management, etc.)?  Please explain.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub integrates with multiple technologies and platforms including ATS, assessments, background checks, job boards, and social media sites."}, {"id": "rfp_273", "category": "General", "question": "Does your technology have AI capabilities for ranking candidates?  Please explain.", "answer": "Yes, the platform uses evaluation criteria derived from the job description to score candidates based on their match. It also provides the recruiter with context explaining the candidate's score."}, {"id": "rfp_274", "category": "General", "question": "Does your technology have AI capabilities for creating requisitions and job descriptions?", "answer": "Yes, Our platform offer capability to create job descriptions from Job title and also offers capabilities to re-write/Re-format job description that come from VMS portal to clean up any sensitive information, re-word to remove any implied bia from the original job description."}, {"id": "rfp_275", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe your communication capabilities (e.g. text, voice, email, chatbots, etc.).", "answer": "KnowledgeHub offers several options for communication including Chatbots, Voice AI Agent, SMS Text, and Email."}, {"id": "rfp_276", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe your talent segmentation capabilities.", "answer": "We build client-specific talent pools using a multi-channel sourcing strategy, combining known candidates, referrals, and job boards. KnowledgeHub auto-populates pools with qualified talent based on match thresholds set by the curation team. As new candidates join Mastercard’s community, they’re added if they meet criteria, ensuring a steady, pre-vetted pipeline ready for current and future hiring needs."}, {"id": "rfp_277", "category": "General", "question": "Does your technology support multiple shift management?  Please explain.", "answer": "Yes, candidates can select their shift preferences in their profiles. Using this information, the platform matches jobs to candidates that align with their specified shift requirements."}, {"id": "rfp_278", "category": "General", "question": "Does your technology support time and expense management?  Please explain.", "answer": "Expense management is typically supported by the VMS."}, {"id": "rfp_279", "category": "General", "question": "Does your technology share requisitions on social media platforms?  Please explain.", "answer": "Yes. The platform provides the sourcing team with multiple options to share jobs via social media."}, {"id": "rfp_280", "category": "General", "question": "Does your technology share requisitions via online job boards? Please explain.", "answer": "The KnowledgeHub platform integrates with c1,000+ global job boards, making it easy for the curation team to share requisitions instantly and maximize reach."}, {"id": "rfp_281", "category": "General", "question": "Does your technology support client career site features?  Please explain.", "answer": "Yes, we can utilize the careers page to route candidates from there to contract jobs."}, {"id": "rfp_282", "category": "General", "question": "Can users access your technology from multiple devices (e.g., mobile, desktop)?", "answer": "Users can access our platform via their mobile phone, iPad, laptop or desktop computer."}, {"id": "rfp_283", "category": "General", "question": "Does your technology support multiple languages, tax rates, and currencies?  Please explain.", "answer": "Aspects of our platform are English only, however the candidate career portal is offered in multi-language and data is hosted regionally. KnowledgeHub is in final stages of launching a multilingual career portal, expected to launch within the next six weeks. This will enable users to seamlessly engage with our services in their preferred language, further enhancing the reach of our technology. We support multiple currencies, however tax rates are typically housed in the VMS."}, {"id": "rfp_284", "category": "General", "question": "How are users given access to your technology?", "answer": "The curation team administrator can create user roles and permissions, granting users access to the platform. If needed, the KnowledgeHub Customer Success Manager can also assist with creating user accounts."}, {"id": "rfp_285", "category": "General", "question": "Do you provide technical support? Please explain.", "answer": "Mastercard will receive full support across technical help, billing, and general services. Users can access our online support team, including a chatbot and live agents. In addition, a dedicated U.S.-based Customer Success Manager will offer personalized support and best practices, our finance team will handle billing needs, and escalations will be managed by our VP of Product Enablement with CPO support. A structured process ensures all issues are quickly and effectively resolved."}, {"id": "rfp_286", "category": "General", "question": "Do you provide training for new users / clients?  Please explain.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub offers comprehensive training resources and ongoing support to ensure the curation team can effectively utilize the platform. Our dedicated Customer Success Manager (CSM) will provide hands-on training, ongoing guidance, a robust library, and best practices to maximize adoption and efficiency."}, {"id": "rfp_287", "category": "General", "question": "Please share a high-level product roadmap for upcoming new features and enhancements.", "answer": "Our roadmap features initiatives to accelerate candidate sourcing, improve recruiter efficiency, enhance talent experience, and support high-volume hiring. Driven by customer needs and iterative feedback, we prioritize what matters most to you. Though typically private, here’s a sneak peek: our AI Sourcing Assistant launches in 4–6 weeks. We look forward to partnering with you as we evolve our offerings."}, {"id": "rfp_288", "category": "General", "question": "What are the top three differentiators of your technology?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is built by curators, for curators—enabling full-cycle sourcing, matching, engagement, and conversion in one seamless platform. Unlike others, we don’t rely on third-party systems or external tools. Our all-in-one solution drives curator productivity, faster time-to-fill, and immediate program success, reducing friction and delivering high-impact results from day one."}, {"id": "rfp_289", "category": "General", "question": "What candidate sourcing features differentiate you from your competition?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub’s AI-driven platform enhances curation and talent pool building with powerful tools like AI-matching, a public talent pool of 700M+ global profiles, and automation. Our Voice AI agent, Maya, handles high-volume candidate engagement, while our conversational chatbot streamlines interactions. Plus, our automated workflow builder ensures seamless sourcing, screening, and engagement—delivering top talent faster and more efficiently."}, {"id": "rfp_290", "category": "General", "question": "What AI features differentiate you from your competition?", "answer": "The KnowledgeHub platform has developed Agentic AI feature sets that enhance the ability to rapidly source and qualify candidates for jobs. By leveraging these AI features, the time to submit candidates and overall candidate satisfaction significantly improves."}, {"id": "rfp_291", "category": "General", "question": "What candidate search features differentiate you from your competition?", "answer": "A key differentiator of KnowledgeHub is its ability to passively grow talent communities through its Public Marketplace, which provides access to a database of 700+ million global candidates. Mastercard can use this feature to continuously expand its reach and identify top talent without relying solely on traditional sourcing methods. Additionally, KnowledgeHub's LinkedIn Chrome Extension allows recruiters to source talent directly from LinkedIn and seamlessly add them to Mastercard's talent pools."}, {"id": "rfp_292", "category": "General", "question": "Who will have access to the data", "answer": "Individuals invited to the private Curatley instance, including the curation team, will have access to the data. Additionally, the KnowledgeHub support and product team, along with our sub-processors such as AWS and Twilio, will have access."}, {"id": "rfp_293", "category": "General", "question": "What talent community management features differentiate you from your competition?", "answer": "Advanced automation features include Journeys, Campaigns, and Workflows. Access a People Database with over 700 million candidate profiles globally, Agentic AI features, and advanced reporting capabilities, including 75 prebuilt dashboards and the ability to create custom reports. The platform is architected to easily integrate with Beeline"}, {"id": "rfp_294", "category": "General", "question": "What skill taxonomy/structure features differentiate you from your competition?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub uses a proprietary AI-powered skill and job taxonomy that normalizes job titles, skills, and industries for better candidate matching. Unlike static libraries, our taxonomy evolves with market trends and integrates real-time data from 200M+ profiles. This enables more accurate search, match, and talent insights—faster and with higher precision than traditional keyword-based systems."}, {"id": "rfp_295", "category": "General", "question": "Please outline any certifications or recognition that your company has and maintains that relate to this RFP.", "answer": "Verified by NYC Bias Audit, and compliant with ISO 27001, ISO 27701, SOC 2 Type 2, and CCPA standards."}, {"id": "rfp_296", "category": "General", "question": "Please list any partnerships that you currently that complement or enable your technology.  Please elaborate on the benefit it would have for Mastercard.", "answer": "Beeline: We have a strong partnership and recently completed a Fortune 50 integration in 4 weeks with zero escalations; one of Beeline's smoothest ever. AGS: We are actively working with JoAnn Estrada and her team to establish a strong, strategic partnership. While still in early stages, our discussions have been productive and focused on identifying key areas where we can align and add value. In addition, we have 1000+ integrations with global job boards and 80+ ATS integrations."}, {"id": "rfp_297", "category": "General", "question": "Minimum Service Level: 99.95% uptime", "answer": "KnowledgeHub AI, Inc."}, {"id": "rfp_298", "category": "General", "question": "Credit: Compensation equivalent to the number of minutes the service was unavailable. Please see below for each service level credit.", "answer": "No"}, {"id": "rfp_299", "category": "General", "question": "Average Page Response Time:", "answer": "Our philosophical approach is rooted in the belief that great hiring starts with human connection, technology should empower, not replace it. We envision a unified direct sourcing platform that removes fragmentation by combining talent sourcing and engagement into one seamless experience. By integrating multiple point solutions, we reduce complexity, eliminate inefficiencies, and put talent at the center—enabling organizations to build deeper, more agile relationships with their workforce."}, {"id": "rfp_300", "category": "General", "question": "Minimum Service Level: 2.00 seconds or less", "answer": "KnowledgeHub AI has been in business since 2020."}, {"id": "rfp_301", "category": "General", "question": "Credit: If the response time exceeds 2.00 seconds, a credit is applied equal to 10% of the monthly fee multiplied by the excess time.", "answer": "Currently, KnowledgeHub employs 48 people across the U.S. and India.  The executive and customer success teams are located in the U.S., and our product team is primarily based in India."}, {"id": "rfp_302", "category": "General", "question": "Incident Resolution Service Credits:", "answer": "Verified by NYC Bias Audit, and compliant with ISO 27001, ISO 27701, SOC 2 Type 2, and CCPA standards."}, {"id": "rfp_303", "category": "General", "question": "Priority 1 (Critical Issues) – Resolution within 4 hours (24x7 support)", "answer": "KnowledgeHub was born out of ASK Consulting, a leading staffing firm, and built by recruiters to solve real-world hiring challenges. In response to urgent hiring needs during COVID-19, ASK developed a custom platform to streamline high-volume hiring, quickly becoming a top supplier. The success led to the creation of CXninja, which evolved into KnowledgeHub. After strong feedback from a Fortune 50 client and Beeline, the platform was reimagined and officially launched in December 2023."}, {"id": "rfp_304", "category": "General", "question": "Credit: 10% of monthly fees if not met.", "answer": "There are no pending mergers, acquisitions or partnerships that will have an impact on the services we offer."}, {"id": "rfp_305", "category": "General", "question": "Priority 2 (High-Priority Issues) – Resolution within 12 hours (24x7 support)", "answer": "KnowledgeHub has been providing direct sourcing solutions since 2020."}, {"id": "rfp_306", "category": "General", "question": "Credit: 5% of monthly fees if not met.", "answer": "Since go-live on 9/6/24, BMS Contingent labor program has filled 175 jobs—138 via direct sourcing—with a 79% fill ratio and 17-day average time-to-fill. Realized savings exceed $390K, with projected savings over $5M. These results demonstrate KnowledgeHub’s ability to deliver quality hires faster and at scale, making it a strategic asset for enterprise hiring efficiency and cost optimization."}, {"id": "rfp_307", "category": "General", "question": "Priority 3 (Standard Issues) – Resolution within 3 business days", "answer": "Our team includes industry experts Karen Gonzalez, Julie Semler, and Manish Karani, who collectively bring 15+ years of experience in launching and managing direct sourcing programs. Karen and Julie have led over 20 enterprise program implementations, guiding clients through change management and driving adoption. Their expertise ensures high-impact, scalable, and sustainable program success."}, {"id": "rfp_308", "category": "General", "question": "Credit: TBD", "answer": "Our roadmap features initiatives to accelerate candidate sourcing, improve recruiter efficiency, enhance talent experience, and support high-volume hiring. Driven by customer needs and iterative feedback, we prioritize what matters most to you."}, {"id": "rfp_309", "category": "General", "question": "Priority 4 (Low-Priority Issues) – Resolution within 5 business days", "answer": "KnowledgeHub provides 70+ pre-built dashboards across six categories: Executive, Community, Recruiter Activity, Sourcing, Pipeline, and Hiring Insights, offering detailed operational views. Its no-code, drag-and-drop tool enables custom dashboard creation. Users can export data to Excel/CSV for analysis. KnowledgeHub’s AI data analyst aids in report generation, dashboard building, and complex calculations, integrating Fieldglass and KnowledgeHub data for comprehensive visualizations and data-driven decisions."}, {"id": "rfp_310", "category": "General", "question": "Credit: TBD", "answer": "We’ve invested heavily in AI-powered search/match, a proprietary skill taxonomy. We added workflow automation, and curator productivity tools. Service investments include implementation playbooks, recruiter training, and white-glove support. Over the next year, we’re investing in an in-app AI chatbot for 24/7 support, Slack/Teams integration for real-time assistance, and deeper analytics—enhancing both curator productivity and stakeholder experience."}, {"id": "rfp_311", "category": "General", "question": "What are the 2 differentiators that make you the best choice from your competitors?", "answer": "An all in one platform that encompasses multiple point solutions allowing the recruiter to work in a single technology coupled with Agentic AI for everything recruiting."}, {"id": "rfp_312", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe any organization strategy of your company that could have a material or significant impact on the services outlined in this RFP or on the structure and/or future of your business.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub’s core strategy is to continuously innovate our AI-driven platform to improve hiring quality, speed, and cost-efficiency. We are founder-led, privately held, and focused solely on direct sourcing technology. There are no planned structural changes that would impact service delivery—only continued investment in product advancement and enterprise success."}, {"id": "rfp_313", "category": "General", "question": "Provide your audited or unaudited financials for 2022, 2023 and 2024.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is a privately held, self-funded, and debt-free HR tech AI company. As such, we do not publicly disclose our financials at this stage. We would be happy to provide audited or unaudited financials under NDA if selected for further consideration in later stages of the evaluation process."}, {"id": "rfp_314", "category": "General", "question": "Did the COVID pandemic impact your company (financially, employees, etc.)?", "answer": "Curateley was founded during the first year of the COVID pandemic and did not have any negative financial impacts as a result of the pandemic. In fact, the COVID pandemic accelerated discussions regarding direct sourcing as organizations were looking for innovative ways to increase productivity and efficiencies, while reducing costs."}, {"id": "rfp_315", "category": "General", "question": "What types of industries do you primarily serve?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub provides services across multiple sectors including all major verticals."}, {"id": "rfp_316", "category": "General", "question": "Can you provide case studies,testimonials and references from other global clients? Pending down-selection, we will ask you to provide the contact names, email addresses and phone numbers.", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_317", "category": "General", "question": "Do you have a commerical payment processing partner, that could qualify as a Mastercard competitor such as American Express, Visa, etc.?", "answer": "We use Stripe as our commercial payment processing partner."}, {"id": "rfp_318", "category": "General", "question": "What is your overall client renewal rate?", "answer": "1"}, {"id": "rfp_319", "category": "General", "question": "Describe your mix of clients (include company names) you currently have with same size and scope as Mastercard and service globally", "answer": "We support large global enterprises including Bristol Myers Squibb (Fortune 50) and Axalta ($6B global manufacturer), delivering scalable direct sourcing programs across multiple regions. Our clients rely on KnowledgeHub for high-volume, high-impact hiring with measurable results. Our platform and services are built to support global scale, enterprise complexity, and localized compliance needs."}, {"id": "rfp_320", "category": "General", "question": "Who do you consider your 3 main competitors and why?", "answer": "TalentNet-they were the first technology to enter into the direct sourcing space, howver their technology is less agile and flexible and is somewhat antiquated compared to other technolgoies in the direct sourcing space. WorkLlama-they tend to be the lowest on price, yet lack the value that others bring to the table.  Opptly-they have robust AI, however their technology lacks the robust elements of other direct sourcing platforms."}, {"id": "rfp_321", "category": "General", "question": "Can the solution be co-branded?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_322", "category": "General", "question": "To what extent can a company customize the landing page of the tool (logos, branding, colors, etc.)?", "answer": "The KnowledgeHub platform is designed with high configurability, leveraging no-code technology to enable Elevance to tailor various aspects such as recruiting workflows, applicant workflows, reporting and analytics, automated campaigns, talent pools, and custom fields. As a highly iterative company, we adhere to the operating principles established by Sam Altman, CEO of OpenAI: listen to customers, iterate, launch, and repeat."}, {"id": "rfp_323", "category": "General", "question": "Do you have agile technology that enables you to address urgent ad-hoc requests and global market trends.", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_324", "category": "General", "question": "Do you have a market-leading, robust technology platform as evaluated by any reputed analyst organization, such as the Forrester, Everest Group, Gartner etc.", "answer": "Yes.  The KnowledgeHub platform has been reviewed by multiple analyst organizations."}, {"id": "rfp_325", "category": "General", "question": "Is the solution hosted on any SAAS/3rd party platform. Provide the hosting infrastructure, technologies used, compliance to standards (ISO, SOX, GDPR, etc.) and expansion capabilities", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is hosted on AWS using a secure, scalable cloud infrastructure with Docker and microservices. It aligns with AWS compliance standards including ISO 27001, SOC 2, SOX, and GDPR. Data is encrypted in transit and at rest, with role-based access controls. The platform is designed for rapid scaling to support global expansion."}, {"id": "rfp_326", "category": "General", "question": "What technical support resources are available?  \na. Support for administrators ?  \nb. Support of end users?", "answer": "For Users, we deliver four 60-min user training sessions covering job posting, applicant tracking, AI matching, personas, LinkedIn tools, analytics, workflows, and journey creation. Administrators receive a 75-min session on user permissions, company settings, and platform management. All sessions are hands-on and tailored to Hilton’s needs, with ongoing support to ensure success."}, {"id": "rfp_327", "category": "General", "question": "Are additional fees charged for any level of support?", "answer": "No"}, {"id": "rfp_328", "category": "General", "question": "Describe the process of escalating technical problems?", "answer": "Utilize KnowledgeHub’s live in-app chat for support or contact your Customer Success Manager directly. Our standard response times are: Level 1 issues resolved in under 1 hour, Level 2 in under 4 hours, and Level 3 in under 24 hours."}, {"id": "rfp_329", "category": "General", "question": "Is there a Service Level Agreement (SLA) governing response and escalation times for problems of different severity levels?  If so, please describe?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub’s Service Level Agreements (SLAs) ensure timely response and resolution for all client inquiries and issues. Our standard response times for issue resolution are:\n• Level 1 (Critical Issues): Resolved within under 1 hour\n• Level 2 (High-Priority Issues): Resolved within under 4 hours\n• Level 3 (Standard Issues): Resolved within under 24 hours"}, {"id": "rfp_330", "category": "General", "question": "How do you communicate service outages and resolutions to customers?", "answer": "Updates/Advancements are communicated via email, in-app notification and release notes in the knowledgebase."}, {"id": "rfp_331", "category": "General", "question": "What has been your system uptime, by month, for the last 12 months? Are there financial guarantees applicable to uptimes and/or response times?  How is this calculated? In other words, if you claim 90% uptime in a month, how long was the system down?", "answer": "Our system uptime over the past 12 months has averaged 99.89%. Uptime is calculated as total system availability excluding planned downtime. We offer financial guarantees tied to uptime and response times as part of our enterprise SLA, ensuring accountability and performance for our clients."}, {"id": "rfp_332", "category": "General", "question": "How often do you release product updates?  What did the previous two releases contain and when did they occur?", "answer": "New features are released in scheduled sprints. As they become available, the company will provide access to release notes. As a SaaS solution, minor features will be rolled out to all customers. For major releases, customers may have the option to opt out on a case-by-case basis."}, {"id": "rfp_333", "category": "General", "question": "What are expected upgrades and features in the next two releases? What is the reliability of the applications after an upgrade a new release?  If something is not working correctly, can the upgrade be undone?", "answer": "Upcoming releases include upgrades to the career page, improved data sync processes, and the launch of our AI-powered Journey Builder for automated talent engagement. Reliability is ensured through staged deployments, testing, and monitoring. If an issue arises, rollback procedures allow us to instantly revert updates, maintaining stability and minimizing disruption."}, {"id": "rfp_334", "category": "General", "question": "Are there separate fees for upgrades?", "answer": "Typically, there is no charge for upgrades to the platform, however we may develop new solutions or \"add-ons\" that may require an additional charge."}, {"id": "rfp_335", "category": "General", "question": "Describe the support level of the account manager? Customer success manager? Project lead? Customer service? From a technical perspective", "answer": "Customer support includes an Online Help Desk, bespoke training videos, in-app chat with a Technical Lead, and access to an Account Manager who will work with all of the key stakeholders to ensure program success."}, {"id": "rfp_336", "category": "General", "question": "Will admins have admin access to the platform? If yes or no, why?", "answer": "We can create an Admin role and they can access the system as needed."}, {"id": "rfp_337", "category": "General", "question": "How are you safeguarding user anonymity?", "answer": "We safeguard user anonymity through data minimization, role-based access controls, and optional anonymization of candidate data during early evaluation stages. Personally identifiable information (PII) is masked where applicable, and access is logged and monitored. Our platform complies with GDPR, CCPA, and ISO 27701, ensuring privacy and responsible data handling throughout the hiring process."}, {"id": "rfp_338", "category": "General", "question": "Does the tool have single sign-on capability?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_339", "category": "General", "question": "Can members access via user name password?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_340", "category": "General", "question": "Mobile/Mobile Application capability?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_341", "category": "General", "question": "How does the platform support Mergers & Aquisition's integrations", "answer": "KnowledgeHub supports M&A integrations through flexible APIs, modular architecture, and data portability features. We enable seamless migration or merging of talent data, user accounts, and workflows across entities. Role-based access ensures secure segregation during transition, while our team provides hands-on support for reconfiguration, identity mapping, and compliance alignment across systems."}, {"id": "rfp_342", "category": "General", "question": "Does the platform support identify propogation to other integrated systems.  Briefly describe on how this is achievable.", "answer": "Yes, KnowledgeHub supports identity propagation across integrated systems using secure APIs and SSO (SAML 2.0/OAuth 2.0). This ensures user identity and roles are consistently maintained when interacting with systems like VMS, ATS, or HRIS platforms. Our platform enables seamless, secure session continuity and auditability across the tech stack."}, {"id": "rfp_343", "category": "General", "question": "Mastercard Standard API integration is. Via. Oauth 2.0 with JWT and MTLS for data during transmission.  Describe how the platform can adhere to the integration standards.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub fully supports Mastercard’s integration standards using OAuth 2.0 with JWT for authentication and mutual TLS (mTLS) for secure data transmission. Our platform is built with enterprise-grade API security and can integrate seamlessly with Mastercard systems. We also support certificate-based authentication, token expiration policies, and encrypted data payloads to ensure compliance and secure communication."}, {"id": "rfp_344", "category": "General", "question": "Can the Architecture diagram of the application clearly articulating Multi Tenant Model (if any) and data storage location be shared ?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_345", "category": "General", "question": "Can you provide a Highlevel Technical Architectural and Data flow diagrams of the system", "answer": "Please see attached data flow diagram"}, {"id": "rfp_346", "category": "General", "question": "What are all the independent audits performed on the system (soc, PCI, DS, etc) and can you share the audit document.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is independently audited and certified for SOC 2, ISO 27001, and ISO 27701. These attest to our strong controls around data security, privacy, and operations."}, {"id": "rfp_347", "category": "General", "question": "Does the system involve sub processors if so please do include", "answer": "AWS – cloud hosting and infrastructure\n\nTwilio – SMS and email delivery services\n\nOpenAI – AI/NLP capabilities and GenAI features\n\nSendGrid – email marketing and bulk communication"}, {"id": "rfp_348", "category": "General", "question": "Do you support RESTful APIs or flat file integrations for custom workflows?", "answer": "Executive Sponsor: Sets strategy, gets approvals, handles escalations. 2 hrs/week. Platform Super User: Partners with Exec Sponsor and team to build procedures and use self-service;16 hrs/week. Marketing: Approves branding and adds KnowledgeHub link to careers page. < 5 hrs. Legal: Reviews co-employment/AI bias, ensures dual logos. < 5 hrs. IT: Reviews InfoSec. < 5 hrs. MSP Team Lead: Partners with Super User for compliance and payroll. 2 hrs/week.(Hours during implementation only)"}, {"id": "rfp_349", "category": "General", "question": "Is SSO (Single Sign-On) supported? Which identity providers are compatible (e.g., Okta, Azure AD)?", "answer": "Yes, KnowledgeHub supports Single Sign-On (SSO) using SAML 2.0 and OAuth 2.0 protocols. We are fully compatible with major identity providers including Okta, Azure AD, Google Workspace, and other SAML-compliant platforms. SSO ensures secure, seamless access for users and centralized identity management for enterprise IT teams."}, {"id": "rfp_350", "category": "General", "question": "Can your platform sync compensation or job data automatically on a scheduled basis?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_351", "category": "General", "question": "Do you provide webhooks or event triggers for real-time integration with internal systems?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_352", "category": "General", "question": "Is the platform cloud-native or hosted on-premises?", "answer": "The KnowledgeHub platform is Cloud Native"}, {"id": "rfp_353", "category": "General", "question": "What infrastructure providers do you use (e.g., AWS, Azure, GCP)?", "answer": "AWS"}, {"id": "rfp_354", "category": "General", "question": "What is your system uptime SLA (Service Level Agreement)?", "answer": "The standard system uptime rate is 99.9%, with any outages typically occurring during scheduled maintenance to ensure optimal performance and security."}, {"id": "rfp_355", "category": "General", "question": "How do you ensure platform performance during peak usage (e.g., merit cycles)?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is built on a scalable cloud-native architecture (AWS) with auto-scaling and load balancing to handle peak usage. We proactively monitor system performance, run regular stress tests, and allocate dedicated resources during high-traffic periods to ensure speed, stability, and responsiveness—even during peak activity like merit cycles or bulk sourcing events."}, {"id": "rfp_356", "category": "General", "question": "Is your solution modular or monolithic? Can we deploy components independently?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is a modular platform offers flexibility, scalability, and customization. It will allow Mastercard to add or adjust features as needs evolve, without disrupting the entire system.  Teams can tailor workflows , integrate with existing tools, and scale efficiently while improving agility and reducing costs."}, {"id": "rfp_357", "category": "General", "question": "Are you compliant with major security standards (e.g., SOC 2 Type II, ISO 27001, GDPR)?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_358", "category": "General", "question": "How is sensitive compensation data encrypted at rest and in transit?", "answer": "Sensitive compensation data is encrypted in transit using TLS 1.2+ and at rest using AES-256 encryption. All data is stored in encrypted volumes managed by AWS KMS, with strict access controls and role-based permissions. Regular audits and key rotation policies ensure ongoing compliance with SOC 2, ISO 27001, and ISO 27701 standards."}, {"id": "rfp_359", "category": "General", "question": "Can we configure role-based access control (RBAC) to restrict visibility by user type or department?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_360", "category": "General", "question": "What data retention and deletion policies do you support?", "answer": "We support configurable data retention and deletion policies based on client requirements and regulatory compliance. Data can be automatically purged after a defined period or upon request. Candidate data is deleted upon withdrawal or inactivity per GDPR/CCPA guidelines. Audit logs track all deletion activity, and backup data follows the same retention rules."}, {"id": "rfp_361", "category": "General", "question": "Do you conduct regular security audits or vulnerability assessments?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_362", "category": "General", "question": "How do you test new features or releases before rollout?", "answer": "Before rollout, new features undergo a structured testing process, including internal alpha testing, followed by a controlled beta phase with select clients. We use automated and manual testing for functionality, performance, and security. Feedback from beta users helps us refine features. Additionally, we run regression tests to ensure that new updates don’t impact existing functionality, followed by a staging deployment before final production release."}, {"id": "rfp_363", "category": "General", "question": "Do you offer a sandbox or staging environment for testing integrations and data?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_364", "category": "General", "question": "What is your release cycle, and how are changes communicated to clients?", "answer": "We have bi-weekly sprints where small fixes and features are released. Updates/Advancements are communicated via email, in-app notification and release notes in the knowledgebase."}, {"id": "rfp_365", "category": "General", "question": "Is there support for rollback or version control in case of errors?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_366", "category": "General", "question": "What is the maximum volume of users, job records, or comp bands the platform can handle?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is built to scale with enterprise needs. The platform supports over 100 million user records, 5,000,000+ job records, and 100,000+ compensation bands without performance degradation. Our cloud-native architecture on AWS enables elastic scaling, ensuring reliable performance during peak loads or large-scale programs across global teams."}, {"id": "rfp_367", "category": "General", "question": "Can you support global pay structures with multiple currencies and localization?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub supports multiple currencies."}, {"id": "rfp_368", "category": "General", "question": "How do you ensure data integrity during syncs or imports?", "answer": "We ensure data integrity through validation rules, checksums, and real-time error monitoring during syncs and imports. All data transfers are logged, and mismatches are flagged for review. Transactions are atomic to prevent partial updates, and rollback mechanisms are in place. Pre-sync staging and sandbox environments allow safe testing before live execution."}, {"id": "rfp_369", "category": "General", "question": "What performance metrics do you monitor (e.g., latency, API call success)?", "answer": "We monitor system latency, API call success/failure rates, uptime, page load speed, database response times, and job queue processing speed. Real-time dashboards and automated alerts help us proactively address performance issues."}, {"id": "rfp_370", "category": "General", "question": "How configurable is the system without vendor intervention (e.g., editing comp bands, user permissions)?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is highly configurable and offers robust self-service capabilities while also having access to our dedicated Customer Success Manager."}, {"id": "rfp_371", "category": "General", "question": "Are audit logs and activity histories available to administrators?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_372", "category": "General", "question": "Do you offer custom fields or workflows for unique business needs?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_373", "category": "General", "question": "Can admins create and manage user groups, roles, or access levels independently?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_374", "category": "General", "question": "Who will be responsible for the ongoing monitoring and performance of the solution?", "answer": "The assigned Customer Success Manager from KnowledgeHub will partner with the MSP and Curation team to monitor the overall solution."}, {"id": "rfp_375", "category": "General", "question": "What tools will Mastercard have to escalate issues, manage performance, contest decisions, etc.", "answer": "The platform provides in-app live chat for sharing product escalations. Additionally, each client is assigned a dedicated Customer Success Manager and an Executive Sponsor to serve as key points of contact for escalations."}, {"id": "rfp_376", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe your processes and timelines for implementation. Are there costs associated specifically with implementation?  If so, please define.", "answer": "Typically, our implementation timeline is 6-8 weeks, however given he global nature of the Mastercard program, we would expect the timeline to expand based on the number of countries included in the scope. Unless there are very bespoke requirements that require additional development, there are no additional costs for implementation."}, {"id": "rfp_377", "category": "General", "question": "What are some of the main challenges and issues with implementation? Outline your key learnings from previous implementations.  What key factors are necessary for a successful implementation?", "answer": "Direct Sourcing implementations are generally straightforward. The primary challenge lies in the design phase, where defining the rules of engagement and best practices is critical. Client participation in setting expectations during this phase is essential. For a successful implementation, all parties must be aligned, and decisions should be made promptly."}, {"id": "rfp_378", "category": "General", "question": "Describe your implementation team including the number of personnel, roles, responsibilities, and duration of involvement in implementation. How will this team vary from an operational or post-implementation environment? Identify the individuals who will provide our company with implementation and ongoing support.   If they are not the same person, how is the handoff managed?", "answer": "Given the strategic importance of Mastercard, Julie Semler, VP of Product Enablement, will oversee the implementation from a configuration and functional perspective. Julie will remain engaged for the first six months to ensure the program achieves its defined objectives. At that point, we will assess whether a transition to another Customer Success team member is necessary. David Kris and Manish Karani will support the Beeline integration. Karen Gonzalez will serve as the Executive Sponsor for the program."}, {"id": "rfp_379", "category": "General", "question": "Describe your project management methodology for implementation. What is your approach for roll out (e.g. big bang, region, job family etc)?", "answer": "Based on the scope of the Mastercard program, our recommendation would be to roll out direct sourcing in a phased approach based on geography.  We will work closely with Mastercard, AGS, Beeline and the curation partner to develop a phased approach that will optimize outcomes for Mastercard."}, {"id": "rfp_380", "category": "General", "question": "What is the process and timeline for onboarding new clients? Describe your approach to assisting the Client in managing change in process, policy, and personnel both during the implementation of your solution and once the program is fully operational. Please include examples of success and failure.", "answer": "Our standard implementation timeline is typically 6–8 weeks. However, due to the global scope of the Mastercard program, we anticipate the timeline may extend based on the number of countries involved. We will work closely with your team to define a phased rollout plan that aligns with regional requirements and ensures a smooth, successful launch across all geographies."}, {"id": "rfp_381", "category": "General", "question": "What level of involvement is typically required from the client & MSP partner during the implementation process?", "answer": "Executive Sponsor: Sets strategy, gains approvals, resolves escalations (2 hrs/week).\nPlatform Super User: Works with Sponsor and KnowledgeHub, manages setup, ops, and TalentNet transition (16 hrs/week).\nMarketing: Approves brand use and adds KnowledgeHub link (<5 hrs).\nLegal: Reviews co-employment and AI bias; supports dual logos (<5 hrs).\nIT: Reviews InfoSec needs (<5 hrs).\nMSP Lead: Ensures compliance, partners with Super User (2 hrs/week).\nCuration Team: Trained and kept informed during rollout."}, {"id": "rfp_382", "category": "General", "question": "What kind of support and training do you provide to ensure successful implementation and ongoing management of the program?", "answer": "In addition to a bespoke training plan created to support the curation team, we will implement a 90-day Hypercare plan ensures direct sourcing program success. Participants include the MSP, Curation Partner, and KnowledgeHub. Agenda: confirm integration functionality, monitor talent growth, verify curation team delivery, ensure best practices, and create action plans for issues. Weeks 1-2: Daily 30-min calls. Weeks 3-4: Biweekly 30-min calls. Weeks 5+: Weekly 30-min calls."}, {"id": "rfp_383", "category": "General", "question": "What ongoing support do you provide to ensure the program’s success?  Outline the plan & timeline for taking the program from implementation to BAU steady state.", "answer": "Please see above. We will continue to support hyper-care activities until the program meets steady state."}, {"id": "rfp_384", "category": "General", "question": "What training and materials are provided to Mastercard?  Are there associated cost?  Can you provide a list and/or samples?", "answer": "In a direct sourcing program, the Mastercard team will not need to access the platform unless they choose to. If Mastercard has specific training needs, we are happy to provide training material."}, {"id": "rfp_385", "category": "General", "question": "What is the role and the expected time commitment of the Account Manager?  What are the key tasks and time commitments of the Corporation during and after implementation?   Describe the Account Management structure, roles and deliverables.", "answer": "Mastercard will have a dedicated Account Manager to ensure the curation team uses the platform effectively, providing ongoing training and coaching. The Account Manager will also collaborate with the team on feature requests and handle escalations."}, {"id": "rfp_386", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe your account management structure.\na. Do you provide a dedicated global customer success manager (account manager), and/or U.S.-specific account manager, and regional/country-level support?", "answer": "The VP of Product Enablement is based in the US Central Time Zone. Her team includes members in the US and India. Platform support can be managed from a centralized location and doesn't require regional support."}, {"id": "rfp_387", "category": "General", "question": "How does your account management team proactively identify client needs and provide innovative solutions?", "answer": "Through weekly meetings and QBRs, the curation team and MSP will identify opportunities for expansion, additional use cases, and feature requests. This information will be presented to the product team for consideration. Additionally, KnowledgeHub’s Idea Portal allows platform users to submit feature suggestions, where other users can vote on requests and provide feedback, enabling us to prioritize development based on user needs."}, {"id": "rfp_388", "category": "General", "question": "If Applicable: will technical concerns be first triaged through the Account Management team or through a generic technical support group?", "answer": "Live In-app chat can be used in conjunction with the Customer Success Manager to address technical concerns."}, {"id": "rfp_389", "category": "General", "question": "Do you measure outcomes of the solution you provide and their effectiveness globally? If so, how and based on what methodologies?", "answer": "Yes, we measure outcomes and effectiveness globally using a combination of platform analytics, client-defined KPIs, and benchmarking across regions. Our methodology includes real-time dashboards, usage data, performance metrics (e.g., time-to-value, adoption rates), and outcome tracking aligned to client goals. We conduct regular reviews and incorporate client feedback to drive continuous optimization and ensure measurable, scalable impact across all markets."}, {"id": "rfp_390", "category": "General", "question": "How do you ensure the quality and consistency of your services across different regions?", "answer": "Not Applicable, This question feels like is directed towards Curation and EOR services."}, {"id": "rfp_391", "category": "General", "question": "What is your process for reporting utilization and outcomes to clients? Please describe your capabilities.\na.Do you provide standard reporting , including on-demand,  \"real-time\" dashboard clients  to \"self-serve\"?", "answer": "We provide comprehensive reporting on utilization and outcomes through a combination of standard scheduled reports, real-time dashboards, and self-service capabilities. Clients have 24/7 access to a customizable dashboard for on-demand insights into usage, performance metrics, and key outcomes. We also offer tailored reporting during regular business reviews to ensure transparency, accountability, and strategic alignment."}, {"id": "rfp_392", "category": "General", "question": "What level of member engagement is expected for your suite of services? How is it/are they measured?", "answer": "Mastercard and curation engagement."}, {"id": "rfp_393", "category": "General", "question": "Do you offer performance guarantees based on outcomes? What percentage of fees are you willing to put at risk?", "answer": "Not Applicable, This question feels like is directed towards Curation and EOR services."}, {"id": "rfp_394", "category": "General", "question": "Do you offer performance guarantees ?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_395", "category": "General", "question": "Identify the metrics for this contract and the process for tracking performance of the metrics.", "answer": "Not Applicable, This question feels like is directed towards Curation and EOR services."}, {"id": "rfp_396", "category": "General", "question": "Do you currently have a performance improvement plan that does not meet the agreed upon SLA standards?", "answer": "Not Applicable, This question feels like is directed towards Curation and EOR services."}, {"id": "rfp_397", "category": "General", "question": "Describe the process for reporting progress and engagement (e.g., utilization segmented by business unit, region, country).\na. Please describe how the reports will be generated (e.g., frequency of reporting, reporting template). For example, automated reports sent to leaders or specific stakeholders at specific intervals.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub provides 75 dashboards to help clients track program progress and engagement. Additionally, program teams can create custom dashboards and reports, accessible anytime by both clients and the Curation team."}, {"id": "rfp_398", "category": "General", "question": "Is the platform or admin dashboard or vendor able to deliver executive-level presentation of reports/outcomes?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_399", "category": "General", "question": "Dashboard/reports have benchmark data and norms (by industry, region, country, etc.) across multiple metrics", "answer": "KnowledgeHub integrates with Brightfield’s platform, to provide data-driven rate guidance for jobs and candidates. Access to Brightfield requires an additional licensing fee. For pay transparency compliance, KnowledgeHub intuitively recognizes state-specific requirements, ensuring pay details are entered before a job posting is published. This built-in compliance feature helps organizations stay aligned with evolving regulations while maintaining transparency and accuracy in job postings."}, {"id": "rfp_400", "category": "General", "question": "Dashboard incorporates suggestions for action planning (e.g. suggestions are provided depending on results across categories)?", "answer": "Yes, our dashboard provides actionable insights based on performance across key metrics—such as fill rate, time-to-fill, and candidate engagement. It includes AI-driven suggestions to improve sourcing strategy, outreach timing, and curator workflows. These recommendations support continuous improvement and action planning across programs."}, {"id": "rfp_401", "category": "General", "question": "Dashboard/reports able to track progress, attraction, utilization, engagement, and provide summary of results (e.i., group progress against overall engagement)?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_402", "category": "General", "question": "What is reporting threshold to maintain confidentiality and anonymity?", "answer": "We enforce minimum reporting thresholds to protect confidentiality and anonymity. Reporting data is aggregated and anonymized, with thresholds (e.g., 5+ individuals) to prevent identification of specific users or candidates. Access to sensitive reports is role-based, and privacy controls comply with GDPR, CCPA, and ISO 27701 standards."}, {"id": "rfp_403", "category": "General", "question": "Please provide a summary of the activity.", "answer": "This activity involves collecting, processing, and managing candidate data to support talent acquisition for Mastercard. Data is used to source, match, engage, and communicate with candidates for contingent or full-time roles. Processing includes resume parsing, AI-based matching, personalized outreach, and recruiter review—all conducted securely and in compliance with data protection laws."}, {"id": "rfp_404", "category": "General", "question": "What Personal Information is used/processed in this activity?", "answer": "We process personal information provided through resumes and user profiles. This includes, but is not limited to, name, contact details, employment history, education, skills, certifications, and other job-relevant information. All data is processed in accordance with applicable privacy laws and client agreements, and is used solely to support talent identification, engagement, and hiring activities."}, {"id": "rfp_405", "category": "General", "question": "Please include any other data categories or types of individuals that were not listed above", "answer": "Not applicable"}, {"id": "rfp_406", "category": "General", "question": "What is the purpose of this processing of Personal Information?", "answer": "The purpose of processing Personal Information is to support the sourcing, engagement, and hiring of talent. This includes identifying qualified candidates, communicating with them about relevant opportunities, evaluating their fit for specific roles, and facilitating the hiring process. All processing is conducted in compliance with applicable data privacy regulations and is aligned with the client’s talent acquisition objectives."}, {"id": "rfp_407", "category": "General", "question": "What are the sources of Personal Information?", "answer": "Personal Information is sourced from multiple channels:\n\nCandidates directly (e.g., applications, talent community sign-ups)\n\nPublicly available professional profiles (e.g., job boards, online resumes)\n\nReferrals or recruiter outreach\n\nVMS or ATS systems integrated with the platform\nAll data is collected with consent or under legitimate interest, in line with privacy laws."}, {"id": "rfp_408", "category": "General", "question": "What are the regions and/or countries of the processing activity or of the individuals whose Personal Information is collected, used, or disclosed (processed)?", "answer": "Personal information may be collected from and processed for individuals in the United States, Canada, European Union, United Kingdom, and India. Processing activities may occur in the same regions and also in secure data centers located in the U.S. All data handling complies with applicable local laws, and international transfers are protected using approved legal mechanisms."}, {"id": "rfp_409", "category": "General", "question": "Please indicate country/ies where technical assets reside,  technology operations or customer support staff with access to data is located.", "answer": "Our technical assets and infrastructure are hosted on AWS data centers located in the United States. Technology operations and customer support staff with access to data are based in the U.S. and India. All access is role-based, logged, and governed by strict security and privacy controls. International data transfers are protected by Standard Contractual Clauses and other required safeguards."}, {"id": "rfp_410", "category": "General", "question": "Please list all suppliers who process Personal Information.", "answer": "Personal Information may be processed by the following supplier categories:\n\nManaged Service Provider (MSP)\n\nVendor Management System (VMS) provider\n\nEmployer of Record (EOR) partner\n\nCuration Partner (e.g., KnowledgeHub)\nEach supplier processes data under a data processing agreement and is required to comply with applicable privacy and security standards."}, {"id": "rfp_411", "category": "General", "question": "Please identify the activity/ies of the supplier", "answer": "The MSP manages the overall contingent workforce program. The VMS facilitates requisition, candidate tracking, and invoicing. The EOR handles onboarding, payroll, and compliance for contingent workers. KnowledgeHub provides the direct sourcing technology platform to enable AI-powered sourcing and engagement. The Curation Partner to identify, curate, and submit qualified talent."}, {"id": "rfp_412", "category": "General", "question": "Where does the supplier use, store, or otherwise process the Personal Information, or access the data from?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub processes and stores personal information on secure AWS infrastructure located in the United States. Authorized team members may access the data from the U.S. and India, strictly for the purpose of platform support and operations. All access is role-based, logged, and subject to strong encryption, monitoring, and compliance with SOC 2, ISO 27001, and applicable data protection regulations."}, {"id": "rfp_413", "category": "General", "question": "Are there other parties that receive, access, or otherwise process Personal Information?", "answer": "Other parties that receive access and/or process personal information include the MSP, VMS, Curation team and EOR."}, {"id": "rfp_414", "category": "General", "question": "Please indicate data retention.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub retains personal data only as long as necessary to fulfill the purpose of processing or as required by the client. Retention periods are configurable based on client requirements and applicable laws. Candidate data may be automatically deleted after a defined period of inactivity. Upon request, data can be deleted, exported, or anonymized in compliance with GDPR, CCPA, and other privacy regulations."}, {"id": "rfp_415", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe the manner in which AI technology will be utilised in this processing activity.\nPlease include details of why AI technology is used, what personal information will be processed using this technology, and how this will work in practice.", "answer": "AI is used to enhance sourcing, matching, and candidate engagement. It processes personal data such as resumes, job history, skills, and location to recommend roles, personalize outreach, and rank fit. AI supports recruiters by increasing speed and accuracy—not making autonomous hiring decisions. All processing complies with GDPR/CCPA and includes human-in-the-loop oversight, transparency, and consent-based data use."}, {"id": "rfp_416", "category": "General", "question": "Is the use of AI technology necessary to carry out the objectives of this processing activity?", "answer": "AI is not strictly necessary but significantly enhances the efficiency, speed, and scalability of the talent acquisition process. It supports—but does not replace—human decision-making."}, {"id": "rfp_417", "category": "General", "question": "Were alternatives to the use of AI technology to carry out the objectives of this processing activity considered?", "answer": "Yes, traditional manual processes were considered, but they are significantly slower, less scalable, and more prone to bias and inconsistency. AI was selected to enhance recruiter productivity, improve candidate experience, and drive better outcomes. Its use is carefully governed with human oversight, ensuring ethical and compliant processing aligned with the intended objectives."}, {"id": "rfp_418", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe the manner in which automated decision making will be utilised in this processing activity.", "answer": "Our platform does not make fully automated hiring decisions. AI is used to assist with ranking, matching, and recommending candidates based on skills, experience, and job relevance. These outputs are reviewed by human recruiters who make the final decisions."}, {"id": "rfp_419", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe the nature of the potential impact on the individual of the automated decision.", "answer": "The KnowledgeHub platform does not make automated decisions; all final decisions are made by qualified recruiters. As such, there is no direct automated decision impact on individuals. The platform’s role is to provide recruiters with data and insights to support informed, fair, and unbiased human decision-making throughout the hiring process. This ensures that candidate outcomes are based on expert judgment rather than automated algorithms."}, {"id": "rfp_420", "category": "General", "question": "Will there be the possible for the individual to request a review by a human of the decision made by way of automated decision making?", "answer": "Since our platform does not perform any automated decision-making, all candidate evaluations and decisions are made by human recruiters. Therefore, every individual’s case is inherently subject to human review. This ensures transparency, fairness, and accountability throughout the hiring process without the need for a separate review request mechanism."}, {"id": "rfp_421", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe which groups are likely to be targeted or included in this processing activity.", "answer": "This processing activity targets job seekers and potential candidates for contingent or full-time roles. Groups include individuals who have applied, joined talent communities, or are publicly discoverable through professional data sources. Data processing is limited to job-relevant information and conducted with consent or under legitimate interest, in compliance with applicable laws."}, {"id": "rfp_422", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe how the processing activity will either specifically target or is likely to significantly process data concerning children or vulnerable individuals.", "answer": "This processing activity does not target or knowingly process data concerning children or vulnerable individuals. Our platform is designed for professional recruitment and only processes data of individuals who are legally eligible for employment. Age-related or sensitive information is not collected unless required for compliance, and controls are in place to prevent unintended processing of such data."}, {"id": "rfp_423", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe any special measures or precautions taken, or proposed to be taken, in order to specifically address the heightened risks to children or vulnerable individuals", "answer": "While our platform is not intended to process data of children or vulnerable individuals, we implement preventive measures including age verification checks, exclusion filters, and restricted data fields. If such data is inadvertently captured, it is flagged for review and promptly deleted. Access controls, consent requirements, and monitoring ensure that heightened risks are proactively managed and mitigated."}, {"id": "rfp_424", "category": "General", "question": "Please detail how and why this processing activity might prevent an individual from exercising a right or using a service or a contract.", "answer": "This processing activity does not prevent individuals from exercising their rights or accessing services. Candidates can access, correct, or delete their data at any time, and participation in AI-driven workflows is optional. Human review is maintained for all key decisions, ensuring that individuals are not excluded from opportunities due to automated processing or withheld consent."}, {"id": "rfp_425", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe the manner in which new technologies or solutions will be utilised in this processing activity, or existing technologies or information will be utilised in a novel or innovative manner.", "answer": "This activity uses AI and automation in a novel way to enhance sourcing, matching, and engagement in talent acquisition. Our platform combines traditional recruitment data with generative AI to create personalized outreach, automate candidate journeys, and improve match relevance—while maintaining human oversight, transparency, and compliance with data protection standards."}, {"id": "rfp_426", "category": "General", "question": "Were alternatives to the use of these technologies or solutions to carry out the objectives of this processing activity considered?", "answer": "Yes, manual and traditional recruitment methods were considered but found to be less efficient, slower to scale, and more prone to human bias. AI and automation were selected to improve speed, consistency, and candidate experience—while still preserving human oversight. These technologies were adopted to meet program goals responsibly and in compliance with legal and ethical standards."}, {"id": "rfp_427", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe the datasets which were combined or matched as part of this processing activity, and what the original purpose of the dataset was.", "answer": "We combine candidate-provided data (e.g., resumes, applications) with publicly available professional data (e.g., LinkedIn-style profiles) to enhance sourcing and matching. All datasets were originally created for professional networking, recruitment, or job-seeking purposes. Data is processed in line with those original intents, and only job-relevant attributes are matched to ensure lawful and ethical use."}, {"id": "rfp_428", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe the manner in which these datasets were combined or matched, what the purpose of combination was, and how this might differ from the original purposes.", "answer": "Datasets are combined using AI-driven entity resolution to match candidate profiles across sources based on skills, job titles, and work history. The purpose is to enrich candidate profiles for better job matching and engagement. This use aligns with the original intent—professional visibility and employment. No sensitive or unrelated personal data is combined, and all processing respects privacy and consent boundaries."}, {"id": "rfp_429", "category": "General", "question": "Would this combination or matching be likely to surprise the individuals to whom the data pertains, and/or seem intrusive to their privacy?", "answer": "No, the combination and matching of data is consistent with the individual’s original intent—seeking job opportunities—and uses only professional, job-relevant information. We avoid processing sensitive or unrelated personal data. Individuals are informed through our privacy policy and consent mechanisms, minimizing surprise or perceived intrusiveness and maintaining transparency throughout the process."}, {"id": "rfp_430", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe any steps taken, if any, to inform individuals or otherwise minimise the surprising or intrusive nature of the combination or matching of these datasets.", "answer": "We minimize surprise by clearly disclosing data use in our privacy policy and candidate communications. Individuals are informed when their data is processed or matched, and we provide access to view, correct, or delete their information. Only professional, job-relevant data is used. We avoid combining sensitive personal data, and users can opt out at any time to maintain trust and control."}, {"id": "rfp_431", "category": "General", "question": "Please select the types of sensitive personal information which may be processed as part of this processing activity.", "answer": "We process standard personal data such as name, email, phone, city, state, employment history, education level, and professional certifications. This information is necessary for recruitment and matching purposes. We do not process sensitive personal data (e.g., health, biometric, political). Any optional compliance data is collected with consent and handled in accordance with privacy laws."}, {"id": "rfp_432", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe the nature of the sensitive personal information to be processed as part of this processing activity.", "answer": "This processing activity does not require or intentionally process sensitive personal information as defined by GDPR or similar laws. We focus only on job-relevant data such as contact details, employment history, education, and certifications. If optional sensitive data (e.g., veteran status or work authorization) is collected for compliance purposes, it is processed with explicit consent and appropriate safeguards."}, {"id": "rfp_433", "category": "General", "question": "Would it be possible to achieve the objectives of the processing activity without using this sensitive personal information or by using less of this information?", "answer": "Yes, the objectives of this processing activity can be achieved without relying on sensitive personal information. Our platform is designed to focus on non-sensitive, job-relevant data such as skills, experience, and qualifications. Any optional sensitive data used for compliance (e.g., veteran status) is collected only when necessary, with consent, and can be excluded without impacting core platform functionality."}, {"id": "rfp_434", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe the nature in which profiling or scoring is carried out as part of this processing activity.", "answer": "Profiling is used to assess candidate-job fit based on factors like skills, experience, location, and job history. AI assigns match scores to help prioritize candidates, but final decisions are made by human recruiters. Scoring is transparent, auditable, and based only on job-relevant data. No sensitive personal data is used, and profiling does not result in automated decision-making with legal or significant effects."}, {"id": "rfp_435", "category": "General", "question": "Are individuals able to opt-out of this profiling or scoring?", "answer": "At this time, individuals cannot opt out of profiling or scoring, as it is an essential part of how our platform enhances candidate-job matching. However, all scoring is used to support—not replace—human decision-making. No fully automated decisions are made, and individuals retain all rights to access, correct, or delete their data in accordance with applicable privacy laws."}, {"id": "rfp_436", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe the type or types of personal information which might be 'sold'.", "answer": "Not Applicable"}, {"id": "rfp_437", "category": "General", "question": "1.29 Please describe the manner in which this personal information might be sold.", "answer": "Not Applicable"}, {"id": "rfp_438", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe the third parties to which this personal information might be sold.", "answer": "Not Applicable"}, {"id": "rfp_439", "category": "General", "question": "Are individuals given the option to opt-out of the sale of their personal information?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_440", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe the manner in which individuals will be systematically monitored as part of this processing operation.", "answer": "Individuals are not systematically monitored in this processing activity. Our platform processes candidate data solely for recruitment purposes—such as matching, communication, and engagement. We do not track user behavior across sites or continuously monitor individuals. All data processing is limited, purpose-driven, and conducted in compliance with applicable privacy regulations."}, {"id": "rfp_441", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe why it is necessary that individuals will be systematically monitored as part of this processing operation, and whether any alternatives were considered.", "answer": "Not Applicable"}, {"id": "rfp_442", "category": "General", "question": "What is the legal basis for Mastercard’s processing of this data? (Multiple selections allowed) (Justification allowed) *", "answer": "The legal basis for Mastercard’s processing of this data may include: (1) legitimate interest in identifying and engaging qualified candidates, (2) performance of a contract or steps prior to entering into a contract with the candidate, and (3) compliance with legal obligations (e.g., diversity reporting)."}, {"id": "rfp_443", "category": "General", "question": "How has the data subject/individual given consent to the processing?", "answer": "Consent is obtained when individuals actively join the talent community, apply for a role, or engage with the platform through forms or outreach. At the point of data collection, individuals are presented with a clear privacy notice outlining how their data will be used. Consent is logged, stored securely, and can be withdrawn at any time, in line with GDPR and other applicable privacy regulations."}, {"id": "rfp_444", "category": "General", "question": "Please select and briefly describe the nature of law or the obligation Mastercard will process this personal information in order to comply with.", "answer": "Mastercard may process personal information to comply with labor, employment, and anti-discrimination laws such as U.S. EEOC reporting requirements, OFCCP obligations, or equivalent diversity and workforce compliance laws in other jurisdictions. This may include collecting optional data related to gender, veteran status, or work authorization, always with appropriate safeguards and, where required, explicit consent."}, {"id": "rfp_445", "category": "General", "question": "Is the personal information adequate, relevant and limited to what is necessary in relation to the purposes for which it is or will be processed (data minimization)?", "answer": "Yes, all personal information collected is adequate, relevant, and limited to what is necessary for recruitment and hiring purposes. We process only job-relevant data such as contact details, work history, skills, and qualifications. Sensitive or non-essential data is not collected unless required for compliance and with consent."}, {"id": "rfp_446", "category": "General", "question": "Please indicate the role of the Supplier(s) in this data processing activity", "answer": "KnowledgeHub acts as a data processor on behalf of Mastercard. We process personal data solely under Mastercard’s instructions and in accordance with applicable data protection agreements and laws. Mastercard, as the data controller, determines the purpose and means of processing, while we ensure secure, compliant, and purpose-limited data handling in support of the recruitment process."}, {"id": "rfp_447", "category": "General", "question": "Is there a data processing agreement (DPA) in place for the listed Supplier(s)?", "answer": "A Data Processing Agreement (DPA) will be executed as part of our engagement with listed supplier(s). Our standard DPA aligns with GDPR, CCPA, and other global data protection laws. It outlines roles, responsibilities, security measures, and subprocessors to ensure lawful and transparent data processing. We are fully prepared to review and align with Mastercard’s DPA requirements as needed."}, {"id": "rfp_448", "category": "General", "question": "Identify the party/parties who has/have a legitimate interest in processing the data.", "answer": "Mastercard, as the data controller, has a legitimate interest in processing personal data to identify, engage, and hire qualified talent. Suppliers—including the MSP, VMS, EOR, and Curation Partner—process data on Mastercard’s behalf to fulfill this purpose. All processing is limited to what is necessary, job-relevant, and conducted under strict contractual and regulatory compliance frameworks."}, {"id": "rfp_449", "category": "General", "question": "Are the individuals provided with information about the processing of their personal information in a concise, transparent, intelligible and easily accessible form, using clear and plain language?", "answer": "Yes, individuals are informed through a clear, concise, and easily accessible privacy notice using plain language. This notice explains what data is collected, how it’s used, who it’s shared with, and their rights. It is presented at the point of data collection (e.g., job application or talent community sign-up) to ensure transparency and compliance with GDPR, CCPA, and other applicable laws."}, {"id": "rfp_450", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe which privacy notice or transparency information is provided to the individual.", "answer": "Individuals are provided with a comprehensive privacy notice at the point of data collection. It includes details on what personal data is collected, the purpose of processing, legal basis, data retention, rights of the individual, and contact information for privacy inquiries. The notice also outlines the use of AI, data sharing with clients like Mastercard, and how individuals can access, correct, or delete their data."}, {"id": "rfp_451", "category": "General", "question": "Please explain how this information is provided to the individual(s).", "answer": "Privacy information is provided at the time of data collection via clearly labeled links on sign-up forms, application portals, and outreach messages. It is accessible through the platform's interface and sent via email when relevant. The notice is written in plain language and available at any time through our website or candidate dashboard, ensuring individuals can easily review how their data is used."}, {"id": "rfp_452", "category": "General", "question": "Is the product or service the service capable of complying with privacy rights requests?", "answer": "Yes, our platform fully supports privacy rights requests in accordance with GDPR, CCPA, and other applicable laws. Individuals can request access, correction, deletion, or restriction of their personal data. These requests are logged, verified, and processed within required timeframes. We also support data portability and the right to object, with controls in place to manage and audit all such requests."}, {"id": "rfp_453", "category": "General", "question": "What transfer mechanism(s), if any, is relied upon to allow international data transfers?", "answer": "We rely on Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) approved by the European Commission to support international data transfers outside the EEA. Where applicable, we also conduct Transfer Impact Assessments (TIAs) and implement additional safeguards such as encryption and access controls. All subprocessors are contractually bound to uphold equivalent data protection standards."}, {"id": "rfp_454", "category": "General", "question": "Please provide details of the transfer mechanism(s) in place for international data transfers, or why no such transfer is necessary.", "answer": "We use Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) to support international data transfers outside the EEA, including to the U.S. and India. Where required, we conduct Transfer Impact Assessments and apply technical and organizational safeguards such as encryption and strict access controls. In cases where data residency is required, processing can be limited to specific regions to avoid cross-border transfers."}, {"id": "rfp_455", "category": "General", "question": "Please select the relevant security measures to protect the personal information", "answer": "We implement robust security measures including:\n\nAES-256 encryption at rest\n\nTLS 1.2+ encryption in transit\n\nRole-based access controls\n\nMulti-factor authentication\n\nRegular vulnerability scans and penetration testing\n\nActivity logging and monitoring\n\nData loss prevention (DLP) policies\n\nIncident response and disaster recovery plans\nAll measures align with SOC 2, ISO 27001, and GDPR standards.**"}, {"id": "rfp_456", "category": "General", "question": "What is your definition of AI with regards to the solution your product(s)/service(s) offers?", "answer": "We define AI as the use of machine learning and natural language processing to automate, enhance, and personalize tasks in the talent acquisition process. In our solution, AI powers resume matching, candidate recommendations, outreach personalization, and generative content creation—always with human oversight to ensure accuracy, fairness, and alignment with hiring goals."}, {"id": "rfp_457", "category": "General", "question": "Will it be possible to configure the level of AI involvement/autonomy in the process (e.g., recommendations only, auto-generated content, opt-in/opt-out)?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_458", "category": "General", "question": "How do you ensure the quality and relevance of the data used to train your generative AI model for talent acquisition and hiring?", "answer": "We use high-quality, curated datasets from verified sources, including anonymized recruiter feedback, job-candidate match data, and market trends. Data is continuously validated for accuracy, diversity, and bias mitigation. Models are fine-tuned with real-world hiring outcomes to ensure relevance. Regular audits and human-in-the-loop reviews maintain quality and compliance."}, {"id": "rfp_459", "category": "General", "question": "Do you contract with an independent technology service to verify your AI claims? If you do, please supply their reports that include a description of their credentials, criteria used, methodology and assessment.", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_460", "category": "General", "question": "Operational Considerations [Scalability, Security, Privacy, Compliance, Training, Documentation]:", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is built for scalability (cloud-native, auto-scaling), enterprise-grade security (SOC 2, ISO 27001/27701), and full GDPR/CCPA compliance. We support SSO, data encryption, and role-based access. Clients receive onboarding, training, and detailed documentation. Our team provides ongoing support, product updates, and audit-ready compliance tools—ensuring secure, scalable, and responsible deployment."}, {"id": "rfp_461", "category": "General", "question": "Describe your methodology for collecting, processing, and verifying data from resumes, job descriptions, feedback, interviews, or other data sources relevant to your solution.", "answer": "We collect data from resumes, job descriptions, interviews, and feedback through structured parsing, API integrations, and user input. Our NLP engine extracts and normalizes key attributes (skills, titles, experience) using proprietary taxonomies. Feedback loops from recruiter actions and hiring outcomes help refine matching. All data is validated, deduplicated, and scored for accuracy and relevance."}, {"id": "rfp_462", "category": "General", "question": "What are the sources of data on which your AI is trained and to what degree to you have the rights to this data?", "answer": "Our AI is trained on a combination of licensed public datasets, anonymized internal platform data, and synthetic datasets created to model hiring behavior. All data used complies with legal and ethical standards. We have full rights to use our proprietary data and access to third-party data under license agreements. No customer or personal data is used without explicit permission or anonymization."}, {"id": "rfp_463", "category": "General", "question": "Describe how your software handles large data sets and high volumes of requests.", "answer": "KnowledgeHub is built on a scalable, cloud-native architecture (AWS) designed to handle large datasets and high request volumes. We use distributed processing, indexed search, and caching to ensure fast performance. Auto-scaling infrastructure supports spikes in usage, while load balancing and queueing systems maintain stability and response times under heavy loads."}, {"id": "rfp_464", "category": "General", "question": "Describe how your solution handles and protects sensitive personal data aimed at protecting end users’ privacy. Provide specific methods used to anonymize data, how data retention policies are administered including the right to be forgotten, and any other measures taken to protect users’ privacy.", "answer": "We protect sensitive data through encryption (AES-256 at rest, TLS 1.2+ in transit), role-based access, and audit logs. Personal data can be anonymized or pseudonymized for analytics. Users can request deletion in line with GDPR’s right to be forgotten. Retention policies are configurable by client and monitored regularly. Privacy by design is built into all features, aligned with ISO 27701."}, {"id": "rfp_465", "category": "General", "question": "Describe your approach to complying with relevant laws and regulations in multiple jurisdictions, such as GDPR, CCPA, or EEOC? If the solution is deployed in Europe, are you aware of the EU AI Act and its implications and compliance to it ?", "answer": "We follow a privacy-by-design approach aligned with GDPR, CCPA, and EEOC. Data collection is consent-based, with configurable retention, access controls, and subject rights workflows. If deployed in Europe, we’re prepared to comply with the EU AI Act, including transparency, fairness, and auditability requirements for high-risk AI systems used in hiring. Our team actively monitors evolving global regulations."}, {"id": "rfp_466", "category": "General", "question": "Are your algorithms, as used in your solution, static? If not, do they continue to learn within our use or, more broadly? How do you support your solution over time?", "answer": "Our algorithms are not static—they improve over time through continuous learning from anonymized user interactions and recruiter feedback. Learning can be limited to your environment or benefit from broader usage patterns, depending on preference. We support the solution with regular updates, performance monitoring, and model tuning to ensure ongoing accuracy, fairness, and alignment with business goals."}, {"id": "rfp_467", "category": "General", "question": "How will the solution tackle the standardization of outputs / lack of diversity and variety that is often seen with AI solutions?", "answer": "We address output standardization by training on diverse, real-world datasets and incorporating human-in-the-loop feedback to fine-tune results. Our AI surfaces a variety of qualified candidates by focusing on skills, context, and relevance—not just pattern matching. Customizable scoring and ranking models help avoid bias and ensure diverse, high-quality talent recommendations."}, {"id": "rfp_468", "category": "General", "question": "What Information Security policies and procedures do you have in place? At a minimum, please share your policies for data protection, encryption, access control, audit logging, and incident response.", "answer": "Please see attached info sec policies"}, {"id": "rfp_469", "category": "General", "question": "How do you support the integration and customization of the (generative) AI solution for talent acquisition and hiring?", "answer": "Yes, our platform includes integrated generative AI for talent engagement, job summarization, and personalized candidate messaging. It supports customization by role, industry, tone, and branding. Clients can tailor prompts, workflows, and outputs to fit their hiring needs."}, {"id": "rfp_470", "category": "General", "question": "Can you adjust the creativity, level of detail, and style of the generated outputs?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_471", "category": "General", "question": "Is it transparent and explainable?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_472", "category": "General", "question": "What level of ongoing support and maintenance is included? How are updates and bug fixes handled?", "answer": "Each client is assigned a Customer Success Manager for direct support. KnowledgeHub also provides in-app chat for users to address recruiter inquiries. Identified bugs are triaged and resolved per our SLA guidelines."}, {"id": "rfp_473", "category": "General", "question": "How do you provide documentation, training, and technical support for users?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub provides comprehensive support through a dedicated Customer Success Manager who offers personalized training. Additionally, we maintain a detailed help desk library for self-guided documentation. For real-time assistance, users can access our in-app chat feature to resolve technical queries efficiently."}, {"id": "rfp_474", "category": "General", "question": "How do you address the issues of data diversity and bias in talent acquisition and hiring?", "answer": "We mitigate bias by using diverse training data, de-identifying candidate information during matching, and continuously auditing model outputs for fairness. Our algorithms are trained to prioritize skills and experience over demographic proxies. We offer clients the ability to customize scoring rules and monitor outcomes to align with DEI goals, ensuring equitable and inclusive hiring practices."}, {"id": "rfp_475", "category": "General", "question": "Do you have the capabilities to assess the solution for bias related to gender, age, and ethnicity?  How do you address potential biases in the data used by your tool? What steps have been taken to detect and mitigate bias across demographics, roles, or regions?", "answer": "Yes, we assess for bias related to gender, age, and ethnicity through third-party audits (e.g., NYC AI bias audit), internal testing, and outcome analysis. We de-identify candidate data during matching, use diverse training sets, and regularly monitor outputs across demographics, roles, and regions. Human-in-the-loop reviews and client feedback loops help detect, mitigate, and continuously improve fairness."}, {"id": "rfp_476", "category": "General", "question": "For vendors that claim they do, would they be able to share bias testing reports with Mastercard?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_477", "category": "General", "question": "How is human input used to guide & refine the generative process, integrated into recruiter workflows? Is there an inbuilt “verify & override” workflow built into the design?", "answer": "Yes, human input is central to our generative AI workflows. Recruiters can review, edit, and approve all AI-generated content before use—whether it’s outreach messages, job summaries, or candidate engagement. The platform includes built-in “verify & override” steps, ensuring recruiters stay in control while benefiting from AI-driven speed, consistency, and personalization."}, {"id": "rfp_478", "category": "General", "question": "How do you prevent or mitigate potential harm or abuse of generative AI, such as plagiarism, inaccurate or misleading information (i.e. hallucinations) or manipulation in talent acquisition and hiring? Describe the guardrails you have put in place.", "answer": "We use strict prompt controls, output filters, and human-in-the-loop review to prevent plagiarism, hallucinations, or manipulation. AI-generated content is transparently labeled and must be verified by recruiters before use. Training data is curated for accuracy and fairness. Regular audits, bias checks, and model tuning ensure the AI aligns with ethical hiring standards and reduces risk of harm or misuse."}, {"id": "rfp_479", "category": "General", "question": "How will you support us if we are audited?", "answer": "We fully support audits by providing SOC 2, ISO 27001/27701 reports, security policies, and system logs. Our compliance team collaborates directly with client audit teams to coordinate documentation, clarify technical details, and complete questionnaires. We follow secure data-sharing protocols, and NDAs are executed to protect confidentiality. Our goal is to ensure a smooth, transparent, and responsive audit experience."}, {"id": "rfp_480", "category": "General", "question": "How do you address the ethical and social implications of using generative AI for talent acquisition and hiring?", "answer": "We take a responsible AI approach grounded in fairness, transparency, and accountability. Our models are trained to reduce bias, and we’ve passed a third-party NYC AI bias audit for compliance. Human oversight is built into all workflows. We monitor outputs for accuracy and fairness, and provide clients with tools to align AI usage with their DEI and ethical hiring goals."}, {"id": "rfp_481", "category": "General", "question": "How do you measure and evaluate the effectiveness, accuracy, and reliability of the generative AI model for talent acquisition and hiring?", "answer": "We evaluate our generative AI through continuous A/B testing, recruiter feedback, and outcome-based metrics such as candidate response rates, quality of match, and time-to-fill. Accuracy is monitored via human-in-the-loop validation, and model performance is benchmarked regularly. We track relevance, bias, and reliability to ensure AI output aligns with hiring goals and delivers measurable impact."}, {"id": "rfp_482", "category": "General", "question": "What are the metrics and benchmarks used to assess the quality and suitability of the generated content, such as candidates, profiles, messages, and reports?", "answer": "We assess quality using metrics like response rates (messages), engagement rates (campaigns), match accuracy (candidates/profiles), recruiter edits (content usefulness), and hiring outcomes. Benchmarks include time-to-fill, submission-to-interview ratio, and feedback scores. AI-generated content is continuously reviewed against these KPIs to ensure it’s relevant, personalized, and driving results."}, {"id": "rfp_483", "category": "General", "question": "Based on your experience in design, development and deployment of such solutions, what do you foresee as its unintended consequences ?", "answer": "Unintended consequences may include over-reliance on AI, reduced human judgment, or subtle biases in outputs if not continuously monitored. To mitigate this, we build human-in-the-loop controls, transparency in AI decisions, and regular audits into our system. We prioritize responsible use, ensuring recruiters remain in control and AI supports—not replaces—critical hiring decisions."}, {"id": "rfp_484", "category": "General", "question": "How do you handle errors, anomalies, or inconsistencies in the generated content or the hiring process?", "answer": "We use automated validation, anomaly detection, and human review to identify and resolve errors or inconsistencies in generated content. Recruiters can flag issues directly in the platform. All flagged content is reviewed, logged, and used to retrain or fine-tune models. For hiring process errors, audit trails and alerts help ensure timely resolution while maintaining compliance and transparency."}, {"id": "rfp_485", "category": "General", "question": "Are there any judgements pending against current, previous clients or yourself with respect to your product/service?", "answer": "No"}, {"id": "rfp_486", "category": "General", "question": "What type of information will be provided for end users to understand the expected use and limitations of the tool? // what level of involvement is expected from ongoing users?", "answer": "We provide end users with onboarding guides, in-platform tooltips, and documentation outlining intended use, AI involvement, and limitations. Recruiters are informed when content is AI-generated and can review, edit, or override as needed. Ongoing users are expected to guide the AI with feedback, monitor results, and remain in control of hiring decisions—ensuring responsible, effective use of the tool."}, {"id": "rfp_487", "category": "General", "question": "Are the algorithms and decision-making processes used by your tool explainable and understandable to non-technical users? Is there a disclosure plan and/or model card for non-technical users?", "answer": "Yes, our AI outputs are explainable and designed for non-technical users. We provide clear justifications for candidate matches and content generation, including key factors influencing results. A model summary (“model card”) and disclosure of AI involvement are available in plain language. This ensures transparency, trust, and informed use across recruiter and stakeholder workflows."}, {"id": "rfp_488", "category": "General", "question": "Are there resources available for troubleshooting and continuous learning of ongoing users?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_489", "category": "General", "question": "Is GenAI involved in your solution. If yes, please answer these additional questions", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_490", "category": "General", "question": "a) will the solution support Zero Data Retention?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_491", "category": "General", "question": "b) is the model assessed for toxicity, hallucination, bias? If not, would they be able to provide API access so that we can assess it with our internal tooling?", "answer": "Models are tested for toxicity, bias, and hallucinations; we can also provide API access for your testing."}, {"id": "rfp_492", "category": "General", "question": "c) If chatbot functionality: are there any subjects that the solution is banned from discussing?", "answer": "Chatbot avoids sensitive or off-topic subjects via prompt controls"}, {"id": "rfp_493", "category": "General", "question": "d) If relying on a foundation model, how are you dealing with larger foundation model updates to ensure a stable SLA ?", "answer": "Foundation model updates are version-controlled and regression-tested to maintain SLA."}, {"id": "rfp_494", "category": "General", "question": "e) How are effectiveness and ongoing performance measured and ensured for this GenAI solution? (Drift is not detected as easily in GenAI vs traditional AI)", "answer": "Performance is monitored via recruiter feedback, engagement metrics, and audit logs to detect drift."}, {"id": "rfp_495", "category": "General", "question": "Explain how your organization identifies, assesses, and determines how to manage uncertainties of achieving the overall goal?", "answer": "We follow a structured risk management framework to identify and assess uncertainties through stakeholder input, historical data, and ongoing performance monitoring. Risks are prioritized based on impact and likelihood, and mitigation strategies are built into implementation and support plans. Regular reviews, client feedback loops, and agile development practices help us adapt quickly and keep progress aligned with client goals."}, {"id": "rfp_496", "category": "General", "question": "Who is accountable for managing the results and to whom do they report?", "answer": "Leadership team responsible for managing results-report directly to CEO."}, {"id": "rfp_497", "category": "General", "question": "How does your company define a client as “successful”?", "answer": "We will work with Mastercard to determine the goals and objectives of the program and together, we will establish mutually agreed upon KPIs in order to guage ongoing performance."}, {"id": "rfp_498", "category": "General", "question": "Will any work on the Mastercard offering be subcontracted to another company? If yes, please specify that company’s name and in what capacity.", "answer": "No"}, {"id": "rfp_499", "category": "General", "question": "Which Certifications does your company have?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub holds the following certifications: SOC 2 Type II, ISO 27001 (Information Security Management), and ISO 27701 (Privacy Information Management). These certifications reflect our commitment to data security, privacy, and operational excellence. We undergo annual audits and maintain rigorous internal controls to ensure ongoing compliance with global standards."}, {"id": "rfp_500", "category": "General", "question": "How will your organization support regulatory audits of worker data?", "answer": "We support regulatory audits, including EEOC reporting, by providing structured, exportable data on worker demographics, hiring outcomes, and process steps. Our platform can track and report on diversity metrics while maintaining privacy compliance. We collaborate with client compliance teams to deliver accurate data for audits and regulatory submissions in a timely, secure, and auditable format."}, {"id": "rfp_501", "category": "General", "question": "Describe the process for monitoring and communicating legal changes", "answer": "We actively monitor legal and regulatory changes in HR, hiring, and AI through legal advisors, industry bodies, and compliance tools. Our team reviews updates (e.g., EEOC, GDPR, CCPA, EU cI Act) and assesses impact on product and processes. Clients are informed of relevant changes through release notes, compliance alerts, and quarterly reviews. Policies and features are updated proactively to maintain compliance."}, {"id": "rfp_502", "category": "General", "question": "What is your data retention policy?", "answer": "Our data retention policy is configurable based on client requirements and applicable regulations (e.g., GDPR, CCPA). By default, candidate data is retained only as long as needed for hiring purposes. Users can request deletion at any time, and inactive data can be auto-purged after a defined period. All deletion activity is logged, and backups follow the same retention rules to ensure compliance and data minimization."}, {"id": "rfp_503", "category": "General", "question": "Please briefly describe how your solution meets data privacy and other country specific legal and regulatory requirements for the countries in scope.", "answer": "Our solution is built with privacy-by-design principles and complies with major data protection laws including GDPR (EU), and CCPA (US). We support country-specific data handling, consent capture, and configurable retention settings. Data is stored securely with encryption, access controls, and audit trails. We continuously monitor global regulations to ensure compliance across all countries in scope."}, {"id": "rfp_504", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe controls you use to address the use, handling, protection and sharing of confidential data shared with subcontractors.", "answer": "Not applicable, We do not use subcontractors to perform our services. This question may be more direct towards Curation services and/or EOR services"}, {"id": "rfp_505", "category": "General", "question": "Please describe any controls you use to address the threat of information knowingly being misused by your workforce and contractors.", "answer": "We implement strict access controls, role-based permissions, and activity logging to prevent data misuse. All employees and contractors undergo background checks, sign confidentiality agreements, and complete security and compliance training. System usage is continuously monitored, and alerts are triggered for anomalous behavior. Violations result in immediate investigation and disciplinary action per our zero-tolerance policy."}, {"id": "rfp_506", "category": "General", "question": "Describe your internal processes for timely detection and communication of data breaches to customers, data protection Authorities, and the impacted individuals.", "answer": "We have an incident response plan aligned with GDPR and global standards. Breaches are detected through 24/7 monitoring, alerts, and audits. Upon confirmation, we notify affected clients within 72 hours, as required, and support communication to data protection authorities and impacted individuals. Root cause analysis, containment, and remediation steps are documented and shared. All processes are tested and reviewed regularly."}, {"id": "rfp_507", "category": "General", "question": "Describe your quality assurance program.", "answer": "Our compliance quality assurance program includes regular internal audits, policy reviews, risk assessments, and control testing aligned with SOC 2, ISO 27001, and SOX frameworks. We maintain documented procedures for data handling, access control, and incident response. Compliance KPIs are tracked, reviewed quarterly, and used to drive corrective actions and continuous improvement across operations."}, {"id": "rfp_508", "category": "General", "question": "Describe your normal SOX control process for customers of our size.", "answer": "For SOX-relevant clients, we support ITGC and application-level controls, including user access reviews, change management logs, audit trails, and segregation of duties. All changes are tracked through version control and approved workflows. We provide evidence for financial and operational controls upon request and align with SOC 2 audit standards to ensure SOX readiness and reporting integrity."}, {"id": "rfp_509", "category": "General", "question": "Describe how you monitor compliance and quality of the services provided.", "answer": "We monitor compliance through internal audits, policy adherence reviews, and ongoing risk assessments. Controls aligned with SOC 2, ISO 27001/27701, and SOX are tested regularly. Access logs, data handling activities, and regulatory obligations (e.g., GDPR, CCPA) are continuously reviewed. Any non-compliance triggers documented remediation and leadership oversight to ensure accountability and legal integrity."}, {"id": "rfp_510", "category": "General", "question": "How do you ensure compliance with local laws and regulations in all of the the countries you serve?", "answer": "We ensure compliance with local laws by working with regional legal experts, monitoring regulatory updates, and aligning our policies with frameworks like GDPR, CCPA, and local labor and data protection laws. Our platform supports configurable data handling, consent management, and retention by country. We conduct regular internal audits and adapt workflows to meet evolving legal requirements in each jurisdiction."}, {"id": "rfp_511", "category": "General", "question": "How do you handle legal and ethical issues that may arise in different regions?", "answer": "We proactively address legal and ethical issues through a governance framework that includes legal review, regional compliance checks, and ethics oversight. Our policies align with local laws and global standards (e.g., GDPR, EEOC, EU AI Act). We consult with legal advisors in each region, provide training to staff, and adapt our platform and practices to ensure culturally and legally appropriate operations worldwide."}, {"id": "rfp_512", "category": "General", "question": "Describe your comprehensive compliance program to support processing of personal information.", "answer": "Our compliance program supports personal data processing through GDPR, CCPA, and ISO 27701-aligned policies. We enforce data minimization, purpose limitation, and consent-based processing. Access is role-based, monitored, and logged. We maintain a data inventory, conduct regular DPIAs, support data subject rights (DSR), and have incident response plans in place. Ongoing audits and staff training ensure continuous compliance."}, {"id": "rfp_513", "category": "General", "question": "Do you have a public-facing privacy policy/privacy notice?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_514", "category": "General", "question": "Do you have experience with GDPR and other international data protection laws?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_515", "category": "General", "question": "How do you ensure the confidentiality and security of worker data?", "answer": "We ensure the confidentiality and security of worker data through encryption (AES-256 at rest, TLS 1.2+ in transit), role-based access controls, audit logging, and secure infrastructure hosted on AWS. Access is limited to authorized personnel, and all activity is monitored. Regular security training, penetration testing, and compliance with SOC 2 and ISO 27001/27701 ensure ongoing protection of sensitive worker data."}, {"id": "rfp_516", "category": "General", "question": "Describe how you comply with Federal and State privacy laws.", "answer": "We comply with applicable U.S. federal and state privacy laws, including CCPA, CPRA, HIPAA (as applicable), and other emerging state regulations. Our platform supports consent management, data subject access and deletion rights, and purpose-limited data use. We maintain a robust privacy policy, conduct regular reviews, and implement technical and organizational controls to meet evolving legal requirements."}, {"id": "rfp_517", "category": "General", "question": "Do you follow HIPAA guidelines? Are you GDPR compliant?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_518", "category": "General", "question": "Do you conduct security audits and will you be able to share the reports ?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_519", "category": "General", "question": "Describe your SLA  & KPI's", "answer": "KnowledgeHub’s SLAs ensure fast, reliable support:\n• Level 1: Resolved <1 hour\n• Level 2: Resolved <4 hours\n• Level 3: Resolved <24 hours\n\nWe acknowledge all issues within 1 hour and escalate as needed to the VP of Product Enablement or CPO. Billing inquiries are reviewed within 1 business day. Standard reports are on demand; custom reports within 5 business days. We’re committed to responsive, transparent, and high-quality service for Mastercard."}, {"id": "rfp_520", "category": "General", "question": "Can you provide a copy of your standard SLA ? Would you be willing to commit to SLAs, with incentives or penalties?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_521", "category": "General", "question": "What are your service availability commitments (e.g., uptime for online platforms, 24/7 accessibility)?", "answer": "Overal Availability:\nMinimum Service Level: 99.95% uptime\nCredit: Compensation equivalent to the number of minutes the service was unavailable. Please see below for each service level credit.\n\nAverage Page Response Time:\nMinimum Service Level: 2.00 seconds or less\nCredit: If the response time exceeds 2.00 seconds, a credit is applied equal to 10% of the monthly fee multiplied by the excess time.\n\nIncident Resolution Service Credits:\nPriority 1 (Critical Issues) – Resolution within 4 hours (24x7 support)\nCredit: 10% of monthly fees if not met.\n\nPriority 2 (High-Priority Issues) – Resolution within 12 hours (24x7 support)\nCredit: 5% of monthly fees if not met.\n\nPriority 3 (Standard Issues) – Resolution within 3 business days\nCredit: TBD\n\nPriority 4 (Low-Priority Issues) – Resolution within 5 business days\nCredit: TBD"}, {"id": "rfp_522", "category": "General", "question": "How do you monitor and ensure adherence to SLAs?", "answer": "We monitor SLA adherence through a centralized ticketing system with built-in tracking for response and resolution times. Alerts are triggered for SLA breaches, and reports are reviewed regularly by our support and success teams. Performance is measured against defined KPIs, and any deviations are investigated through root cause analysis to ensure accountability and continuous improvement."}, {"id": "rfp_523", "category": "General", "question": "What penalties or remedies are in place if service levels are not met?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub will offer credits to Mastercard if SLAs are not met."}, {"id": "rfp_524", "category": "General", "question": "How often do you review and adjust SLAs based on client needs or industry standards?", "answer": "We will collaborate closely with Mastercard to determine whether the existing SLAs should be revised in any way to ensure we are meeting your needs and expectations."}, {"id": "rfp_525", "category": "General", "question": "Do you provide regular performance reports demonstrating compliance with SLAs?", "answer": "Yes"}, {"id": "rfp_526", "category": "General", "question": "What percentage of service requests are typically resolved within your defined SLA timelines?", "answer": "Over 95% of service requests are resolved within our defined SLA timelines. We prioritize issues by severity and have clear response and resolution targets. Our support team tracks all requests through a centralized ticketing system, ensuring transparency, accountability, and timely resolution. Regular reviews help maintain and improve service performance."}, {"id": "rfp_527", "category": "General", "question": "How do you handle escalations when SLA commitments are not met?", "answer": "If SLA commitments are not met, issues are escalated through a defined tiered process involving senior support staff and, if needed, product or engineering leads. Clients receive regular updates until resolution. Root cause analysis is conducted, and corrective actions are documented to prevent recurrence. Escalation paths and response times are outlined in our support agreement."}, {"id": "rfp_528", "category": "General", "question": "Are there any exclusions or limitations to your standard SLAs that we should be aware of?", "answer": "Yes, SLA timelines may be impacted if resolution depends on third-party systems (e.g., VMS, ATS) or delays in client-side input or access. Exclusions also apply to issues arising from scheduled maintenance, force majeure events, or unsupported custom configurations. All such cases are communicated proactively, and we work collaboratively with all parties to resolve issues promptly."}, {"id": "rfp_529", "category": "General", "question": "What is customer satisfaction score guaranteed?", "answer": "While we’ve never been asked to guarantee a CSAT score, our satisfaction ratings consistently exceed 90%. We are open to discussing and defining a mutually agreeable CSAT target with Mastercard as part of our partnership to ensure service quality and accountability."}, {"id": "rfp_530", "category": "General", "question": "What is your pricing model, and does it vary by region?    Will you offer a hybrid pricing approach if requested (Licence, Volume based)", "answer": "We offer a flexible pricing model aligned with Mastercard’s business objectives. Our standard options include a tiered percentage of spend or a fixed-fee subscription. Pricing does not vary by region. If preferred, we’re open to a hybrid model (e.g., license + volume-based) to ensure maximum value and alignment with your program goals."}, {"id": "rfp_531", "category": "General", "question": "Are there additional costs for providing services in certain countries?", "answer": "SMS costs differ by country. For countries with higher costs than the United States, those additional fees will be passed through at cost."}, {"id": "rfp_532", "category": "General", "question": "How do you handle billing and invoicing for multinational clients?", "answer": "KnowledgeHub supports weekly or monthly invoicing based on spend by location, in the local currency of the contracting Mastercard entity, as required. For example, transactions tied to a Belgian entity will be billed in EUR. For flat subscription models, KnowledgeHub can issue a single consolidated invoice in USD. Invoicing formats, frequency, and delivery preferences can be tailored to Mastercard’s global billing needs."}, {"id": "rfp_533", "category": "General", "question": "Please provide a detailed pricing proposal for the cost of your proposed solution for the 3 keys identified areas.  Please provide a detailed breakdown of all cost including assumptions, pricing tiers, volume discounts, rebates, implementation costs, training costs, and support costs.  All prices should be quoted in USD and exclusive of any applicable taxes.", "answer": "Our proposed pricing is based on a tiered percentage of contingent labor spend across all regions (US, EU & India, Canada):\n\n2.00% on spend up to $10M\n\n1.50% on spend from $10M–$25M\n\n1.00% on spend above $25M\nThere are no additional charges for implementation, training, support, or integrations. All pricing is in USD and exclusive of applicable taxes. hybrid models available upon request."}, {"id": "rfp_534", "category": "General", "question": "Are there any additional fees for specialized services or after-hours support?", "answer": "No"}, {"id": "rfp_535", "category": "General", "question": "Please outline innovative pricing models that you would recommend", "answer": "We recommend an innovative fixed-fee license model: $60K (Year 1), $90K (Year 2), $150K (Year 4), and $270K (Year 5), covering the full program across the US and global expansion. This provides Mastercard with predictable budgeting, cost control, and flexibility to scale the program over time. It supports ramp-up while delivering long-term value."}, {"id": "rfp_536", "category": "General", "question": "How does your company pro-actively generate, document, and deliver year over year savings for your client?", "answer": "We track and report year-over-year savings through detailed analytics on fill ratios, time-to-fill, agency avoidance, and cost per hire. Our team conducts quarterly business reviews to document outcomes, benchmark performance, and identify new opportunities for savings. By continuously optimizing sourcing strategies and curator efficiency, we proactively drive measurable value and cost reduction for our clients."}, {"id": "rfp_537", "category": "General", "question": "Please outline what you consider to be cost savings versus cost avoidance.", "answer": "Cost savings refer to measurable reductions in spend—e.g., lower markups, fewer third-party fees, or faster fills reducing reliance on expensive suppliers. Cost avoidance refers to preventing future spend—e.g., avoiding agency fees by building internal talent pipelines or reducing turnover through better matching. KnowledgeHub delivers both by enabling direct hires and increasing program efficiency."}, {"id": "rfp_538", "category": "Data Security", "question": "What kind of data does the product handle or process? What is the sensitivity/data classification?", "answer": "Our Direct Sourcing platform handles candidate and client workforce data necessary to enable sourcing, engagement, and hiring workflows. This includes: \n\nYahoo Highly Confidential: Candidate information (contact details, résumé/CV data, skills, job history, pay expectations). \n\nPublic and Yahoo Private or Internal (Partially): Job requisition details (title, description, compensation range, location). \n\nYahoo Private or internal: Client system integration data (job IDs, recruiter assignments, hiring workflows)."}, {"id": "rfp_539", "category": "Data Security", "question": "Where does the data used in this system originate, and where does it go?", "answer": "Origination: Candidate data may be entered directly by job seekers, imported from client ATS/HRIS systems, the VMS or aggregated through sourcing channels such as job boards and talent pools. \n\nDestination: Data remains within the platform’s secure environment, is shared with authorized client users, and may integrate back to ATS/HRIS/VMS systems or MSP and Curation partners as designated by the client."}, {"id": "rfp_540", "category": "Data Security", "question": "Do any components store, transmit, or process data that would be considered non-public information?", "answer": "Yes. Candidate PII and client workforce data are classified as non-public information  \n\nStrategies to protect that data: \n\nRole-based access controls (RBAC). \n\nEnforced MFA (multi-factor authentication). \n\nSOC 2 Type II and GDPR compliance controls. \n\nAES-256 encryption at rest \n\nTLS 1.2+ encryption in transit \n\nMulti-factor authentication \n\nRegular vulnerability scans and penetration testing \n\nActivity logging and monitoring \n\nData loss prevention (DLP) policies \n\nEncryption: \n\nWe use TLS 1.2 or higher for all data transmission, ensuring data is encrypted in transit using industry best practices. Our platform supports strong encryption algorithms such as AES-256 and RSA with secure key exchange protocols. We also enforce HTTPS across all endpoints and regularly test for vulnerabilities. \n\nHighest classification stored/processed: Yahoo highly confidential"}, {"id": "rfp_541", "category": "Data Security", "question": "How is access to the product managed?", "answer": "Access is managed through role-based access controls, single sign-on (SSO) integration with client and/or curation providers, and MFA. Clients can define permissions at a granular level for recruiters, hiring managers, and administrators."}, {"id": "rfp_542", "category": "Data Security", "question": "Is there an administrator control panel? If so:", "answer": "Capabilities administrators have : \n\nCreate, edit, and deactivate user accounts. \n\nAssign roles and permissions. \n\nManage integrations and data feeds. \n\nConfigure branding, compliance settings (e.g., pay transparency), and workflows. \n\nAccess system activity logs and reporting. \n\nLogging: \n\nAll admin activities (user provisioning, permission changes, data access, configuration changes) are logged and available for audit. \n\nNumber of users with admin panel access: \n\nDetermined by the client and curation partner: generally limited to a small number of authorized system administrators to reduce risk exposure."}, {"id": "rfp_543", "category": "Data Security", "question": "Are AI/ML/LLM integrations involved in this product?", "answer": "Yes. AI/ML models are used within the platform to: \n\nEnhance candidate-to-role matching. \n\nSupport conversational engagement with candidates (chatbots). \n\nProvide data/insights to Recruiter regarding how candidate is ranked for a specific job. \n\nSafeguards: \n\nAI components do not expose raw PII to third-party models as KnowledgeHub crated and  owns our AI model. \n\nContinuous monitoring ensures compliance with evolving AI governance and data security standards, including bias."}];

